AI systems that are equally capable. They both solve the exact same engineering problem with the exact same accuracy, but they have totally different impacts on the human using them. Let's walk through these, because this thought experiment perfectly encapsulates the warning of the paper. The author calls System 1 the idealized oracle. Okay, System 1. Picture this. You are a programmer, and you have a nasty memory leak in your software that you just can't figure out. You give your code to System 1, the oracle. And what does it do? It processes it for two seconds and instantly spits out the perfect, bug-free block of code to replace yours. Just hands you the answer. The interaction is incredibly efficient. You copy the code, you paste it into your project, the software works perfectly, and you move on with your day. The immediate problem disappears. Productivity is maximized. But, crucially, your personal competence remains exactly the same as it was before you asked the question. You didn't learn why the memory leak happened. You didn't learn the architectural principle of memory management that fixes it. You don't know how to spot it next time. The representation, the conceptual understanding of the system, stayed completely inside the machine's neural network. Only the finished, polished artifact crossed over the screen to you. Yeah. I outsourced my reasoning. Exactly. Now, consider System 2. The author calls this the educator. You feed it the same broken code. It analyzes it and reaches the exact same accurate conclusion about how to fix it. But instead of just handing you the finished code on a silver platter, it exposes the reasoning. An educator system would have to be architected entirely differently. It would identify the underlying abstractions. It would point out the conceptual structures you violated. It might say, I notice your program is continuously allocating memory in this loop without freeing it. Here is the principle of garbage collection you are missing. And here is a conceptual map of how we construct a solution. It guides you to read the code yourself. It's the difference between a vending machine and a teaching kitchen. System 1 is the vending machine. You press a button, you insert a coin, and a perfectly cooked gourmet meal drops out. Fast and effortless. Fast, delicious, requires zero effort. But if the vending machine ever unplugs, or if the company raises the price of the meal to $1,000, you are going to starve because you have absolutely no idea how to chop an onion or turn on a stove. Right. System 2 is the teaching kitchen. It takes a little bit more time, it requires cognitive friction and engagement, but you walk out of that room actually knowing how to cook. The competence was transferred to you. A fantastic analogy. And from the perspective of an executive looking at a spreadsheet of immediate productivity, both systems look equally valuable. The software bug was fixed in both scenarios. The meal was delivered. But from the perspective of civilizational memory, the paper argues these two systems produce entirely divergent futures. System 1 creates a civilization that accumulates increasingly sophisticated magical artifacts, while leaving all the reconstructive competence locked inside the proprietary server farms of a few AI companies. We become incredibly productive, but our productivity is a brittle house of cards relying entirely on external representation. The paper draws a really sharp parallel here to the history of automation and the de-skilling of labor, like the tractor analogy we used earlier. Oh right. When we mechanized farming with the tractor, we displaced immense amounts of physical labor. We needed far fewer people swinging scythes or guiding oxen in the field. But in displacing that physical labor, the technology created an immense demand for new conceptual labor. We suddenly needed mechanical engineers to design the tractors, logisticians to manage the supply chain, agronomists to study soil chemistry, and industrial managers. The physical labor was outsourced to the machine, but the conceptual labor remained human. But AI isn't a tractor for our muscles, it's a tractor for our minds. Exactly. AI threatens to centralize the conceptual labor itself. If we use these systems purely as oracles, we risk building an economy where humans merely act as requesters. We constantly request brilliant artifacts from the black box, but we slowly atrophy the cognitive frameworks required to even critically examine, debug, modify, or extend the results we are given. If you don't know how to code, how can you verify that the oracle's code is secure? You can't. If you don't understand legal precedent, how can you verify that oracle's legal brief isn't a hallucination? We lose the ability to judge the framework that produced the answer. We become a society of passive consumers, just typing prompts into the void and hoping the magic box gives us something good. And if we lose the ability to evaluate the answer, we are entirely unmoored from reality. Which brings us to the ultimate question posed by this entire deep dive. This is the crux of it. If we can't just look at how fast our microchips are, or how many lines of code our AI can write per minute, or how high the GDP is, how should we measure whether our society is actually progressing? This is where the fliction paper brings all these historical and technical threads together into a unified theory of progress. The author does not dismiss productivity. Material abundance, economic growth, computational capability, these are undeniably vital. They freed us from famine. Exactly. They are what freed humanity from the brutal historical realities of scarcity. A society that cannot reliably produce food, medicine, or shelter, cannot sustain high-level scientific inquiry. We should celebrate our productivity. But the author insists, productivity is an insufficient measure of civilizational success. Progress must simultaneously be measured by that phrase we started with, reconstructive capacity. And the text gives us one final sweeping thought experiment to really hammer this home. It asks us to picture two different societies existing side by side. Okay, Society A and Society B. On the surface, they are technologically identical. They both have advanced stealth aircraft, incredible MRI machines, light and fast quantum computers. If you walk down the main street in Society A or Society B, the gadgets in people's hands and the cars on the road would look exactly the same. But underneath the surface, their architectures of knowledge are completely different. Right. In Society A, knowledge is highly distributed. Engineers, educators, mechanics, open source communities, and ordinary citizens collectively hold the understanding of how their world works. No single institution acts as an irreplaceable bottleneck for competence. Exactly. The knowledge flows freely between university research labs, private industry, and public life. The tools they build are permeable. The abstractions are ladders. The representations are shared. But in Society B, they have the exact same glittering gadgets. But the reconstructive competence is held by a tiny handful of opaque, hyper-centralized organizations. The citizens interact with magic every day. They touch glass screens and things happen. But hardly anyone outside those few corporate campuses possesses the conceptual resources to understand, modify, or rebuild the systems independently. Their tools are sealed black boxes. And here is the terrifying punchline of the paper. However, conventional economics cannot tell these two societies apart. Their GDP is identical. Their average standard of living is identical. Consumer satisfaction surveys might even be identical. But Society A has accumulated durable competence. Society B has only accumulated fragile artifacts. Society B is brittle. If a massive disruption occurs, a political collapse, a geomagnetic storm that wipes out data centers, a shift in corporate incentives, or an economic catastrophe, the artifacts will remain for a while, just like the Roman aqueducts. But the capacity to regenerate those systems, to fix them when they break, will rapidly vanish. So what does this all mean? Well, when you strip away all the academic terminology, the hashing algorithms, a history of calculus, the core warning of this source material is that we are currently making a silent, unacknowledged trade. We are trading our permanent civilizational memory for temporary capability. We are trading the messy, slow, occasionally frustrating, but incredibly resilient process of distributing knowledge for the frictionless, lightning-fast, incredibly fragile process of renting convenience. What's fascinating here is how this framework redefines the entire purpose of technology. The author concludes that the highest purpose of technological innovation isn't actually making sophisticated machines. It's not. The machines, the software, the AI, they're just a byproduct. The true purpose of technology is expanding humanity's representational repertoire. Representational repertoire. Explain that. When Euclid formalized geometry, or when Newton formalized mechanics, they didn't just give us tools to build better aqueducts or aim cannons more accurately. They fundamentally expanded humanity's shared capacity to think. Oh, I see. That geometry and that physics became a permanent part of who we are as a species. They gave future generations a richer conceptual foundation to stand on. That is true progress. When a tool becomes a new language for human thought, civilization advances. When a tool just performs a magic trick behind a proprietary curtain, we really consume. And that puts the responsibility squarely on us, on the consumers, and crucially on the engineers and institutions building the next generation of infrastructure. Because the AI models, the cloud platforms, the digital ecosystems, they don't have an intrinsic bias toward opacity. They can be built as ladders or they can be built as walls. They can be engineered to transfer competence, to act as educators, or they can be built to hoard it, to act as oracles. It is an architectural choice. It is entirely a choice. The technology itself cannot determine which future emerges. It depends on whether our economic structures continue to exclusively reward the artificial scarcity of competence, or whether we demand systems that leave behind more capable human minds after every interaction. A civilization only truly remembers its inventions when its citizens remember how to invent. Which brings us all back to you, listening to this right now. Tomorrow morning, you are going to wake up and immediately interact with dozens of deeply complex, beautifully designed digital systems. You are going to use perfectly optimized platforms. You might ask an AI to draft an email, debug a piece of code, or explain a complex concept for a meeting. And when you do, the source material we've explored today asks you to pause and ask yourself one simple question. Is this tool acting as a ladder or a wall? Are you renting this competence, or is it being transferred to you? Are you acquiring a new capability, or are you just happily consuming a result? I'd take it a step further. Because if we continue down this current path, if we blindly accept the convenience without demanding the representation, if we continue outsourcing our capacity to reason and reconstruct to proprietary black boxes... We have to ask ourselves what kind of world we are leaving behind for the next generation. Exactly. Will historians of the future look back at our era, not as the pinnacle of the information age, but as the quiet, comfortable, frictionless beginning of a technological dark age? An era where the cities were dazzlingly bright, the algorithms ran flawlessly, the information flowed endlessly... But nobody was actually home. ...a haunting extrapolation. But an absolutely essential one to consider before the walls get too high to climb. That's our deep dive for today. Keep climbing the ladders, and we'll catch you next time.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.3, "text": " Imagine, for just a moment, that you wake up tomorrow morning in a fully functioning modern city.", "tokens": [50365, 11739, 11, 337, 445, 257, 1623, 11, 300, 291, 6634, 493, 4153, 2446, 294, 257, 4498, 18483, 4363, 2307, 13, 50630], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 1, "seek": 0, "start": 5.54, "end": 6.84, "text": " Okay, I am picturing it.", "tokens": [50642, 1033, 11, 286, 669, 2317, 1345, 309, 13, 50707], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 2, "seek": 0, "start": 6.94, "end": 10.98, "text": " Right, so it is dawn, the streetlights are glowing perfectly against the gray sky,", "tokens": [50712, 1779, 11, 370, 309, 307, 18192, 11, 264, 4838, 20827, 366, 27064, 6239, 1970, 264, 10855, 5443, 11, 50914], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 3, "seek": 0, "start": 11.28, "end": 16.44, "text": " and they're, you know, turning off one by one as ambient light sensors detect the sunrise.", "tokens": [50929, 293, 436, 434, 11, 291, 458, 11, 6246, 766, 472, 538, 472, 382, 22997, 1442, 14840, 5531, 264, 33675, 13, 51187], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 4, "seek": 0, "start": 16.740000000000002, "end": 18.68, "text": " Just a normal, automated morning.", "tokens": [51202, 1449, 257, 2710, 11, 18473, 2446, 13, 51299], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 5, "seek": 0, "start": 18.82, "end": 22.96, "text": " Exactly. And down the street, the hospitals are just humming along,", "tokens": [51306, 7587, 13, 400, 760, 264, 4838, 11, 264, 13014, 366, 445, 34965, 2051, 11, 51513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 6, "seek": 0, "start": 23.38, "end": 25.44, "text": " performing these advanced robotic surgeries.", "tokens": [51534, 10205, 613, 7339, 30468, 33455, 13, 51637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14071976372955042, "compression_ratio": 1.605072463768116, "no_speech_prob": 1.1290735056970758e-12}, {"id": 7, "seek": 2544, "start": 25.44, "end": 32.72, "text": " Your internet connection is blazing fast, pulling down gigabits of data from, like, servers across the ocean.", "tokens": [50365, 2260, 4705, 4984, 307, 16379, 8781, 2370, 11, 8407, 760, 8741, 455, 1208, 295, 1412, 490, 11, 411, 11, 15909, 2108, 264, 7810, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 8, "seek": 2544, "start": 32.84, "end": 34.44, "text": " Global supply chains are moving, I assume.", "tokens": [50735, 14465, 5847, 12626, 366, 2684, 11, 286, 6552, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 9, "seek": 2544, "start": 34.56, "end": 39.78, "text": " Oh, absolutely. Coordinating ships, trains, delivery drones, airplanes are taken off right on schedule.", "tokens": [50821, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 39620, 990, 11434, 11, 16329, 11, 8982, 23823, 11, 32947, 366, 2726, 766, 558, 322, 7567, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 10, "seek": 2544, "start": 39.94, "end": 41.28, "text": " Everything is running perfectly.", "tokens": [51090, 5471, 307, 2614, 6239, 13, 51157], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 11, "seek": 2544, "start": 41.480000000000004, "end": 42.66, "text": " Sounds ideal, honestly.", "tokens": [51167, 14576, 7157, 11, 6095, 13, 51226], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 12, "seek": 2544, "start": 42.94, "end": 48.58, "text": " It does. Every single invention we have accumulated over the last few centuries is operating exactly as intended.", "tokens": [51240, 467, 775, 13, 2048, 2167, 22265, 321, 362, 31346, 670, 264, 1036, 1326, 13926, 307, 7447, 2293, 382, 10226, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 13, "seek": 2544, "start": 49.18000000000001, "end": 54.46, "text": " But there is one massive, really unsettling catch to all of this.", "tokens": [51552, 583, 456, 307, 472, 5994, 11, 534, 43964, 1688, 3745, 281, 439, 295, 341, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08705099354619565, "compression_ratio": 1.565079365079365, "no_speech_prob": 7.520639926789086e-13}, {"id": 14, "seek": 5446, "start": 54.46, "end": 55.22, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 30, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 15, "seek": 5446, "start": 55.36, "end": 58.02, "text": " Almost nobody alive actually knows how any of it works.", "tokens": [50410, 12627, 5079, 5465, 767, 3255, 577, 604, 295, 309, 1985, 13, 50543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 16, "seek": 5446, "start": 58.18, "end": 61.7, "text": " Oh, wow. Yeah, that is a genuinely eerie thought experiment.", "tokens": [50551, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 865, 11, 300, 307, 257, 17839, 308, 17487, 1194, 5120, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 17, "seek": 5446, "start": 62.18, "end": 67.48, "text": " The systems just continue to run blindly, but the human understanding underneath them has completely evaporated.", "tokens": [50751, 440, 3652, 445, 2354, 281, 1190, 47744, 11, 457, 264, 1952, 3701, 7223, 552, 575, 2584, 26315, 770, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 18, "seek": 5446, "start": 67.8, "end": 71.84, "text": " Right. Like, the engineers who designed the power grid, they're gone.", "tokens": [51032, 1779, 13, 1743, 11, 264, 11955, 567, 4761, 264, 1347, 10748, 11, 436, 434, 2780, 13, 51234], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 19, "seek": 5446, "start": 72.28, "end": 78.02, "text": " The physicists who discovered the underlying electromagnetic principles just disappeared.", "tokens": [51256, 440, 48716, 567, 6941, 264, 14217, 32214, 9156, 445, 13954, 13, 51543], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 20, "seek": 5446, "start": 78.26, "end": 82.48, "text": " And the programmers who wrote the millions of lines of routing code for those planes, I guess?", "tokens": [51555, 400, 264, 41504, 567, 4114, 264, 6803, 295, 3876, 295, 32722, 3089, 337, 729, 14952, 11, 286, 2041, 30, 51766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12162581357088956, "compression_ratio": 1.5833333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.6356249037466353e-12}, {"id": 21, "seek": 8248, "start": 82.48, "end": 88.16, "text": " Nowhere to be found. Or, like, the material scientists who formulated the alloys for the jet engines.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 6703, 281, 312, 1352, 13, 1610, 11, 411, 11, 264, 2527, 7708, 567, 48936, 264, 439, 44131, 337, 264, 14452, 12982, 13, 50649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 22, "seek": 8248, "start": 88.48, "end": 93.56, "text": " The only reason the factories keep churning out replacement parts is because they are entirely automated.", "tokens": [50665, 440, 787, 1778, 264, 24813, 1066, 417, 10656, 484, 14419, 3166, 307, 570, 436, 366, 7696, 18473, 13, 50919], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 23, "seek": 8248, "start": 93.72, "end": 97.86, "text": " So they are just blindly following instructions written by people who no longer exist.", "tokens": [50927, 407, 436, 366, 445, 47744, 3480, 9415, 3720, 538, 561, 567, 572, 2854, 2514, 13, 51134], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 24, "seek": 8248, "start": 97.98, "end": 102.76, "text": " Exactly. Instructions based on principles that have completely faded from common knowledge.", "tokens": [51140, 7587, 13, 2730, 1757, 626, 2361, 322, 9156, 300, 362, 2584, 36352, 490, 2689, 3601, 13, 51379], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 25, "seek": 8248, "start": 102.92, "end": 103.08000000000001, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51387, 865, 13, 51395], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 26, "seek": 8248, "start": 103.2, "end": 108.86, "text": " So on paper, or, you know, to an outside observer, this civilization looks incredibly prosperous.", "tokens": [51401, 407, 322, 3035, 11, 420, 11, 291, 458, 11, 281, 364, 2380, 27878, 11, 341, 18036, 1542, 6252, 38928, 13, 51684], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08269145753648546, "compression_ratio": 1.6013071895424837, "no_speech_prob": 2.0602833675220644e-12}, {"id": 27, "seek": 10886, "start": 108.86, "end": 111.48, "text": " It looks like the absolute pinnacle of human achievement.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1542, 411, 264, 8236, 5447, 77, 7041, 295, 1952, 15838, 13, 50496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1350072186167647, "compression_ratio": 1.4429223744292237, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691661937518921e-12}, {"id": 28, "seek": 10886, "start": 111.76, "end": 115.4, "text": " It really does. But underneath, there's this terrifying void.", "tokens": [50510, 467, 534, 775, 13, 583, 7223, 11, 456, 311, 341, 18106, 22009, 13, 50692], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1350072186167647, "compression_ratio": 1.4429223744292237, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691661937518921e-12}, {"id": 29, "seek": 10886, "start": 116.2, "end": 120.64, "text": " And, well, that scenario is the exact premise of the material we are diving into today.", "tokens": [50732, 400, 11, 731, 11, 300, 9005, 307, 264, 1900, 22045, 295, 264, 2527, 321, 366, 20241, 666, 965, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1350072186167647, "compression_ratio": 1.4429223744292237, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691661937518921e-12}, {"id": 30, "seek": 10886, "start": 120.74, "end": 122.28, "text": " It is a profound piece of writing.", "tokens": [50959, 467, 307, 257, 14382, 2522, 295, 3579, 13, 51036], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1350072186167647, "compression_ratio": 1.4429223744292237, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691661937518921e-12}, {"id": 31, "seek": 10886, "start": 122.7, "end": 126.86, "text": " Yeah. We're looking at a 2026 paper by Affliction Independent Researcher.", "tokens": [51057, 865, 13, 492, 434, 1237, 412, 257, 945, 10880, 3035, 538, 12840, 75, 4105, 40310, 10303, 260, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1350072186167647, "compression_ratio": 1.4429223744292237, "no_speech_prob": 1.7691661937518921e-12}, {"id": 32, "seek": 12686, "start": 126.86, "end": 134.82, "text": " It's titled The Privatization of Competence, Civilizational Memory, Institutional Knowledge, and the Purpose of Technological Progress.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 19841, 440, 8087, 23352, 2144, 295, 32216, 655, 11, 13405, 590, 1478, 38203, 11, 2730, 41859, 32906, 11, 293, 264, 14682, 43501, 295, 8337, 4383, 32587, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09967410143683939, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 2.0923980863923886e-12}, {"id": 33, "seek": 12686, "start": 135.2, "end": 147.6, "text": " And I think it's important to frame this right away because we normally evaluate our progress by looking at things like GDP, right, or computational power, or just the sheer abundance of consumer goods on the shelves.", "tokens": [50782, 400, 286, 519, 309, 311, 1021, 281, 3920, 341, 558, 1314, 570, 321, 5646, 13059, 527, 4205, 538, 1237, 412, 721, 411, 19599, 11, 558, 11, 420, 28270, 1347, 11, 420, 445, 264, 23061, 23391, 295, 9711, 10179, 322, 264, 24349, 13, 51402], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09967410143683939, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 2.0923980863923886e-12}, {"id": 34, "seek": 12686, "start": 147.76, "end": 148.62, "text": " We look at the output.", "tokens": [51410, 492, 574, 412, 264, 5598, 13, 51453], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09967410143683939, "compression_ratio": 1.5161290322580645, "no_speech_prob": 2.0923980863923886e-12}, {"id": 35, "seek": 14862, "start": 148.62, "end": 156.54, "text": " Exactly. The output. But this paper asks us to look at something much more fragile. We aren't looking at economics today, and we aren't looking at politics.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 5598, 13, 583, 341, 3035, 8962, 505, 281, 574, 412, 746, 709, 544, 23847, 13, 492, 3212, 380, 1237, 412, 14564, 965, 11, 293, 321, 3212, 380, 1237, 412, 7341, 13, 50761], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0699688007957057, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310972975579595e-12}, {"id": 36, "seek": 14862, "start": 156.94, "end": 159.88, "text": " No, we are exploring civilizational memory.", "tokens": [50781, 883, 11, 321, 366, 12736, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 13, 50928], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0699688007957057, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310972975579595e-12}, {"id": 37, "seek": 14862, "start": 160.06, "end": 175.88, "text": " Right. The core thesis here is that humanity might be making a grave historical error. We are confusing the accumulation of cool, convenient gadgets, what the author calls artifacts, with the accumulation of actual, durable knowledge.", "tokens": [50937, 1779, 13, 440, 4965, 22288, 510, 307, 300, 10243, 1062, 312, 1455, 257, 12525, 8584, 6713, 13, 492, 366, 13181, 264, 35647, 295, 1627, 11, 10851, 37635, 11, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 24617, 11, 365, 264, 35647, 295, 3539, 11, 22308, 3601, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0699688007957057, "compression_ratio": 1.6730769230769231, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310972975579595e-12}, {"id": 38, "seek": 17588, "start": 175.88, "end": 183.6, "text": " Okay, let's unpack this. Because if all our incredible modern technology is actually making humanity smarter, well, that's a massive win.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 718, 311, 26699, 341, 13, 1436, 498, 439, 527, 4651, 4363, 2899, 307, 767, 1455, 10243, 20294, 11, 731, 11, 300, 311, 257, 5994, 1942, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06475295402385571, "compression_ratio": 1.6012861736334405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724694124250814e-12}, {"id": 39, "seek": 17588, "start": 183.76, "end": 184.64, "text": " Right. Ideally.", "tokens": [50759, 1779, 13, 40817, 13, 50803], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06475295402385571, "compression_ratio": 1.6012861736334405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724694124250814e-12}, {"id": 40, "seek": 17588, "start": 184.85999999999999, "end": 195.6, "text": " But this paper is basically asking whether we, quietly, almost systematically, forgetting how our world works, while massive, invisible institutions hold all the keys.", "tokens": [50814, 583, 341, 3035, 307, 1936, 3365, 1968, 321, 11, 19141, 11, 1920, 39531, 11, 25428, 577, 527, 1002, 1985, 11, 1339, 5994, 11, 14603, 8142, 1797, 439, 264, 9317, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06475295402385571, "compression_ratio": 1.6012861736334405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724694124250814e-12}, {"id": 41, "seek": 17588, "start": 195.98, "end": 204.18, "text": " It's a scary thought. And to even start wrapping our heads around how we might be losing our knowledge, we have to completely redefine what a civilization's memory actually is.", "tokens": [51370, 467, 311, 257, 6958, 1194, 13, 400, 281, 754, 722, 21993, 527, 8050, 926, 577, 321, 1062, 312, 7027, 527, 3601, 11, 321, 362, 281, 2584, 38818, 533, 437, 257, 18036, 311, 4675, 767, 307, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06475295402385571, "compression_ratio": 1.6012861736334405, "no_speech_prob": 1.3724694124250814e-12}, {"id": 42, "seek": 20418, "start": 204.18, "end": 211.68, "text": " Yeah, because when I hear, uh, civilizational memory, my mind instantly goes to physical storage.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 11, 570, 562, 286, 1568, 11, 2232, 11, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 11, 452, 1575, 13518, 1709, 281, 4001, 6725, 13, 50740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08574979495158237, "compression_ratio": 1.5272108843537415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4328588229112205e-12}, {"id": 43, "seek": 20418, "start": 211.86, "end": 213.44, "text": " Oh, totally. Like, what?", "tokens": [50749, 876, 11, 3879, 13, 1743, 11, 437, 30, 50828], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08574979495158237, "compression_ratio": 1.5272108843537415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4328588229112205e-12}, {"id": 44, "seek": 20418, "start": 213.58, "end": 225.48000000000002, "text": " Like, I picture the Library of Congress, or I picture those massive, climate-controlled server farms buried under mountains, filled with, you know, digitized encyclopedias and open-source code.", "tokens": [50835, 1743, 11, 286, 3036, 264, 12806, 295, 6426, 11, 420, 286, 3036, 729, 5994, 11, 5659, 12, 49344, 7154, 20366, 14101, 833, 10233, 11, 6412, 365, 11, 291, 458, 11, 14293, 1602, 465, 34080, 27277, 4609, 293, 1269, 12, 41676, 3089, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08574979495158237, "compression_ratio": 1.5272108843537415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4328588229112205e-12}, {"id": 45, "seek": 20418, "start": 225.52, "end": 229.58, "text": " Which is the exact instinct the author wants to dismantle right out of the gate.", "tokens": [51432, 3013, 307, 264, 1900, 16556, 264, 3793, 2738, 281, 30506, 306, 558, 484, 295, 264, 8539, 13, 51635], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08574979495158237, "compression_ratio": 1.5272108843537415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4328588229112205e-12}, {"id": 46, "seek": 20418, "start": 229.74, "end": 232.14000000000001, "text": " Really? But isn't that where we keep our knowledge?", "tokens": [51643, 4083, 30, 583, 1943, 380, 300, 689, 321, 1066, 527, 3601, 30, 51763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08574979495158237, "compression_ratio": 1.5272108843537415, "no_speech_prob": 1.4328588229112205e-12}, {"id": 47, "seek": 23214, "start": 232.14, "end": 242.89999999999998, "text": " We have this deep-seated tendency to look at physical and digital repositories and feel a sense of security. We look at a massive archive and think, ah, there is our memory, safe and sound.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 341, 2452, 12, 405, 770, 18187, 281, 574, 412, 4001, 293, 4562, 22283, 2083, 293, 841, 257, 2020, 295, 3825, 13, 492, 574, 412, 257, 5994, 23507, 293, 519, 11, 3716, 11, 456, 307, 527, 4675, 11, 3273, 293, 1626, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 48, "seek": 23214, "start": 243.07999999999998, "end": 243.73999999999998, "text": " Yeah, exactly.", "tokens": [50912, 865, 11, 2293, 13, 50945], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 49, "seek": 23214, "start": 243.76, "end": 256.34, "text": " But the source text argues forcefully that civilizational memory does not live in objects. It does not live in databases. Libraries, blueprints, massive hard drives full of unread source code, these are not memory.", "tokens": [50946, 583, 264, 4009, 2487, 38218, 3464, 2277, 300, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 775, 406, 1621, 294, 6565, 13, 467, 775, 406, 1621, 294, 22380, 13, 12006, 4889, 11, 888, 23547, 47523, 11, 5994, 1152, 11754, 1577, 295, 517, 2538, 4009, 3089, 11, 613, 366, 406, 4675, 13, 51575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 50, "seek": 23214, "start": 256.65999999999997, "end": 257.97999999999996, "text": " Wait, if they aren't memory, what are they?", "tokens": [51591, 3802, 11, 498, 436, 3212, 380, 4675, 11, 437, 366, 436, 30, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 51, "seek": 23214, "start": 258.03999999999996, "end": 259.15999999999997, "text": " They are merely records.", "tokens": [51660, 814, 366, 17003, 7724, 13, 51716], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 52, "seek": 23214, "start": 259.24, "end": 261.5, "text": " That's records. Okay. So they're like dead storage.", "tokens": [51720, 663, 311, 7724, 13, 1033, 13, 407, 436, 434, 411, 3116, 6725, 13, 51833], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09607142987458603, "compression_ratio": 1.6875, "no_speech_prob": 1.4325104687532009e-12}, {"id": 53, "seek": 26150, "start": 261.5, "end": 268.9, "text": " Precisely. A book that no one reads is just bleached wood pulp with dried chemicals smeared on it in specific patterns.", "tokens": [50365, 48746, 736, 13, 316, 1446, 300, 572, 472, 15700, 307, 445, 5408, 15095, 4576, 37489, 365, 13538, 16152, 41818, 1642, 322, 309, 294, 2685, 8294, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0787925282749561, "compression_ratio": 1.6167247386759582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839902310465058e-12}, {"id": 54, "seek": 26150, "start": 268.98, "end": 272.26, "text": " Wow. That is the perfect way to look at it. Just wood pulp.", "tokens": [50739, 3153, 13, 663, 307, 264, 2176, 636, 281, 574, 412, 309, 13, 1449, 4576, 37489, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0787925282749561, "compression_ratio": 1.6167247386759582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839902310465058e-12}, {"id": 55, "seek": 26150, "start": 272.34, "end": 283.48, "text": " A highly detailed blueprint of, say, a quantum microchip, if no one alive can comprehend the physics required to manufacture it, is just a collection of intersecting lines.", "tokens": [50907, 316, 5405, 9942, 35868, 295, 11, 584, 11, 257, 13018, 4532, 339, 647, 11, 498, 572, 472, 5465, 393, 38183, 264, 10649, 4739, 281, 27400, 309, 11, 307, 445, 257, 5765, 295, 27815, 278, 3876, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0787925282749561, "compression_ratio": 1.6167247386759582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839902310465058e-12}, {"id": 56, "seek": 26150, "start": 283.64, "end": 288.74, "text": " Right. And source code that cannot be interpreted by a human mind is just a meaningless arrangement of symbols.", "tokens": [51472, 1779, 13, 400, 4009, 3089, 300, 2644, 312, 26749, 538, 257, 1952, 1575, 307, 445, 257, 33232, 17620, 295, 16944, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0787925282749561, "compression_ratio": 1.6167247386759582, "no_speech_prob": 1.4839902310465058e-12}, {"id": 57, "seek": 28874, "start": 288.74, "end": 296.14, "text": " Exactly. The paper asserts that true memory resides entirely in what it calls distributed reconstructive capacity.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 440, 3035, 19810, 82, 300, 2074, 4675, 47157, 7696, 294, 437, 309, 5498, 12631, 16891, 21673, 6042, 13, 50735], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07518037882718173, "compression_ratio": 1.5736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675997826203325e-12}, {"id": 58, "seek": 28874, "start": 297.14, "end": 306.86, "text": " Distributed reconstructive capacity. Let's break that down because, I mean, it sounds like some heavy academic jargon, but the concept behind it is actually the key to the whole paper.", "tokens": [50785, 9840, 2024, 4866, 16891, 21673, 6042, 13, 961, 311, 1821, 300, 760, 570, 11, 286, 914, 11, 309, 3263, 411, 512, 4676, 7778, 15181, 10660, 11, 457, 264, 3410, 2261, 309, 307, 767, 264, 2141, 281, 264, 1379, 3035, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07518037882718173, "compression_ratio": 1.5736842105263158, "no_speech_prob": 1.5675997826203325e-12}, {"id": 59, "seek": 30686, "start": 306.86, "end": 319.04, "text": " It breaks down to a very specific metric. The true measure of a civilization's memory is simply the number of living, breathing people who can actually understand, recreate, and extend those artifacts.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 9857, 760, 281, 257, 588, 2685, 20678, 13, 440, 2074, 3481, 295, 257, 18036, 311, 4675, 307, 2935, 264, 1230, 295, 2647, 11, 9570, 561, 567, 393, 767, 1223, 11, 25833, 11, 293, 10101, 729, 24617, 13, 50974], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06361657097226098, "compression_ratio": 1.3673469387755102, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169125500314907e-12}, {"id": 60, "seek": 31904, "start": 319.04, "end": 322.36, "text": " And do it without relying on the institution that originally made them, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 360, 309, 1553, 24140, 322, 264, 7818, 300, 7993, 1027, 552, 11, 558, 30, 50531], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07025129920557925, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.4772659007525335e-12}, {"id": 61, "seek": 31904, "start": 322.42, "end": 332.84000000000003, "text": " Yes. That is the crucial part. A society only truly remembers an invention if you could completely wipe out the company or the university or the government agency that created it,", "tokens": [50534, 1079, 13, 663, 307, 264, 11462, 644, 13, 316, 4086, 787, 4908, 26228, 364, 22265, 498, 291, 727, 2584, 14082, 484, 264, 2237, 420, 264, 5454, 420, 264, 2463, 7934, 300, 2942, 309, 11, 51055], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07025129920557925, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.4772659007525335e-12}, {"id": 62, "seek": 31904, "start": 333.04, "end": 338.62, "text": " and humanity itself would still retain the underlying competence to rebuild that invention from scratch.", "tokens": [51065, 293, 10243, 2564, 576, 920, 18340, 264, 14217, 39965, 281, 16877, 300, 22265, 490, 8459, 13, 51344], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07025129920557925, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.4772659007525335e-12}, {"id": 63, "seek": 31904, "start": 338.86, "end": 344.26, "text": " Okay. I have an analogy for this. It's like inheriting a fully functioning alien spaceship.", "tokens": [51356, 1033, 13, 286, 362, 364, 21663, 337, 341, 13, 467, 311, 411, 9484, 1748, 257, 4498, 18483, 12319, 39185, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.07025129920557925, "compression_ratio": 1.6366906474820144, "no_speech_prob": 1.4772659007525335e-12}, {"id": 64, "seek": 34426, "start": 344.26, "end": 345.78, "text": " Oh, I like this. Go on.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 286, 411, 341, 13, 1037, 322, 13, 50441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 65, "seek": 34426, "start": 346.24, "end": 352.3, "text": " Imagine you find a flying saucer parked in your backyard. You climb inside and you fiddle around.", "tokens": [50464, 11739, 291, 915, 257, 7137, 49181, 260, 28491, 294, 428, 20036, 13, 509, 10724, 1854, 293, 291, 24553, 2285, 926, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 66, "seek": 34426, "start": 352.62, "end": 356.53999999999996, "text": " And you figure out that pressing the green triangle makes it hover.", "tokens": [50783, 400, 291, 2573, 484, 300, 12417, 264, 3092, 13369, 1669, 309, 20076, 13, 50979], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 67, "seek": 34426, "start": 356.78, "end": 357.14, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [50991, 1033, 13, 51009], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 68, "seek": 34426, "start": 357.34, "end": 363.24, "text": " And pressing the red square makes it shoot forward. So you have the artifact. You can use it perfectly to fly around.", "tokens": [51019, 400, 12417, 264, 2182, 3732, 1669, 309, 3076, 2128, 13, 407, 291, 362, 264, 34806, 13, 509, 393, 764, 309, 6239, 281, 3603, 926, 13, 51314], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 69, "seek": 34426, "start": 363.36, "end": 364.34, "text": " But you didn't build it.", "tokens": [51320, 583, 291, 994, 380, 1322, 309, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 70, "seek": 34426, "start": 364.82, "end": 372.36, "text": " Exactly. If a single thruster breaks or if, like, the navigation array shorts out, you're entirely toast.", "tokens": [51393, 7587, 13, 759, 257, 2167, 739, 8393, 9857, 420, 498, 11, 411, 11, 264, 17346, 10225, 19848, 484, 11, 291, 434, 7696, 15354, 13, 51770], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.120635741796249, "compression_ratio": 1.6263736263736264, "no_speech_prob": 1.5610609593180724e-12}, {"id": 71, "seek": 37236, "start": 372.36, "end": 378.96000000000004, "text": " You don't know propulsion physics. You don't know the metallurgy of the hull. You are a consumer of the spaceship, not a creator of it.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 500, 380, 458, 49375, 10649, 13, 509, 500, 380, 458, 264, 20866, 374, 1480, 295, 264, 32335, 13, 509, 366, 257, 9711, 295, 264, 39185, 11, 406, 257, 14181, 295, 309, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 72, "seek": 37236, "start": 379.14, "end": 383.8, "text": " You possess the capability, but you lack the competence. That is a great way to frame it.", "tokens": [50704, 509, 17490, 264, 13759, 11, 457, 291, 5011, 264, 39965, 13, 663, 307, 257, 869, 636, 281, 3920, 309, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 73, "seek": 37236, "start": 383.84000000000003, "end": 384.8, "text": " Yeah. You're just pushing buttons.", "tokens": [50939, 865, 13, 509, 434, 445, 7380, 9905, 13, 50987], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 74, "seek": 37236, "start": 385.04, "end": 393.52000000000004, "text": " And history provides stark warnings about what happens when a society possesses sophisticated artifacts without retaining that underlying representational competence.", "tokens": [50999, 400, 2503, 6417, 17417, 30009, 466, 437, 2314, 562, 257, 4086, 17490, 279, 16950, 24617, 1553, 34936, 300, 14217, 2906, 1478, 39965, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 75, "seek": 37236, "start": 393.74, "end": 398.5, "text": " Oh, the paper brings up a magnificent historical illustration of this exact phenomenon, doesn't it?", "tokens": [51434, 876, 11, 264, 3035, 5607, 493, 257, 23690, 8584, 22645, 295, 341, 1900, 14029, 11, 1177, 380, 309, 30, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 76, "seek": 37236, "start": 398.58000000000004, "end": 400.04, "text": " Yes. Roman concrete.", "tokens": [51676, 1079, 13, 8566, 9859, 13, 51749], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08012518335561283, "compression_ratio": 1.691358024691358, "no_speech_prob": 1.3938725390919005e-12}, {"id": 77, "seek": 40004, "start": 400.04, "end": 413.3, "text": " I was really hoping we would get into this because, you know, we are talking about a civilization that built structures 2,000 years ago, structures like the Pantheon, massive aqueducts, deepwater harbors that are literally still standing today.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 390, 534, 7159, 321, 576, 483, 666, 341, 570, 11, 291, 458, 11, 321, 366, 1417, 466, 257, 18036, 300, 3094, 9227, 568, 11, 1360, 924, 2057, 11, 9227, 411, 264, 7557, 3322, 266, 11, 5994, 2373, 292, 11130, 82, 11, 2452, 8002, 2233, 65, 830, 300, 366, 3736, 920, 4877, 965, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08828849995389898, "compression_ratio": 1.4981132075471697, "no_speech_prob": 2.150735752687316e-12}, {"id": 78, "seek": 40004, "start": 413.46000000000004, "end": 418.08000000000004, "text": " And meanwhile, a modern concrete driveway sometimes cracks after one harsh winter.", "tokens": [51036, 400, 29252, 11, 257, 4363, 9859, 38276, 2171, 21770, 934, 472, 14897, 6355, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08828849995389898, "compression_ratio": 1.4981132075471697, "no_speech_prob": 2.150735752687316e-12}, {"id": 79, "seek": 40004, "start": 418.36, "end": 423.02000000000004, "text": " Exactly. It's wild. The contrast is staggering. So how do they do it?", "tokens": [51281, 7587, 13, 467, 311, 4868, 13, 440, 8712, 307, 42974, 13, 407, 577, 360, 436, 360, 309, 30, 51514], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08828849995389898, "compression_ratio": 1.4981132075471697, "no_speech_prob": 2.150735752687316e-12}, {"id": 80, "seek": 42302, "start": 423.02, "end": 431.44, "text": " Well, the Romans possessed a very specific formulation for concrete that involved volcanic ash, specifically a type called pozzolana.", "tokens": [50365, 1042, 11, 264, 20252, 29608, 257, 588, 2685, 37642, 337, 9859, 300, 3288, 35813, 12588, 11, 4682, 257, 2010, 1219, 714, 4313, 401, 2095, 13, 50786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10149221535188606, "compression_ratio": 1.5066666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.729401990878011e-12}, {"id": 81, "seek": 42302, "start": 431.56, "end": 432.85999999999996, "text": " Okay. Volcanic ash.", "tokens": [50792, 1033, 13, 8911, 7035, 299, 12588, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10149221535188606, "compression_ratio": 1.5066666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.729401990878011e-12}, {"id": 82, "seek": 42302, "start": 432.96, "end": 442.08, "text": " Right. And they mixed it with lime and seawater. Now, this wasn't just a strong building material. It actually involved an active chemical reaction.", "tokens": [50862, 1779, 13, 400, 436, 7467, 309, 365, 22035, 293, 369, 1607, 771, 13, 823, 11, 341, 2067, 380, 445, 257, 2068, 2390, 2527, 13, 467, 767, 3288, 364, 4967, 7313, 5480, 13, 51318], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10149221535188606, "compression_ratio": 1.5066666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.729401990878011e-12}, {"id": 83, "seek": 42302, "start": 442.2, "end": 443.9, "text": " Wait, active? Like it kept reacting?", "tokens": [51324, 3802, 11, 4967, 30, 1743, 309, 4305, 25817, 30, 51409], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10149221535188606, "compression_ratio": 1.5066666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.729401990878011e-12}, {"id": 84, "seek": 44390, "start": 443.9, "end": 458.02, "text": " Yes. It allowed the concrete to cure underwater and, amazingly, grow stronger over centuries. The seawater actually dissolved certain components and formed new, incredibly resilient crystals within the concrete matrix.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 467, 4350, 264, 9859, 281, 13698, 20967, 293, 11, 31762, 11, 1852, 7249, 670, 13926, 13, 440, 369, 1607, 771, 767, 30651, 1629, 6677, 293, 8693, 777, 11, 6252, 23699, 23772, 1951, 264, 9859, 8141, 13, 51071], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09487005129252395, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.868624612683112e-12}, {"id": 85, "seek": 44390, "start": 458.06, "end": 460.26, "text": " Oh, wow. Crystals growing inside the concrete.", "tokens": [51073, 876, 11, 6076, 13, 12267, 372, 1124, 4194, 1854, 264, 9859, 13, 51183], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09487005129252395, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.868624612683112e-12}, {"id": 86, "seek": 44390, "start": 460.41999999999996, "end": 463.62, "text": " They're called tobermorate. It was an absolute engineering marvel.", "tokens": [51191, 814, 434, 1219, 281, 607, 40220, 473, 13, 467, 390, 364, 8236, 7043, 23893, 13, 51351], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09487005129252395, "compression_ratio": 1.5586854460093897, "no_speech_prob": 1.868624612683112e-12}, {"id": 87, "seek": 46362, "start": 463.62, "end": 469.06, "text": " So they had this incredible technology. They built a massive empire with it. And then, you know, Rome falls.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 436, 632, 341, 4651, 2899, 13, 814, 3094, 257, 5994, 17506, 365, 309, 13, 400, 550, 11, 291, 458, 11, 12043, 8804, 13, 50637], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08206158040839935, "compression_ratio": 1.595890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 2.446628403346418e-12}, {"id": 88, "seek": 46362, "start": 469.68, "end": 469.78000000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50668, 1779, 13, 50673], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08206158040839935, "compression_ratio": 1.595890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 2.446628403346418e-12}, {"id": 89, "seek": 46362, "start": 470.06, "end": 476.96, "text": " And I assume the paper's point here is that the buildings themselves didn't vanish, but the mindset, the knowledge of how to make it did.", "tokens": [50687, 400, 286, 6552, 264, 3035, 311, 935, 510, 307, 300, 264, 7446, 2969, 994, 380, 43584, 11, 457, 264, 12543, 11, 264, 3601, 295, 577, 281, 652, 309, 630, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08206158040839935, "compression_ratio": 1.595890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 2.446628403346418e-12}, {"id": 90, "seek": 46362, "start": 477.22, "end": 489.6, "text": " Exactly. The artifacts survived for centuries. Subsequent generations of people live right among these towering marvels of engineering. But civilization lost the competence to recreate them.", "tokens": [51045, 7587, 13, 440, 24617, 14433, 337, 13926, 13, 8511, 11834, 317, 10593, 295, 561, 1621, 558, 3654, 613, 10567, 278, 23893, 82, 295, 7043, 13, 583, 18036, 2731, 264, 39965, 281, 25833, 552, 13, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08206158040839935, "compression_ratio": 1.595890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 2.446628403346418e-12}, {"id": 91, "seek": 46362, "start": 489.8, "end": 490.82, "text": " They lost the recipe.", "tokens": [51674, 814, 2731, 264, 6782, 13, 51725], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08206158040839935, "compression_ratio": 1.595890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 2.446628403346418e-12}, {"id": 92, "seek": 49082, "start": 490.82, "end": 501.62, "text": " The practical knowledge, the specific ratios of ash to lime, the understanding of the chemical interactions, what the paper calls the representation, was entirely lost.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8496, 3601, 11, 264, 2685, 32435, 295, 12588, 281, 22035, 11, 264, 3701, 295, 264, 7313, 13280, 11, 437, 264, 3035, 5498, 264, 10290, 11, 390, 7696, 2731, 13, 50905], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.046301187928189935, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851507570561315e-12}, {"id": 93, "seek": 49082, "start": 501.88, "end": 503.58, "text": " Because the supply chains broke down, right?", "tokens": [50918, 1436, 264, 5847, 12626, 6902, 760, 11, 558, 30, 51003], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.046301187928189935, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851507570561315e-12}, {"id": 94, "seek": 49082, "start": 503.78, "end": 513.54, "text": " Yes. The supply chains for the volcanic ash broke down. The master builders died without passing on the full depth of their knowledge. And that reconstructive capacity just fragmented.", "tokens": [51013, 1079, 13, 440, 5847, 12626, 337, 264, 35813, 12588, 6902, 760, 13, 440, 4505, 36281, 4539, 1553, 8437, 322, 264, 1577, 7161, 295, 641, 3601, 13, 400, 300, 16891, 21673, 6042, 445, 9241, 14684, 13, 51501], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.046301187928189935, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851507570561315e-12}, {"id": 95, "seek": 49082, "start": 513.72, "end": 515.5, "text": " And how long did it take us to figure it out again?", "tokens": [51510, 400, 577, 938, 630, 309, 747, 505, 281, 2573, 309, 484, 797, 30, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.046301187928189935, "compression_ratio": 1.6791044776119404, "no_speech_prob": 2.4851507570561315e-12}, {"id": 96, "seek": 51550, "start": 515.5, "end": 522.42, "text": " It took us until the modern era. We had to use electron microscopes and advanced X-ray diffraction to truly reverse engineer how they did it.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1890, 505, 1826, 264, 4363, 4249, 13, 492, 632, 281, 764, 6084, 30483, 279, 293, 7339, 1783, 12, 3458, 7593, 26766, 281, 4908, 9943, 11403, 577, 436, 630, 309, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06820968828703228, "compression_ratio": 1.565891472868217, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106500256100274e-12}, {"id": 97, "seek": 51550, "start": 522.64, "end": 536.36, "text": " Which is just wild to think about. I mean, you have hundreds of years of medieval citizens walking past the Pantheon, looking up at this massive unreinforced concrete dome, which is still the largest in the world, by the way, and essentially viewing it as magic.", "tokens": [50722, 3013, 307, 445, 4868, 281, 519, 466, 13, 286, 914, 11, 291, 362, 6779, 295, 924, 295, 24078, 7180, 4494, 1791, 264, 7557, 3322, 266, 11, 1237, 493, 412, 341, 5994, 20584, 259, 2994, 1232, 9859, 27191, 11, 597, 307, 920, 264, 6443, 294, 264, 1002, 11, 538, 264, 636, 11, 293, 4476, 17480, 309, 382, 5585, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.06820968828703228, "compression_ratio": 1.565891472868217, "no_speech_prob": 1.4106500256100274e-12}, {"id": 98, "seek": 53636, "start": 536.36, "end": 542.38, "text": " They had the artifact in their daily lives, but the civilizational memory of how it was created was dead.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 632, 264, 34806, 294, 641, 5212, 2909, 11, 457, 264, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 295, 577, 309, 390, 2942, 390, 3116, 13, 50666], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 99, "seek": 53636, "start": 542.5, "end": 543.5, "text": " Dead and gone.", "tokens": [50672, 12550, 293, 2780, 13, 50722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 100, "seek": 53636, "start": 543.94, "end": 547.74, "text": " Which brings me to a question for you, the listener, tuning into this deep dive.", "tokens": [50744, 3013, 5607, 385, 281, 257, 1168, 337, 291, 11, 264, 31569, 11, 15164, 666, 341, 2452, 9192, 13, 50934], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 101, "seek": 53636, "start": 547.84, "end": 548.96, "text": " It's a sobering question.", "tokens": [50939, 467, 311, 257, 26212, 278, 1168, 13, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 102, "seek": 53636, "start": 549.04, "end": 549.34, "text": " It is.", "tokens": [50999, 467, 307, 13, 51014], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 103, "seek": 53636, "start": 549.9, "end": 552.1, "text": " I want you to look around the room you're in right now.", "tokens": [51042, 286, 528, 291, 281, 574, 926, 264, 1808, 291, 434, 294, 558, 586, 13, 51152], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 104, "seek": 53636, "start": 552.62, "end": 557.66, "text": " Look at your phone, your laptop, the smart thermostat on your wall, the LED bulbs in your lamp.", "tokens": [51178, 2053, 412, 428, 2593, 11, 428, 10732, 11, 264, 4069, 8810, 39036, 322, 428, 2929, 11, 264, 11261, 32871, 294, 428, 12684, 13, 51430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10867162987037941, "compression_ratio": 1.5819672131147542, "no_speech_prob": 1.6619894479749653e-12}, {"id": 105, "seek": 55766, "start": 557.66, "end": 566.24, "text": " How many of those objects do you own? Versus how many could you actually rebuild from scratch if the global supply chain vanished tomorrow?", "tokens": [50365, 1012, 867, 295, 729, 6565, 360, 291, 1065, 30, 12226, 301, 577, 867, 727, 291, 767, 16877, 490, 8459, 498, 264, 4338, 5847, 5021, 37518, 4153, 30, 50794], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12068522958194508, "compression_ratio": 1.512396694214876, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404729800117754e-12}, {"id": 106, "seek": 55766, "start": 566.4599999999999, "end": 568.88, "text": " The answer is probably zero for most of us.", "tokens": [50805, 440, 1867, 307, 1391, 4018, 337, 881, 295, 505, 13, 50926], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12068522958194508, "compression_ratio": 1.512396694214876, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404729800117754e-12}, {"id": 107, "seek": 55766, "start": 568.9399999999999, "end": 572.2199999999999, "text": " Exactly. We are essentially surrounded by alien spaceships.", "tokens": [50929, 7587, 13, 492, 366, 4476, 13221, 538, 12319, 7673, 7640, 13, 51093], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12068522958194508, "compression_ratio": 1.512396694214876, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404729800117754e-12}, {"id": 108, "seek": 55766, "start": 572.3399999999999, "end": 578.98, "text": " We are swimming in artifacts. And, you know, this realization brings us to a critical historical friction point.", "tokens": [51099, 492, 366, 11989, 294, 24617, 13, 400, 11, 291, 458, 11, 341, 25138, 5607, 505, 281, 257, 4924, 8584, 17710, 935, 13, 51431], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12068522958194508, "compression_ratio": 1.512396694214876, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404729800117754e-12}, {"id": 109, "seek": 55766, "start": 579.3, "end": 579.7199999999999, "text": " Which is?", "tokens": [51447, 3013, 307, 30, 51468], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12068522958194508, "compression_ratio": 1.512396694214876, "no_speech_prob": 1.3404729800117754e-12}, {"id": 110, "seek": 57972, "start": 579.72, "end": 588.52, "text": " If civilizational memory relies so heavily on living human beings actually knowing how to build things, how did we ever manage to progress this far?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 30910, 370, 10950, 322, 2647, 1952, 8958, 767, 5276, 577, 281, 1322, 721, 11, 577, 630, 321, 1562, 3067, 281, 4205, 341, 1400, 30, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061283197488870705, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096265608428248e-12}, {"id": 111, "seek": 57972, "start": 588.62, "end": 589.28, "text": " That's a good point.", "tokens": [50810, 663, 311, 257, 665, 935, 13, 50843], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061283197488870705, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096265608428248e-12}, {"id": 112, "seek": 57972, "start": 589.52, "end": 593.9, "text": " Why didn't knowledge just stay locked up with the original inventors throughout history?", "tokens": [50855, 1545, 994, 380, 3601, 445, 1754, 9376, 493, 365, 264, 3380, 7962, 830, 3710, 2503, 30, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061283197488870705, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096265608428248e-12}, {"id": 113, "seek": 57972, "start": 593.9, "end": 607.98, "text": " Hang on. Because, I mean, if I invent something world-changing in the year 1200, say I figure out a new way to smelt steel or navigate by the stars, my absolute first instinct is to keep it a heavily guarded secret.", "tokens": [51074, 14070, 322, 13, 1436, 11, 286, 914, 11, 498, 286, 7962, 746, 1002, 12, 27123, 294, 264, 1064, 29139, 11, 584, 286, 2573, 484, 257, 777, 636, 281, 899, 2018, 8269, 420, 12350, 538, 264, 6105, 11, 452, 8236, 700, 16556, 307, 281, 1066, 309, 257, 10950, 44157, 4054, 13, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.061283197488870705, "compression_ratio": 1.5490196078431373, "no_speech_prob": 1.3096265608428248e-12}, {"id": 114, "seek": 60798, "start": 607.98, "end": 611.22, "text": " Of course. So you can extract all the wealth and power from it.", "tokens": [50365, 2720, 1164, 13, 407, 291, 393, 8947, 439, 264, 7203, 293, 1347, 490, 309, 13, 50527], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 115, "seek": 60798, "start": 611.3000000000001, "end": 613.4, "text": " Right. I don't want to teach everyone else. I want a monopoly.", "tokens": [50531, 1779, 13, 286, 500, 380, 528, 281, 2924, 1518, 1646, 13, 286, 528, 257, 37061, 13, 50636], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 116, "seek": 60798, "start": 613.9200000000001, "end": 618.3000000000001, "text": " That is the natural incentive. Institutions have always desired a monopoly on knowledge.", "tokens": [50662, 663, 307, 264, 3303, 22346, 13, 33897, 3666, 362, 1009, 14721, 257, 37061, 322, 3601, 13, 50881], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 117, "seek": 60798, "start": 618.74, "end": 626.1, "text": " But the paper points out that historically, technological progress was defined by one overarching, almost unstoppable force.", "tokens": [50903, 583, 264, 3035, 2793, 484, 300, 16180, 11, 18439, 4205, 390, 7642, 538, 472, 45501, 11, 1920, 48261, 3464, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 118, "seek": 60798, "start": 626.16, "end": 626.62, "text": " And what is that?", "tokens": [51274, 400, 437, 307, 300, 30, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 119, "seek": 60798, "start": 627.3000000000001, "end": 635.1, "text": " Diffusion. The text highlights a profound asymmetry in human innovation. Discovering something new is incredibly expensive.", "tokens": [51331, 413, 3661, 5704, 13, 440, 2487, 14254, 257, 14382, 37277, 9889, 294, 1952, 8504, 13, 40386, 278, 746, 777, 307, 6252, 5124, 13, 51721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 120, "seek": 60798, "start": 635.36, "end": 637.0, "text": " Expensive in terms of time and money, yeah.", "tokens": [51734, 21391, 2953, 294, 2115, 295, 565, 293, 1460, 11, 1338, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11388501964631628, "compression_ratio": 1.5843373493975903, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370865387789867e-12}, {"id": 121, "seek": 63700, "start": 637.0, "end": 645.68, "text": " It requires years of blind experimentation, massive capital investment, institutional coordination, and profound intellectual risk.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 7029, 924, 295, 6865, 37142, 11, 5994, 4238, 6078, 11, 18391, 21252, 11, 293, 14382, 12576, 3148, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09845022151344701, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108538114512072e-12}, {"id": 122, "seek": 63700, "start": 646.0, "end": 651.36, "text": " But teaching that established principle to the next generation, that is remarkably cheap.", "tokens": [50815, 583, 4571, 300, 7545, 8665, 281, 264, 958, 5125, 11, 300, 307, 37381, 7084, 13, 51083], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09845022151344701, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108538114512072e-12}, {"id": 123, "seek": 63700, "start": 651.46, "end": 655.8, "text": " Oh, right. Because you don't have to reinvent the wheel. You just have to show someone how the wheel rolls.", "tokens": [51088, 876, 11, 558, 13, 1436, 291, 500, 380, 362, 281, 33477, 264, 5589, 13, 509, 445, 362, 281, 855, 1580, 577, 264, 5589, 15767, 13, 51305], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09845022151344701, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108538114512072e-12}, {"id": 124, "seek": 63700, "start": 655.92, "end": 657.62, "text": " The trial and error is over.", "tokens": [51311, 440, 7308, 293, 6713, 307, 670, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09845022151344701, "compression_ratio": 1.5633187772925765, "no_speech_prob": 1.6108538114512072e-12}, {"id": 125, "seek": 65762, "start": 657.62, "end": 665.22, "text": " Exactly. And because of this asymmetry, knowledge historically always escaped the institutions that created it.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 400, 570, 295, 341, 37277, 9889, 11, 3601, 16180, 1009, 20397, 264, 8142, 300, 2942, 309, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13244342803955078, "compression_ratio": 1.6448979591836734, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552111464964269e-12}, {"id": 126, "seek": 65762, "start": 665.42, "end": 670.08, "text": " It leaked out and became what the author calls ordinary cultural competence.", "tokens": [50755, 467, 31779, 484, 293, 3062, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 10547, 6988, 39965, 13, 50988], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13244342803955078, "compression_ratio": 1.6448979591836734, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552111464964269e-12}, {"id": 127, "seek": 65762, "start": 670.3, "end": 672.32, "text": " So it starts elite and becomes ordinary.", "tokens": [50999, 407, 309, 3719, 17801, 293, 3643, 10547, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13244342803955078, "compression_ratio": 1.6448979591836734, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552111464964269e-12}, {"id": 128, "seek": 65762, "start": 672.88, "end": 683.46, "text": " Precisely. And the paper details this historical trajectory with several compelling examples, starting with the very foundation of recorded history itself, which is writing.", "tokens": [51128, 48746, 736, 13, 400, 264, 3035, 4365, 341, 8584, 21512, 365, 2940, 20050, 5110, 11, 2891, 365, 264, 588, 7030, 295, 8287, 2503, 2564, 11, 597, 307, 3579, 13, 51657], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13244342803955078, "compression_ratio": 1.6448979591836734, "no_speech_prob": 1.5552111464964269e-12}, {"id": 129, "seek": 68346, "start": 683.46, "end": 689.32, "text": " Yeah. If you were a king in ancient Mesopotamia, reading and writing wasn't something the general public did.", "tokens": [50365, 865, 13, 759, 291, 645, 257, 4867, 294, 7832, 17485, 45225, 335, 654, 11, 3760, 293, 3579, 2067, 380, 746, 264, 2674, 1908, 630, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10855539639790852, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281943020738821e-12}, {"id": 130, "seek": 68346, "start": 689.72, "end": 695.8000000000001, "text": " It was basically a mystical elite technology guarded by a highly specialized scribe class.", "tokens": [50678, 467, 390, 1936, 257, 40565, 17801, 2899, 44157, 538, 257, 5405, 19813, 5545, 650, 1508, 13, 50982], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10855539639790852, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281943020738821e-12}, {"id": 131, "seek": 68346, "start": 696.64, "end": 700.9200000000001, "text": " Uniform was immensely complex. It took years of dedicated study to master.", "tokens": [51024, 1156, 8629, 390, 38674, 3997, 13, 467, 1890, 924, 295, 8374, 2979, 281, 4505, 13, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10855539639790852, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281943020738821e-12}, {"id": 132, "seek": 68346, "start": 701.48, "end": 706.34, "text": " It granted massive administrative, economic, and political authority to a tiny fraction of the population.", "tokens": [51266, 467, 12344, 5994, 17900, 11, 4836, 11, 293, 3905, 8281, 281, 257, 5870, 14135, 295, 264, 4415, 13, 51509], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10855539639790852, "compression_ratio": 1.5528455284552845, "no_speech_prob": 1.7281943020738821e-12}, {"id": 133, "seek": 70634, "start": 706.34, "end": 708.76, "text": " They were basically the gatekeepers of the empire's memory.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 645, 1936, 264, 8539, 43153, 295, 264, 17506, 311, 4675, 13, 50486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 134, "seek": 70634, "start": 708.96, "end": 712.4, "text": " They were. But over centuries, that technology diffused.", "tokens": [50496, 814, 645, 13, 583, 670, 13926, 11, 300, 2899, 7593, 4717, 13, 50668], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 135, "seek": 70634, "start": 712.76, "end": 715.48, "text": " Phonetic alphabets were developed, simplifying the system dramatically.", "tokens": [50686, 2623, 266, 3532, 419, 950, 455, 1385, 645, 4743, 11, 6883, 5489, 264, 1185, 17548, 13, 50822], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 136, "seek": 70634, "start": 715.9, "end": 718.0, "text": " The knowledge escaped the scribal class.", "tokens": [50843, 440, 3601, 20397, 264, 39435, 304, 1508, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 137, "seek": 70634, "start": 718.14, "end": 719.88, "text": " Because teaching it became cheaper and easier.", "tokens": [50955, 1436, 4571, 309, 3062, 12284, 293, 3571, 13, 51042], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 138, "seek": 70634, "start": 720.2, "end": 720.5600000000001, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51058, 1079, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 139, "seek": 70634, "start": 721.2800000000001, "end": 726.1800000000001, "text": " The true civilizational achievement of writing wasn't just that clay tablets survived.", "tokens": [51112, 440, 2074, 5605, 590, 1478, 15838, 295, 3579, 2067, 380, 445, 300, 13517, 27622, 14433, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 140, "seek": 70634, "start": 726.86, "end": 735.5600000000001, "text": " It was that reading and writing gradually transitioned from an elite institutional secret into an ordinary public expectation.", "tokens": [51391, 467, 390, 300, 3760, 293, 3579, 13145, 47346, 490, 364, 17801, 18391, 4054, 666, 364, 10547, 1908, 14334, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16198084375879787, "compression_ratio": 1.6390728476821192, "no_speech_prob": 1.6881577516100754e-12}, {"id": 141, "seek": 73556, "start": 735.56, "end": 740.76, "text": " And the paper tracks this exact same trajectory with higher level concepts, too, right?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 264, 3035, 10218, 341, 1900, 912, 21512, 365, 2946, 1496, 10392, 11, 886, 11, 558, 30, 50625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 142, "seek": 73556, "start": 740.8399999999999, "end": 742.16, "text": " Like the invention of calculus.", "tokens": [50629, 1743, 264, 22265, 295, 33400, 13, 50695], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 143, "seek": 73556, "start": 742.56, "end": 744.4, "text": " Calculus is a fascinating case study.", "tokens": [50715, 3511, 36002, 307, 257, 10343, 1389, 2979, 13, 50807], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 144, "seek": 73556, "start": 745.06, "end": 753.5799999999999, "text": " When Isaac Newton and Gottfried Wilhelm Leibniz independently developed calculus in the late 17th century, it was mind-bending intellectual property.", "tokens": [50840, 1133, 22505, 19541, 293, 19133, 22773, 9483, 48319, 1456, 897, 77, 590, 21761, 4743, 33400, 294, 264, 3469, 3282, 392, 4901, 11, 309, 390, 1575, 12, 65, 2029, 12576, 4707, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 145, "seek": 73556, "start": 753.7199999999999, "end": 755.2399999999999, "text": " It was basically magic at the time.", "tokens": [51273, 467, 390, 1936, 5585, 412, 264, 565, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 146, "seek": 73556, "start": 755.42, "end": 759.7199999999999, "text": " It was the absolute bleeding edge frontier of human thought.", "tokens": [51358, 467, 390, 264, 8236, 19312, 4691, 35853, 295, 1952, 1194, 13, 51573], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 147, "seek": 73556, "start": 759.9, "end": 761.8399999999999, "text": " The mathematics of continuous change.", "tokens": [51582, 440, 18666, 295, 10957, 1319, 13, 51679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13550066716462664, "compression_ratio": 1.5294117647058822, "no_speech_prob": 2.0206284562229726e-12}, {"id": 148, "seek": 76184, "start": 761.84, "end": 766.6600000000001, "text": " But it didn't stay locked in their minds or within the walls of Cambridge or the courts of Hanover.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 309, 994, 380, 1754, 9376, 294, 641, 9634, 420, 1951, 264, 7920, 295, 24876, 420, 264, 14141, 295, 7820, 3570, 13, 50606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11244882090707843, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205795807886172e-12}, {"id": 149, "seek": 76184, "start": 766.9, "end": 767.4, "text": " It got out.", "tokens": [50618, 467, 658, 484, 13, 50643], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11244882090707843, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205795807886172e-12}, {"id": 150, "seek": 76184, "start": 767.8000000000001, "end": 772.94, "text": " It was formalized, standardized into textbooks, and absorbed into civilization's shared memory.", "tokens": [50663, 467, 390, 9860, 1602, 11, 31677, 666, 33587, 11, 293, 20799, 666, 18036, 311, 5507, 4675, 13, 50920], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11244882090707843, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205795807886172e-12}, {"id": 151, "seek": 76184, "start": 773.64, "end": 779.6600000000001, "text": " Today, modern structural engineers don't have to possess the singular genius of Newton to build a suspension bridge.", "tokens": [50955, 2692, 11, 4363, 15067, 11955, 500, 380, 362, 281, 17490, 264, 20010, 14017, 295, 19541, 281, 1322, 257, 15771, 7283, 13, 51256], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11244882090707843, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205795807886172e-12}, {"id": 152, "seek": 76184, "start": 780.0, "end": 784.2800000000001, "text": " They simply learn calculus as a standard staple of ordinary scientific education.", "tokens": [51273, 814, 2935, 1466, 33400, 382, 257, 3832, 32361, 295, 10547, 8134, 3309, 13, 51487], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11244882090707843, "compression_ratio": 1.5675675675675675, "no_speech_prob": 1.9205795807886172e-12}, {"id": 153, "seek": 78428, "start": 784.28, "end": 790.6999999999999, "text": " So the representation, the underlying logic of how the math works, was successfully transferred from the inventors to the general public.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 264, 10290, 11, 264, 14217, 9952, 295, 577, 264, 5221, 1985, 11, 390, 10727, 15809, 490, 264, 7962, 830, 281, 264, 2674, 1908, 13, 50686], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 154, "seek": 78428, "start": 791.24, "end": 791.72, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50713, 7587, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 155, "seek": 78428, "start": 792.1, "end": 795.8, "text": " But, you know, early scientists actually had to be forced into this arrangement, didn't they?", "tokens": [50756, 583, 11, 291, 458, 11, 2440, 7708, 767, 632, 281, 312, 7579, 666, 341, 17620, 11, 994, 380, 436, 30, 50941], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 156, "seek": 78428, "start": 795.88, "end": 796.5799999999999, "text": " They did.", "tokens": [50945, 814, 630, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 157, "seek": 78428, "start": 796.74, "end": 802.28, "text": " Yeah, I remember reading that before scientific journals existed, scientists used to hide their discoveries in anagrams.", "tokens": [50988, 865, 11, 286, 1604, 3760, 300, 949, 8134, 29621, 13135, 11, 7708, 1143, 281, 6479, 641, 28400, 294, 364, 3914, 82, 13, 51265], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 158, "seek": 78428, "start": 803.0799999999999, "end": 810.74, "text": " Like, Galileo would discover the rings of Saturn, but instead of publishing it clearly, he'd send out a scrambled sentence.", "tokens": [51305, 1743, 11, 46576, 78, 576, 4411, 264, 11136, 295, 24601, 11, 457, 2602, 295, 17832, 309, 4448, 11, 415, 1116, 2845, 484, 257, 49127, 8174, 13, 51688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11410480737686157, "compression_ratio": 1.5865384615384615, "no_speech_prob": 1.6232403875909851e-12}, {"id": 159, "seek": 81074, "start": 810.74, "end": 816.5, "text": " Right, so no one else could steal his work, but he could later unscramble it to prove he was the first to see it.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 11, 370, 572, 472, 1646, 727, 11009, 702, 589, 11, 457, 415, 727, 1780, 2693, 66, 48382, 309, 281, 7081, 415, 390, 264, 700, 281, 536, 309, 13, 50653], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10457495069995369, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 160, "seek": 81074, "start": 816.58, "end": 818.28, "text": " Exactly. It's such a funny workaround.", "tokens": [50657, 7587, 13, 467, 311, 1270, 257, 4074, 589, 25762, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10457495069995369, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 161, "seek": 81074, "start": 818.5, "end": 822.5, "text": " It's an excellent piece of history, and it perfectly illustrates the author's point.", "tokens": [50753, 467, 311, 364, 7103, 2522, 295, 2503, 11, 293, 309, 6239, 41718, 264, 3793, 311, 935, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10457495069995369, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 162, "seek": 81074, "start": 823.04, "end": 830.44, "text": " The creation of scientific journals by institutions like the Royal Society wasn't just a polite way for scientists to share news.", "tokens": [50980, 440, 8016, 295, 8134, 29621, 538, 8142, 411, 264, 12717, 13742, 2067, 380, 445, 257, 25171, 636, 337, 7708, 281, 2073, 2583, 13, 51350], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10457495069995369, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 163, "seek": 81074, "start": 830.8, "end": 831.58, "text": " What was it, then?", "tokens": [51368, 708, 390, 309, 11, 550, 30, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10457495069995369, "compression_ratio": 1.562753036437247, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080595835286538e-12}, {"id": 164, "seek": 83158, "start": 831.58, "end": 838.6800000000001, "text": " The author argues that journals were deliberately designed mechanisms meant to convert private insight into collective memory.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 38218, 300, 29621, 645, 23506, 4761, 15902, 4140, 281, 7620, 4551, 11269, 666, 12590, 4675, 13, 50720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 165, "seek": 83158, "start": 839.58, "end": 843.0200000000001, "text": " Peer review forced scientists to abandon the anagrams.", "tokens": [50765, 2396, 260, 3131, 7579, 7708, 281, 9072, 264, 364, 3914, 82, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 166, "seek": 83158, "start": 843.1, "end": 846.2800000000001, "text": " Ah, so if you wanted the credit, you had to explain the work.", "tokens": [50941, 2438, 11, 370, 498, 291, 1415, 264, 5397, 11, 291, 632, 281, 2903, 264, 589, 13, 51100], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 167, "seek": 83158, "start": 846.6, "end": 847.1600000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51116, 48746, 736, 13, 51144], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 168, "seek": 83158, "start": 847.62, "end": 857.5400000000001, "text": " If you wanted the prestige of discovery, you had to explicitly expose your methods, your underlying assumptions, and your evidence to public examination.", "tokens": [51167, 759, 291, 1415, 264, 42531, 295, 12114, 11, 291, 632, 281, 20803, 19219, 428, 7150, 11, 428, 14217, 17695, 11, 293, 428, 4467, 281, 1908, 23874, 13, 51663], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 169, "seek": 83158, "start": 858.22, "end": 859.62, "text": " You had to hand over the representation.", "tokens": [51697, 509, 632, 281, 1011, 670, 264, 10290, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12863397598266602, "compression_ratio": 1.6816479400749065, "no_speech_prob": 1.489938055744544e-12}, {"id": 170, "seek": 85962, "start": 859.62, "end": 862.44, "text": " And engineering followed the same path, didn't it?", "tokens": [50365, 400, 7043, 6263, 264, 912, 3100, 11, 994, 380, 309, 30, 50506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 171, "seek": 85962, "start": 862.62, "end": 873.34, "text": " Moving from secretive guild workshops, where a master craftsman held all the knowledge, to a public discipline with standardized technical drawings and, like, university curricula.", "tokens": [50515, 14242, 490, 4054, 488, 37435, 19162, 11, 689, 257, 4505, 27831, 1601, 5167, 439, 264, 3601, 11, 281, 257, 1908, 13635, 365, 31677, 6191, 18618, 293, 11, 411, 11, 5454, 13179, 3780, 13, 51051], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 172, "seek": 85962, "start": 873.44, "end": 877.66, "text": " Yes, a complete shift from private hoarding to public infrastructure.", "tokens": [51056, 1079, 11, 257, 3566, 5513, 490, 4551, 45940, 278, 281, 1908, 6896, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 173, "seek": 85962, "start": 877.98, "end": 880.78, "text": " I have to challenge this golden age of diffusion idea, though.", "tokens": [51283, 286, 362, 281, 3430, 341, 9729, 3205, 295, 25242, 1558, 11, 1673, 13, 51423], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 174, "seek": 85962, "start": 880.84, "end": 882.24, "text": " It sounds a bit too neat, you know.", "tokens": [51426, 467, 3263, 257, 857, 886, 10654, 11, 291, 458, 13, 51496], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 175, "seek": 85962, "start": 882.8, "end": 886.0600000000001, "text": " History is full of people violently protecting their secrets.", "tokens": [51524, 12486, 307, 1577, 295, 561, 46728, 12316, 641, 14093, 13, 51687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 176, "seek": 85962, "start": 886.22, "end": 886.86, "text": " Oh, absolutely.", "tokens": [51695, 876, 11, 3122, 13, 51727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09945517453280363, "compression_ratio": 1.5469255663430421, "no_speech_prob": 1.43273077863465e-12}, {"id": 177, "seek": 88686, "start": 886.86, "end": 889.02, "text": " Like, what about the Venetian glassmakers?", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 437, 466, 264, 11182, 302, 952, 4276, 15870, 30, 50473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 178, "seek": 88686, "start": 889.82, "end": 897.32, "text": " The Republic of Venice literally threatened to assassinate any glassmaker who tried to leave the island of Murano because their mirror-making technology was so valuable.", "tokens": [50513, 440, 5564, 295, 32707, 3736, 18268, 281, 16475, 13923, 604, 4276, 18821, 567, 3031, 281, 1856, 264, 6077, 295, 9373, 3730, 570, 641, 8013, 12, 12402, 2899, 390, 370, 8263, 13, 50888], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 179, "seek": 88686, "start": 897.6, "end": 898.36, "text": " That's not diffusion.", "tokens": [50902, 663, 311, 406, 25242, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 180, "seek": 88686, "start": 898.66, "end": 900.26, "text": " That's hoarding at the point of a sword.", "tokens": [50955, 663, 311, 45940, 278, 412, 264, 935, 295, 257, 10576, 13, 51035], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 181, "seek": 88686, "start": 900.52, "end": 901.38, "text": " That is a fair point.", "tokens": [51048, 663, 307, 257, 3143, 935, 13, 51091], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 182, "seek": 88686, "start": 901.58, "end": 905.28, "text": " And the author doesn't deny the violence or the intense desire to hoard.", "tokens": [51101, 400, 264, 3793, 1177, 380, 15744, 264, 6270, 420, 264, 9447, 7516, 281, 45940, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 183, "seek": 88686, "start": 906.14, "end": 911.26, "text": " The paper completely acknowledges that institutions have always tried to capture and protect their innovations.", "tokens": [51329, 440, 3035, 2584, 15195, 2880, 300, 8142, 362, 1009, 3031, 281, 7983, 293, 2371, 641, 24283, 13, 51585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 184, "seek": 88686, "start": 912.0600000000001, "end": 914.36, "text": " Okay, so they admit the Venetians were ruthless.", "tokens": [51625, 1033, 11, 370, 436, 9796, 264, 11182, 302, 2567, 645, 47096, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1297003428141276, "compression_ratio": 1.6803797468354431, "no_speech_prob": 1.942742841598566e-12}, {"id": 185, "seek": 91436, "start": 914.36, "end": 915.12, "text": " They do.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 360, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 186, "seek": 91436, "start": 915.58, "end": 917.72, "text": " The Venetian glassmakers are a prime example.", "tokens": [50426, 440, 11182, 302, 952, 4276, 15870, 366, 257, 5835, 1365, 13, 50533], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 187, "seek": 91436, "start": 918.1800000000001, "end": 919.5, "text": " The guild protects its secret.", "tokens": [50556, 440, 37435, 22583, 1080, 4054, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 188, "seek": 91436, "start": 920.04, "end": 922.86, "text": " The modern firm patents its manufacturing process.", "tokens": [50649, 440, 4363, 6174, 38142, 1080, 11096, 1399, 13, 50790], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 189, "seek": 91436, "start": 923.24, "end": 925.0, "text": " Governments classify military tech.", "tokens": [50809, 5515, 1117, 33872, 4632, 7553, 13, 50897], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 190, "seek": 91436, "start": 925.38, "end": 928.6, "text": " But the vital phrase in the paper is temporary advantage.", "tokens": [50916, 583, 264, 11707, 9535, 294, 264, 3035, 307, 13413, 5002, 13, 51077], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 191, "seek": 91436, "start": 929.1, "end": 930.74, "text": " Ah, temporary.", "tokens": [51102, 2438, 11, 13413, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.26453848618727466, "compression_ratio": 1.4497041420118344, "no_speech_prob": 1.4661681157351891e-12}, {"id": 192, "seek": 93074, "start": 930.74, "end": 936.46, "text": " So no matter how hard they try to build a wall around the knowledge, it inevitably fails.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 572, 1871, 577, 1152, 436, 853, 281, 1322, 257, 2929, 926, 264, 3601, 11, 309, 28171, 18199, 13, 50651], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 193, "seek": 93074, "start": 937.22, "end": 944.92, "text": " If we connect this to the bigger picture, civilization advances exactly because the immense cost of discovery doesn't have to be paid repeatedly.", "tokens": [50689, 759, 321, 1745, 341, 281, 264, 3801, 3036, 11, 18036, 25297, 2293, 570, 264, 22920, 2063, 295, 12114, 1177, 380, 362, 281, 312, 4835, 18227, 13, 51074], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 194, "seek": 93074, "start": 945.26, "end": 948.24, "text": " And those walls always eventually crumble.", "tokens": [51091, 400, 729, 7920, 1009, 4728, 47478, 13, 51240], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 195, "seek": 93074, "start": 948.46, "end": 949.6800000000001, "text": " Because someone always talks.", "tokens": [51251, 1436, 1580, 1009, 6686, 13, 51312], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 196, "seek": 93074, "start": 949.8, "end": 950.6, "text": " Or sneaks out.", "tokens": [51318, 1610, 9244, 5461, 484, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 197, "seek": 93074, "start": 951.02, "end": 953.04, "text": " The Venetians couldn't keep their secrets forever.", "tokens": [51379, 440, 11182, 302, 2567, 2809, 380, 1066, 641, 14093, 5680, 13, 51480], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 198, "seek": 93074, "start": 953.54, "end": 954.58, "text": " Glassmakers were bribed.", "tokens": [51505, 23752, 15870, 645, 272, 2024, 292, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 199, "seek": 93074, "start": 954.66, "end": 955.84, "text": " They smuggled out techniques.", "tokens": [51561, 814, 899, 3562, 1493, 484, 7512, 13, 51620], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 200, "seek": 93074, "start": 956.02, "end": 957.82, "text": " Competitors reverse engineer the mirrors.", "tokens": [51629, 32216, 9862, 9943, 11403, 264, 24238, 13, 51719], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 201, "seek": 93074, "start": 957.92, "end": 959.52, "text": " And patents eventually expire, too.", "tokens": [51724, 400, 38142, 4728, 45447, 11, 886, 13, 51804], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1527546983424241, "compression_ratio": 1.584375, "no_speech_prob": 1.661379475832725e-12}, {"id": 202, "seek": 95952, "start": 959.52, "end": 960.16, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1877185252674839, "compression_ratio": 1.5421052631578946, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305392586997812e-12}, {"id": 203, "seek": 95952, "start": 960.8, "end": 967.66, "text": " The underlying knowledge, the representation, always escaped the original institution and became a permanent part of humanity's conceptual infrastructure.", "tokens": [50429, 440, 14217, 3601, 11, 264, 10290, 11, 1009, 20397, 264, 3380, 7818, 293, 3062, 257, 10996, 644, 295, 10243, 311, 24106, 6896, 13, 50772], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1877185252674839, "compression_ratio": 1.5421052631578946, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305392586997812e-12}, {"id": 204, "seek": 95952, "start": 968.16, "end": 974.12, "text": " The institution got a temporary economic or political monopoly, but civilization got a permanent upgrade.", "tokens": [50797, 440, 7818, 658, 257, 13413, 4836, 420, 3905, 37061, 11, 457, 18036, 658, 257, 10996, 11484, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1877185252674839, "compression_ratio": 1.5421052631578946, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305392586997812e-12}, {"id": 205, "seek": 95952, "start": 974.48, "end": 975.52, "text": " That makes total sense.", "tokens": [51113, 663, 1669, 3217, 2020, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1877185252674839, "compression_ratio": 1.5421052631578946, "no_speech_prob": 1.5305392586997812e-12}, {"id": 206, "seek": 97552, "start": 975.52, "end": 980.02, "text": " The historical norm is that invention happens in a closed, locked room.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 8584, 2026, 307, 300, 22265, 2314, 294, 257, 5395, 11, 9376, 1808, 13, 50590], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 207, "seek": 97552, "start": 980.6999999999999, "end": 984.9399999999999, "text": " It generates a massive amount of wealth or power for the people inside that room for a while.", "tokens": [50624, 467, 23815, 257, 5994, 2372, 295, 7203, 420, 1347, 337, 264, 561, 1854, 300, 1808, 337, 257, 1339, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 208, "seek": 97552, "start": 985.0799999999999, "end": 985.18, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50843, 1779, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 209, "seek": 97552, "start": 985.56, "end": 987.22, "text": " But eventually the door cracks open.", "tokens": [50867, 583, 4728, 264, 2853, 21770, 1269, 13, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 210, "seek": 97552, "start": 987.5, "end": 989.0799999999999, "text": " The knowledge spills out into the street.", "tokens": [50964, 440, 3601, 637, 2565, 484, 666, 264, 4838, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 211, "seek": 97552, "start": 989.38, "end": 991.64, "text": " And humanity as a whole levels up.", "tokens": [51058, 400, 10243, 382, 257, 1379, 4358, 493, 13, 51171], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 212, "seek": 97552, "start": 992.36, "end": 993.62, "text": " That's the engine of progress.", "tokens": [51207, 663, 311, 264, 2848, 295, 4205, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 213, "seek": 97552, "start": 993.92, "end": 995.14, "text": " That was the engine of progress.", "tokens": [51285, 663, 390, 264, 2848, 295, 4205, 13, 51346], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 214, "seek": 97552, "start": 995.38, "end": 995.5, "text": " It was.", "tokens": [51358, 467, 390, 13, 51364], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 215, "seek": 97552, "start": 995.64, "end": 995.8199999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51371, 1033, 13, 51380], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 216, "seek": 97552, "start": 996.04, "end": 996.22, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [51391, 865, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21497687926659217, "compression_ratio": 1.6228070175438596, "no_speech_prob": 2.2627769883515336e-12}, {"id": 217, "seek": 99622, "start": 996.22, "end": 1004.74, "text": " But the central concern of this deep dive and the core of the affliction text is that the digital age has completely inverted this historical norm.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 264, 5777, 3136, 295, 341, 2452, 9192, 293, 264, 4965, 295, 264, 2096, 75, 4105, 2487, 307, 300, 264, 4562, 3205, 575, 2584, 38969, 341, 8584, 2026, 13, 50791], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12475742896397908, "compression_ratio": 1.489795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411006447351496e-12}, {"id": 218, "seek": 99622, "start": 1005.38, "end": 1009.5600000000001, "text": " We have entered what the author calls the era of institutional capture.", "tokens": [50823, 492, 362, 9065, 437, 264, 3793, 5498, 264, 4249, 295, 18391, 7983, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12475742896397908, "compression_ratio": 1.489795918367347, "no_speech_prob": 1.7411006447351496e-12}, {"id": 219, "seek": 100956, "start": 1009.56, "end": 1018.9399999999999, "text": " And this is the pivot where the paper gets genuinely unnerving because it argues that modern digital platforms are fundamentally changing how knowledge moves through society.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 307, 264, 14538, 689, 264, 3035, 2170, 17839, 517, 1193, 798, 570, 309, 38218, 300, 4363, 4562, 9473, 366, 17879, 4473, 577, 3601, 6067, 807, 4086, 13, 50834], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 220, "seek": 100956, "start": 1019.14, "end": 1020.2399999999999, "text": " They're reversing the flow.", "tokens": [50844, 814, 434, 14582, 278, 264, 3095, 13, 50899], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 221, "seek": 100956, "start": 1020.3399999999999, "end": 1020.4799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50904, 1779, 13, 50911], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 222, "seek": 100956, "start": 1020.78, "end": 1031.08, "text": " Instead of the historical pattern where the blueprint eventually leaks out to the public, these modern systems distribute the outputs of the knowledge, the convenience, the final polished product.", "tokens": [50926, 7156, 295, 264, 8584, 5102, 689, 264, 35868, 4728, 28885, 484, 281, 264, 1908, 11, 613, 4363, 3652, 20594, 264, 23930, 295, 264, 3601, 11, 264, 19283, 11, 264, 2572, 29079, 1674, 13, 51441], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 223, "seek": 100956, "start": 1031.3, "end": 1034.78, "text": " But they successfully and permanently retain the representations.", "tokens": [51452, 583, 436, 10727, 293, 24042, 18340, 264, 33358, 13, 51626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 224, "seek": 100956, "start": 1035.12, "end": 1037.34, "text": " The actual understanding of how the thing works.", "tokens": [51643, 440, 3539, 3701, 295, 577, 264, 551, 1985, 13, 51754], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13352383919132566, "compression_ratio": 1.6645367412140575, "no_speech_prob": 1.5127087950317364e-12}, {"id": 225, "seek": 103734, "start": 1037.34, "end": 1037.98, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50365, 1079, 13, 50397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 226, "seek": 103734, "start": 1038.58, "end": 1046.76, "text": " We are eagerly sharing the products of representation, but leaving the representations themselves concentrated within massive, opaque institutions.", "tokens": [50427, 492, 366, 18259, 356, 5414, 264, 3383, 295, 10290, 11, 457, 5012, 264, 33358, 2969, 21321, 1951, 5994, 11, 42687, 8142, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 227, "seek": 103734, "start": 1047.12, "end": 1054.78, "text": " To understand how this trap functions, the paper draws a vital distinction between a productive abstraction and an opaque abstraction.", "tokens": [50854, 1407, 1223, 577, 341, 11487, 6828, 11, 264, 3035, 20045, 257, 11707, 16844, 1296, 257, 13304, 37765, 293, 364, 42687, 37765, 13, 51237], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 228, "seek": 103734, "start": 1055.1599999999999, "end": 1055.3799999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51256, 1033, 13, 51267], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 229, "seek": 103734, "start": 1055.4599999999998, "end": 1061.3, "text": " We definitely need to define abstraction here because in software and engineering, abstraction isn't a bad word.", "tokens": [51271, 492, 2138, 643, 281, 6964, 37765, 510, 570, 294, 4722, 293, 7043, 11, 37765, 1943, 380, 257, 1578, 1349, 13, 51563], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 230, "seek": 103734, "start": 1061.52, "end": 1062.1999999999998, "text": " It's essential.", "tokens": [51574, 467, 311, 7115, 13, 51608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 231, "seek": 103734, "start": 1062.5, "end": 1063.9199999999998, "text": " It is entirely essential.", "tokens": [51623, 467, 307, 7696, 7115, 13, 51694], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1774892089187458, "compression_ratio": 1.7777777777777777, "no_speech_prob": 2.1173798391699306e-12}, {"id": 232, "seek": 106392, "start": 1063.92, "end": 1071.14, "text": " Like, I don't want to have to understand the binary logic gates of a microchip just to send a text message or order a pizza.", "tokens": [50365, 1743, 11, 286, 500, 380, 528, 281, 362, 281, 1223, 264, 17434, 9952, 19792, 295, 257, 4532, 339, 647, 445, 281, 2845, 257, 2487, 3636, 420, 1668, 257, 8298, 13, 50726], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 233, "seek": 106392, "start": 1071.72, "end": 1073.7, "text": " I want the complexity hidden from me.", "tokens": [50755, 286, 528, 264, 14024, 7633, 490, 385, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 234, "seek": 106392, "start": 1073.9, "end": 1077.94, "text": " Abstraction is arguably the most powerful intellectual tool in human history.", "tokens": [50864, 46853, 26766, 307, 26771, 264, 881, 4005, 12576, 2290, 294, 1952, 2503, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 235, "seek": 106392, "start": 1078.68, "end": 1082.88, "text": " It allows us to compress overwhelming complexity into manageable concepts.", "tokens": [51103, 467, 4045, 505, 281, 14778, 13373, 14024, 666, 38798, 10392, 13, 51313], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 236, "seek": 106392, "start": 1083.0600000000002, "end": 1083.22, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51322, 1779, 13, 51330], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 237, "seek": 106392, "start": 1083.28, "end": 1087.0600000000002, "text": " Like how we use folders on a computer screen instead of looking at raw magnetic data.", "tokens": [51333, 1743, 577, 321, 764, 31082, 322, 257, 3820, 2568, 2602, 295, 1237, 412, 8936, 12688, 1412, 13, 51522], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11877351058156867, "compression_ratio": 1.539622641509434, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080525362145327e-12}, {"id": 238, "seek": 108706, "start": 1087.06, "end": 1087.72, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50365, 7587, 13, 50398], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 239, "seek": 108706, "start": 1088.46, "end": 1093.28, "text": " Programming languages like Python abstract away the nightmare of managing raw computer memory.", "tokens": [50435, 8338, 2810, 8650, 411, 15329, 12649, 1314, 264, 18724, 295, 11642, 8936, 3820, 4675, 13, 50676], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 240, "seek": 108706, "start": 1093.82, "end": 1098.94, "text": " Scientific theories abstract millions of individual observations into a single, elegant formula.", "tokens": [50703, 47437, 13667, 12649, 6803, 295, 2609, 18163, 666, 257, 2167, 11, 21117, 8513, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 241, "seek": 108706, "start": 1099.1, "end": 1100.08, "text": " So abstraction is good.", "tokens": [50967, 407, 37765, 307, 665, 13, 51016], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 242, "seek": 108706, "start": 1100.32, "end": 1105.32, "text": " But the author argues that a healthy, productive abstraction functions like a ladder.", "tokens": [51028, 583, 264, 3793, 38218, 300, 257, 4627, 11, 13304, 37765, 6828, 411, 257, 18325, 13, 51278], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 243, "seek": 108706, "start": 1105.84, "end": 1110.34, "text": " You can climb up it to work quickly at a high level, ignoring the details below.", "tokens": [51304, 509, 393, 10724, 493, 309, 281, 589, 2661, 412, 257, 1090, 1496, 11, 26258, 264, 4365, 2507, 13, 51529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 244, "seek": 108706, "start": 1110.44, "end": 1110.6399999999999, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51534, 1033, 13, 51544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17497882623782104, "compression_ratio": 1.562992125984252, "no_speech_prob": 1.957982387335022e-12}, {"id": 245, "seek": 111064, "start": 1110.64, "end": 1111.4, "text": " I like that image.", "tokens": [50365, 286, 411, 300, 3256, 13, 50403], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 246, "seek": 111064, "start": 1111.5800000000002, "end": 1111.94, "text": " A ladder.", "tokens": [50412, 316, 18325, 13, 50430], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 247, "seek": 111064, "start": 1112.38, "end": 1122.94, "text": " But if you need to say, if you are a curious student or a frustrated engineer trying to fix a bug, you can climb down the ladder to see exactly how the underlying mechanisms work.", "tokens": [50452, 583, 498, 291, 643, 281, 584, 11, 498, 291, 366, 257, 6369, 3107, 420, 257, 15751, 11403, 1382, 281, 3191, 257, 7426, 11, 291, 393, 10724, 760, 264, 18325, 281, 536, 2293, 577, 264, 14217, 15902, 589, 13, 50980], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 248, "seek": 111064, "start": 1123.16, "end": 1128.76, "text": " It hides detail to aid your focus, but it does not destroy your access to that detail.", "tokens": [50991, 467, 35953, 2607, 281, 9418, 428, 1879, 11, 457, 309, 775, 406, 5293, 428, 2105, 281, 300, 2607, 13, 51271], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 249, "seek": 111064, "start": 1129.24, "end": 1131.3400000000001, "text": " But modern digital platforms don't build ladders.", "tokens": [51295, 583, 4363, 4562, 9473, 500, 380, 1322, 6632, 15633, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 250, "seek": 111064, "start": 1131.68, "end": 1132.6200000000001, "text": " They build walls.", "tokens": [51417, 814, 1322, 7920, 13, 51464], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17298138526178175, "compression_ratio": 1.5782608695652174, "no_speech_prob": 1.7014032327108963e-12}, {"id": 251, "seek": 113262, "start": 1132.62, "end": 1135.6799999999998, "text": " They turn abstraction into a sheer wall of opacity.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 1261, 37765, 666, 257, 23061, 2929, 295, 41693, 13, 50518], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 252, "seek": 113262, "start": 1136.4399999999998, "end": 1139.9599999999998, "text": " You encounter this beautifully elegant, frictionless interface on your screen.", "tokens": [50556, 509, 8593, 341, 16525, 21117, 11, 17710, 1832, 9226, 322, 428, 2568, 13, 50732], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 253, "seek": 113262, "start": 1140.4399999999998, "end": 1145.28, "text": " But the internal workings, the logic, the algorithms are completely inaccessible.", "tokens": [50756, 583, 264, 6920, 589, 1109, 11, 264, 9952, 11, 264, 14642, 366, 2584, 33230, 780, 964, 13, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 254, "seek": 113262, "start": 1145.36, "end": 1147.2199999999998, "text": " You cannot climb down to see how it works.", "tokens": [51002, 509, 2644, 10724, 760, 281, 536, 577, 309, 1985, 13, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 255, "seek": 113262, "start": 1147.32, "end": 1147.76, "text": " You cannot.", "tokens": [51100, 509, 2644, 13, 51122], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 256, "seek": 113262, "start": 1148.2199999999998, "end": 1153.26, "text": " And the paper gives a highly specific, fascinating technical example to illustrate this shift.", "tokens": [51145, 400, 264, 3035, 2709, 257, 5405, 2685, 11, 10343, 6191, 1365, 281, 23221, 341, 5513, 13, 51397], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 257, "seek": 113262, "start": 1154.1799999999998, "end": 1155.56, "text": " Content-sensitive hashing.", "tokens": [51443, 30078, 12, 82, 34465, 575, 571, 13, 51512], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 258, "seek": 113262, "start": 1155.6599999999999, "end": 1155.9599999999998, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51517, 1079, 13, 51532], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 259, "seek": 113262, "start": 1156.26, "end": 1157.82, "text": " Let's dive into the mechanics of hashing.", "tokens": [51547, 961, 311, 9192, 666, 264, 12939, 295, 575, 571, 13, 51625], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1509325592606156, "compression_ratio": 1.614814814814815, "no_speech_prob": 1.996901342199431e-12}, {"id": 260, "seek": 115782, "start": 1157.82, "end": 1163.04, "text": " Because when I read this section, it perfectly crystallized what the author means by institutional capture.", "tokens": [50365, 1436, 562, 286, 1401, 341, 3541, 11, 309, 6239, 31924, 1602, 437, 264, 3793, 1355, 538, 18391, 7983, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 261, "seek": 115782, "start": 1163.54, "end": 1167.82, "text": " To understand content-sensitive hashing, we first need to quickly define a hash function.", "tokens": [50651, 1407, 1223, 2701, 12, 82, 34465, 575, 571, 11, 321, 700, 643, 281, 2661, 6964, 257, 22019, 2445, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 262, "seek": 115782, "start": 1168.76, "end": 1170.6399999999999, "text": " Imagine a mathematical meat grinder.", "tokens": [50912, 11739, 257, 18894, 4615, 41424, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 263, "seek": 115782, "start": 1170.72, "end": 1171.1599999999999, "text": " A meat grinder.", "tokens": [51010, 316, 4615, 41424, 13, 51032], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 264, "seek": 115782, "start": 1171.3, "end": 1171.48, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51039, 1033, 13, 51048], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 265, "seek": 115782, "start": 1171.6599999999999, "end": 1173.82, "text": " You can drop any digital file into it.", "tokens": [51057, 509, 393, 3270, 604, 4562, 3991, 666, 309, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 266, "seek": 115782, "start": 1174.02, "end": 1177.1399999999999, "text": " A text document, a photo, a massive movie file.", "tokens": [51175, 316, 2487, 4166, 11, 257, 5052, 11, 257, 5994, 3169, 3991, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 267, "seek": 115782, "start": 1177.62, "end": 1183.1, "text": " And the algorithm grinds it up and spits out a fixed-length string of letters and numbers.", "tokens": [51355, 400, 264, 9284, 16700, 82, 309, 493, 293, 637, 1208, 484, 257, 6806, 12, 45390, 6798, 295, 7825, 293, 3547, 13, 51629], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 268, "seek": 115782, "start": 1183.6599999999999, "end": 1185.62, "text": " A unique digital fingerprint.", "tokens": [51657, 316, 3845, 4562, 30715, 13, 51755], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 269, "seek": 115782, "start": 1185.84, "end": 1186.06, "text": " Okay.", "tokens": [51766, 1033, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 270, "seek": 115782, "start": 1186.3799999999999, "end": 1186.74, "text": " Got it.", "tokens": [51793, 5803, 309, 13, 51811], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16819505842905197, "compression_ratio": 1.6203389830508474, "no_speech_prob": 1.6169103816271457e-12}, {"id": 271, "seek": 118674, "start": 1186.74, "end": 1192.68, "text": " If you change even one pixel in that movie and run it through the grinder again, the fingerprint changes completely.", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 1319, 754, 472, 19261, 294, 300, 3169, 293, 1190, 309, 807, 264, 41424, 797, 11, 264, 30715, 2962, 2584, 13, 50662], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 272, "seek": 118674, "start": 1193.06, "end": 1198.24, "text": " But if you run the exact same file through, you always get the exact same fingerprint.", "tokens": [50681, 583, 498, 291, 1190, 264, 1900, 912, 3991, 807, 11, 291, 1009, 483, 264, 1900, 912, 30715, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 273, "seek": 118674, "start": 1198.54, "end": 1201.54, "text": " And you can't reverse the process to get the movie back from the fingerprint.", "tokens": [50955, 400, 291, 393, 380, 9943, 264, 1399, 281, 483, 264, 3169, 646, 490, 264, 30715, 13, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 274, "seek": 118674, "start": 1201.6200000000001, "end": 1201.86, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51109, 1779, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 275, "seek": 118674, "start": 1202.06, "end": 1205.48, "text": " But it's a perfect way to verify that a file is exactly what it claims to be.", "tokens": [51131, 583, 309, 311, 257, 2176, 636, 281, 16888, 300, 257, 3991, 307, 2293, 437, 309, 9441, 281, 312, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 276, "seek": 118674, "start": 1205.58, "end": 1206.3, "text": " Exactly that.", "tokens": [51307, 7587, 300, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 277, "seek": 118674, "start": 1206.6200000000001, "end": 1209.3, "text": " Now, apply this to massive cloud storage platforms.", "tokens": [51359, 823, 11, 3079, 341, 281, 5994, 4588, 6725, 9473, 13, 51493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 278, "seek": 118674, "start": 1209.58, "end": 1214.78, "text": " Imagine a million different users all uploading the exact same viral video to a cloud drive.", "tokens": [51507, 11739, 257, 2459, 819, 5022, 439, 27301, 264, 1900, 912, 16132, 960, 281, 257, 4588, 3332, 13, 51767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10704693603515625, "compression_ratio": 1.797945205479452, "no_speech_prob": 1.9280920176417693e-12}, {"id": 279, "seek": 121478, "start": 1214.78, "end": 1215.58, "text": " Oh, okay.", "tokens": [50365, 876, 11, 1392, 13, 50405], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14886159716912037, "compression_ratio": 1.36875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077869066822737e-12}, {"id": 280, "seek": 121478, "start": 1215.68, "end": 1222.36, "text": " So in the early days of computing, the server would literally have to save one million separate copies of that file on physical hard drives, right?", "tokens": [50410, 407, 294, 264, 2440, 1708, 295, 15866, 11, 264, 7154, 576, 3736, 362, 281, 3155, 472, 2459, 4994, 14341, 295, 300, 3991, 322, 4001, 1152, 11754, 11, 558, 30, 50744], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14886159716912037, "compression_ratio": 1.36875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077869066822737e-12}, {"id": 281, "seek": 121478, "start": 1222.52, "end": 1226.22, "text": " Consuming massive amounts of space, electricity, and cooling.", "tokens": [50752, 6923, 24919, 5994, 11663, 295, 1901, 11, 10356, 11, 293, 14785, 13, 50937], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14886159716912037, "compression_ratio": 1.36875, "no_speech_prob": 1.7077869066822737e-12}, {"id": 282, "seek": 122622, "start": 1226.22, "end": 1228.24, "text": " Which is incredibly inefficient.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 307, 6252, 43495, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14834330115519778, "compression_ratio": 1.5198019801980198, "no_speech_prob": 1.542540617807675e-12}, {"id": 283, "seek": 122622, "start": 1228.24, "end": 1231.8, "text": " It's just petabytes of redundant data sitting in a server farm.", "tokens": [50466, 467, 311, 445, 3817, 24538, 295, 40997, 1412, 3798, 294, 257, 7154, 5421, 13, 50644], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14834330115519778, "compression_ratio": 1.5198019801980198, "no_speech_prob": 1.542540617807675e-12}, {"id": 284, "seek": 122622, "start": 1232.16, "end": 1233.0, "text": " Terribly inefficient.", "tokens": [50662, 6564, 18409, 43495, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14834330115519778, "compression_ratio": 1.5198019801980198, "no_speech_prob": 1.542540617807675e-12}, {"id": 285, "seek": 122622, "start": 1233.64, "end": 1237.16, "text": " So engineers develop systems using content-sensitive hashing.", "tokens": [50736, 407, 11955, 1499, 3652, 1228, 2701, 12, 82, 34465, 575, 571, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14834330115519778, "compression_ratio": 1.5198019801980198, "no_speech_prob": 1.542540617807675e-12}, {"id": 286, "seek": 122622, "start": 1237.52, "end": 1244.92, "text": " When you try to upload that viral video, the platform's software runs it through the mathematical meat grinder on your device.", "tokens": [50930, 1133, 291, 853, 281, 6580, 300, 16132, 960, 11, 264, 3663, 311, 4722, 6676, 309, 807, 264, 18894, 4615, 41424, 322, 428, 4302, 13, 51300], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14834330115519778, "compression_ratio": 1.5198019801980198, "no_speech_prob": 1.542540617807675e-12}, {"id": 287, "seek": 124492, "start": 1244.92, "end": 1246.1200000000001, "text": " Before it even uploads.", "tokens": [50365, 4546, 309, 754, 48611, 13, 50425], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 288, "seek": 124492, "start": 1246.24, "end": 1246.4, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50431, 1079, 13, 50439], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 289, "seek": 124492, "start": 1246.54, "end": 1248.2, "text": " It generates the hash, the fingerprint.", "tokens": [50446, 467, 23815, 264, 22019, 11, 264, 30715, 13, 50529], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 290, "seek": 124492, "start": 1248.5, "end": 1254.22, "text": " It sends just the fingerprint to the server and asks, do you already have a file with this exact fingerprint?", "tokens": [50544, 467, 14790, 445, 264, 30715, 281, 264, 7154, 293, 8962, 11, 360, 291, 1217, 362, 257, 3991, 365, 341, 1900, 30715, 30, 50830], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 291, "seek": 124492, "start": 1254.42, "end": 1254.66, "text": " Ah.", "tokens": [50840, 2438, 13, 50852], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 292, "seek": 124492, "start": 1255.04, "end": 1260.3200000000002, "text": " And the server checks its database, finds that someone else already uploaded it, and says, yes, I have it.", "tokens": [50871, 400, 264, 7154, 13834, 1080, 8149, 11, 10704, 300, 1580, 1646, 1217, 17135, 309, 11, 293, 1619, 11, 2086, 11, 286, 362, 309, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 293, "seek": 124492, "start": 1260.42, "end": 1260.9, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51140, 7587, 13, 51164], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 294, "seek": 124492, "start": 1261.22, "end": 1270.24, "text": " So instead of uploading the heavy video file, the system just saves a tiny pointer, a little link, connecting your account to the original file already on the server.", "tokens": [51180, 407, 2602, 295, 27301, 264, 4676, 960, 3991, 11, 264, 1185, 445, 19155, 257, 5870, 23918, 11, 257, 707, 2113, 11, 11015, 428, 2696, 281, 264, 3380, 3991, 1217, 322, 264, 7154, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1386127965203647, "compression_ratio": 1.7481203007518797, "no_speech_prob": 1.5370884903428972e-12}, {"id": 295, "seek": 127024, "start": 1270.24, "end": 1278.48, "text": " That is brilliant. Millions of users think they have their own copy of the video in their drives, but in reality, there is only one actual file stored.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 307, 10248, 13, 7190, 626, 295, 5022, 519, 436, 362, 641, 1065, 5055, 295, 264, 960, 294, 641, 11754, 11, 457, 294, 4103, 11, 456, 307, 787, 472, 3539, 3991, 12187, 13, 50777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12059612457568829, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485472705164318e-12}, {"id": 296, "seek": 127024, "start": 1278.6, "end": 1290.1, "text": " Redundancy is eliminated. Storage costs absolutely plummet. Technically, it is a triumph of engineering. It is an incredibly elegant solution to a massive infrastructural problem.", "tokens": [50783, 4477, 997, 6717, 307, 20308, 13, 36308, 5497, 3122, 25854, 5537, 13, 42494, 11, 309, 307, 257, 29156, 295, 7043, 13, 467, 307, 364, 6252, 21117, 3827, 281, 257, 5994, 6534, 1757, 1807, 1154, 13, 51358], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12059612457568829, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485472705164318e-12}, {"id": 297, "seek": 127024, "start": 1290.3, "end": 1293.72, "text": " What? Here's where it gets really interesting and a little dark.", "tokens": [51368, 708, 30, 1692, 311, 689, 309, 2170, 534, 1880, 293, 257, 707, 2877, 13, 51539], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12059612457568829, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485472705164318e-12}, {"id": 298, "seek": 127024, "start": 1293.98, "end": 1297.74, "text": " Yes. Here is the critical catch that the paper highlights.", "tokens": [51552, 1079, 13, 1692, 307, 264, 4924, 3745, 300, 264, 3035, 14254, 13, 51740], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12059612457568829, "compression_ratio": 1.5689655172413792, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485472705164318e-12}, {"id": 299, "seek": 129774, "start": 1297.74, "end": 1307.5, "text": " Historically, an architectural breakthrough of that magnitude-like calculus or the scientific method or the printing press would become a public standard.", "tokens": [50365, 25108, 984, 11, 364, 26621, 22397, 295, 300, 15668, 12, 4092, 33400, 420, 264, 8134, 3170, 420, 264, 14699, 1886, 576, 1813, 257, 1908, 3832, 13, 50853], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11951889862885347, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080519941134464e-12}, {"id": 300, "seek": 129774, "start": 1307.8, "end": 1310.24, "text": " It would be taught in introductory computer science classes.", "tokens": [50868, 467, 576, 312, 5928, 294, 39048, 3820, 3497, 5359, 13, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11951889862885347, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080519941134464e-12}, {"id": 301, "seek": 129774, "start": 1310.74, "end": 1315.82, "text": " It would be an open protocol that any small business or individual could build into their own local networks.", "tokens": [51015, 467, 576, 312, 364, 1269, 10336, 300, 604, 1359, 1606, 420, 2609, 727, 1322, 666, 641, 1065, 2654, 9590, 13, 51269], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11951889862885347, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080519941134464e-12}, {"id": 302, "seek": 129774, "start": 1316.1, "end": 1317.78, "text": " But that's not what happens today.", "tokens": [51283, 583, 300, 311, 406, 437, 2314, 965, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11951889862885347, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7080519941134464e-12}, {"id": 303, "seek": 131778, "start": 1317.78, "end": 1328.3999999999999, "text": " Instead of becoming public engineering knowledge, this brilliant hashing architecture becomes a hidden proprietary feature locked inside a massive corporate cloud service.", "tokens": [50365, 7156, 295, 5617, 1908, 7043, 3601, 11, 341, 10248, 575, 571, 9482, 3643, 257, 7633, 38992, 4111, 9376, 1854, 257, 5994, 10896, 4588, 2643, 13, 50896], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987787139549684, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.068011126926672e-12}, {"id": 304, "seek": 131778, "start": 1328.52, "end": 1336.68, "text": " Right. The users get the result. They get cheaper storage tiers, faster upload speeds, a seamless syncing experience across their devices.", "tokens": [50902, 1779, 13, 440, 5022, 483, 264, 1874, 13, 814, 483, 12284, 6725, 40563, 11, 4663, 6580, 16411, 11, 257, 28677, 5451, 2175, 1752, 2108, 641, 5759, 13, 51310], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987787139549684, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.068011126926672e-12}, {"id": 305, "seek": 131778, "start": 1336.8799999999999, "end": 1338.68, "text": " But they do not get the representation.", "tokens": [51320, 583, 436, 360, 406, 483, 264, 10290, 13, 51410], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987787139549684, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.068011126926672e-12}, {"id": 306, "seek": 131778, "start": 1339.1, "end": 1343.48, "text": " They don't get the algorithm, the server architecture, or the understanding of how it operates.", "tokens": [51431, 814, 500, 380, 483, 264, 9284, 11, 264, 7154, 9482, 11, 420, 264, 3701, 295, 577, 309, 22577, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.0987787139549684, "compression_ratio": 1.6397058823529411, "no_speech_prob": 2.068011126926672e-12}, {"id": 307, "seek": 134348, "start": 1343.48, "end": 1346.74, "text": " The efficiency is entirely walled off behind an API.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10493, 307, 7696, 2929, 292, 766, 2261, 364, 9362, 13, 50528], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 308, "seek": 134348, "start": 1347.1, "end": 1351.14, "text": " It is the difference between a glass-bottom boat and a sealed black box.", "tokens": [50546, 467, 307, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 4276, 12, 65, 1521, 298, 6582, 293, 257, 21514, 2211, 2424, 13, 50748], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 309, "seek": 134348, "start": 1351.7, "end": 1355.24, "text": " If you're riding in a glass-bottom boat, you can sit back and enjoy the ride.", "tokens": [50776, 759, 291, 434, 9546, 294, 257, 4276, 12, 65, 1521, 298, 6582, 11, 291, 393, 1394, 646, 293, 2103, 264, 5077, 13, 50953], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 310, "seek": 134348, "start": 1355.44, "end": 1360.66, "text": " But you can also look down and study the engine, watch the propeller turn, and see the mechanics of propulsion.", "tokens": [50963, 583, 291, 393, 611, 574, 760, 293, 2979, 264, 2848, 11, 1159, 264, 25577, 4658, 1261, 11, 293, 536, 264, 12939, 295, 49375, 13, 51224], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 311, "seek": 134348, "start": 1361.0, "end": 1362.1200000000001, "text": " You have the option to learn.", "tokens": [51241, 509, 362, 264, 3614, 281, 1466, 13, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 312, "seek": 134348, "start": 1362.44, "end": 1362.82, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51313, 7587, 13, 51332], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 313, "seek": 134348, "start": 1363.22, "end": 1368.82, "text": " If you have the time and curiosity, you can learn the principles of marine engineering just by observing.", "tokens": [51352, 759, 291, 362, 264, 565, 293, 18769, 11, 291, 393, 1466, 264, 9156, 295, 20246, 7043, 445, 538, 22107, 13, 51632], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11301256815592448, "compression_ratio": 1.7100371747211895, "no_speech_prob": 1.513255666607538e-12}, {"id": 314, "seek": 136882, "start": 1368.82, "end": 1374.8, "text": " But modern technology is increasingly a sealed, opaque black box.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 4363, 2899, 307, 12980, 257, 21514, 11, 42687, 2211, 2424, 13, 50664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 315, "seek": 136882, "start": 1375.12, "end": 1377.8, "text": " It might be a thousand times faster than the glass-bottom boat.", "tokens": [50680, 467, 1062, 312, 257, 4714, 1413, 4663, 813, 264, 4276, 12, 65, 1521, 298, 6582, 13, 50814], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 316, "seek": 136882, "start": 1377.98, "end": 1381.08, "text": " It might have leather seats and perfect climate control.", "tokens": [50823, 467, 1062, 362, 12821, 11069, 293, 2176, 5659, 1969, 13, 50978], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 317, "seek": 136882, "start": 1381.34, "end": 1386.12, "text": " But you are entirely dependent on the company that holds the key to the box.", "tokens": [50991, 583, 291, 366, 7696, 12334, 322, 264, 2237, 300, 9190, 264, 2141, 281, 264, 2424, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 318, "seek": 136882, "start": 1386.34, "end": 1391.34, "text": " You are enthusiastically consuming the outcome without acquiring a single drop of the method.", "tokens": [51241, 509, 366, 18076, 22808, 19867, 264, 9700, 1553, 37374, 257, 2167, 3270, 295, 264, 3170, 13, 51491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 319, "seek": 136882, "start": 1391.7, "end": 1392.26, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [51509, 48746, 736, 13, 51537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1579857530265019, "compression_ratio": 1.5793991416309012, "no_speech_prob": 1.579840533567911e-12}, {"id": 320, "seek": 139226, "start": 1392.26, "end": 1398.7, "text": " Now, I think we have to be very careful here about the tone we use when discussing the companies building these black boxes.", "tokens": [50365, 823, 11, 286, 519, 321, 362, 281, 312, 588, 5026, 510, 466, 264, 8027, 321, 764, 562, 10850, 264, 3431, 2390, 613, 2211, 9002, 13, 50687], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 321, "seek": 139226, "start": 1398.92, "end": 1399.42, "text": " Oh, for sure.", "tokens": [50698, 876, 11, 337, 988, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 322, "seek": 139226, "start": 1400.04, "end": 1402.04, "text": " Because it's easy to sound like a conspiracy theorist.", "tokens": [50754, 1436, 309, 311, 1858, 281, 1626, 411, 257, 20439, 27423, 468, 13, 50854], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 323, "seek": 139226, "start": 1402.14, "end": 1406.18, "text": " The paper goes out of its way to clarify that this isn't some malicious corporate plot.", "tokens": [50859, 440, 3035, 1709, 484, 295, 1080, 636, 281, 17594, 300, 341, 1943, 380, 512, 33496, 10896, 7542, 13, 51061], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 324, "seek": 139226, "start": 1406.66, "end": 1413.64, "text": " There isn't a secret cabal of tech CEOs sitting in a boardroom, twirling their mustaches, plotting to keep humanity in the dark.", "tokens": [51085, 821, 1943, 380, 257, 4054, 5487, 304, 295, 7553, 40736, 3798, 294, 257, 3150, 2861, 11, 683, 1648, 278, 641, 1633, 13272, 11, 41178, 281, 1066, 10243, 294, 264, 2877, 13, 51434], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 325, "seek": 139226, "start": 1413.78, "end": 1414.48, "text": " It's not a conspiracy.", "tokens": [51441, 467, 311, 406, 257, 20439, 13, 51476], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 326, "seek": 139226, "start": 1415.02, "end": 1417.02, "text": " It is entirely rational economics.", "tokens": [51503, 467, 307, 7696, 15090, 14564, 13, 51603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 327, "seek": 139226, "start": 1417.46, "end": 1417.8, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51625, 1079, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1270569669521921, "compression_ratio": 1.6033898305084746, "no_speech_prob": 1.7216028949662565e-12}, {"id": 328, "seek": 141780, "start": 1417.8, "end": 1424.6, "text": " The author points out that modern economic models heavily reward repeated access over permanent understanding.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 2793, 484, 300, 4363, 4836, 5245, 10950, 7782, 10477, 2105, 670, 10996, 3701, 13, 50705], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1007020886739095, "compression_ratio": 1.5687203791469195, "no_speech_prob": 1.335451606070126e-12}, {"id": 329, "seek": 141780, "start": 1425.48, "end": 1433.36, "text": " If a company invents a better way to filter water, and they teach you the mechanics of that filtration, you only need to interact with them once.", "tokens": [50749, 759, 257, 2237, 1048, 791, 257, 1101, 636, 281, 6608, 1281, 11, 293, 436, 2924, 291, 264, 12939, 295, 300, 43623, 11, 291, 787, 643, 281, 4648, 365, 552, 1564, 13, 51143], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1007020886739095, "compression_ratio": 1.5687203791469195, "no_speech_prob": 1.335451606070126e-12}, {"id": 330, "seek": 141780, "start": 1433.54, "end": 1433.76, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51152, 1779, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1007020886739095, "compression_ratio": 1.5687203791469195, "no_speech_prob": 1.335451606070126e-12}, {"id": 331, "seek": 141780, "start": 1434.08, "end": 1436.96, "text": " You take the knowledge, you go home, and you build your own filter.", "tokens": [51179, 509, 747, 264, 3601, 11, 291, 352, 1280, 11, 293, 291, 1322, 428, 1065, 6608, 13, 51323], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1007020886739095, "compression_ratio": 1.5687203791469195, "no_speech_prob": 1.335451606070126e-12}, {"id": 332, "seek": 143696, "start": 1436.96, "end": 1448.2, "text": " But if they invent a better filtration method, hide the mechanism behind a tamper-proof casing, and charge you a monthly subscription to access the clean water, they have secured a durable competitive advantage.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 498, 436, 7962, 257, 1101, 43623, 3170, 11, 6479, 264, 7513, 2261, 257, 7677, 610, 12, 15690, 45109, 11, 293, 4602, 291, 257, 12878, 17231, 281, 2105, 264, 2541, 1281, 11, 436, 362, 22905, 257, 22308, 10043, 5002, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 333, "seek": 143696, "start": 1448.52, "end": 1455.06, "text": " The knowledge continues to generate recurring revenue for the institution, precisely because the knowledge remains concentrated.", "tokens": [50943, 440, 3601, 6515, 281, 8460, 32279, 9324, 337, 264, 7818, 11, 13402, 570, 264, 3601, 7023, 21321, 13, 51270], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 334, "seek": 143696, "start": 1455.64, "end": 1457.9, "text": " So the scarcity of the modern world has shifted.", "tokens": [51299, 407, 264, 44181, 295, 264, 4363, 1002, 575, 18892, 13, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 335, "seek": 143696, "start": 1458.08, "end": 1460.08, "text": " It isn't about technical difficulty anymore.", "tokens": [51421, 467, 1943, 380, 466, 6191, 10360, 3602, 13, 51521], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 336, "seek": 143696, "start": 1460.26, "end": 1461.48, "text": " We have the computing power.", "tokens": [51530, 492, 362, 264, 15866, 1347, 13, 51591], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 337, "seek": 143696, "start": 1461.6000000000001, "end": 1462.96, "text": " We have the manufacturing base.", "tokens": [51597, 492, 362, 264, 11096, 3096, 13, 51665], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 338, "seek": 143696, "start": 1463.04, "end": 1465.66, "text": " We have the algorithms to solve almost anything.", "tokens": [51669, 492, 362, 264, 14642, 281, 5039, 1920, 1340, 13, 51800], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.08805133178170803, "compression_ratio": 1.7, "no_speech_prob": 1.3406762679191164e-12}, {"id": 339, "seek": 146566, "start": 1465.66, "end": 1468.4, "text": " The scarcity we're dealing with now is artificial.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 44181, 321, 434, 6260, 365, 586, 307, 11677, 13, 50502], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11215355470008456, "compression_ratio": 1.7014388489208634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130251652256677e-12}, {"id": 340, "seek": 146566, "start": 1468.92, "end": 1470.8000000000002, "text": " It's the artificial scarcity of competence.", "tokens": [50528, 467, 311, 264, 11677, 44181, 295, 39965, 13, 50622], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11215355470008456, "compression_ratio": 1.7014388489208634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130251652256677e-12}, {"id": 341, "seek": 146566, "start": 1471.74, "end": 1478.38, "text": " The company makes sure you can never build this spaceship yourself, so your only option is to indefinitely rent a seat on theirs.", "tokens": [50669, 440, 2237, 1669, 988, 291, 393, 1128, 1322, 341, 39185, 1803, 11, 370, 428, 787, 3614, 307, 281, 24162, 10925, 6214, 257, 6121, 322, 22760, 13, 51001], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11215355470008456, "compression_ratio": 1.7014388489208634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130251652256677e-12}, {"id": 342, "seek": 146566, "start": 1478.78, "end": 1490.2, "text": " And this shift from public leaky knowledge to hidden rentable infrastructure fundamentally changes the psychological and structural relationship we have with our tools.", "tokens": [51021, 400, 341, 5513, 490, 1908, 476, 15681, 3601, 281, 7633, 6214, 712, 6896, 17879, 2962, 264, 14346, 293, 15067, 2480, 321, 362, 365, 527, 3873, 13, 51592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11215355470008456, "compression_ratio": 1.7014388489208634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130251652256677e-12}, {"id": 343, "seek": 146566, "start": 1490.3200000000002, "end": 1494.4, "text": " It transitions our technology from acting as a teacher to acting as a platform.", "tokens": [51598, 467, 23767, 527, 2899, 490, 6577, 382, 257, 5027, 281, 6577, 382, 257, 3663, 13, 51802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11215355470008456, "compression_ratio": 1.7014388489208634, "no_speech_prob": 1.5130251652256677e-12}, {"id": 344, "seek": 149440, "start": 1494.4, "end": 1501.52, "text": " Which brings us to an incredibly profound observation the author makes about the unique nature of education itself.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 364, 6252, 14382, 14816, 264, 3793, 1669, 466, 264, 3845, 3687, 295, 3309, 2564, 13, 50721], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11342803878013534, "compression_ratio": 1.660649819494585, "no_speech_prob": 1.755562058572413e-12}, {"id": 345, "seek": 149440, "start": 1501.7800000000002, "end": 1505.9, "text": " Yeah, the contrast the paper draws between a teacher and a platform really struck me.", "tokens": [50734, 865, 11, 264, 8712, 264, 3035, 20045, 1296, 257, 5027, 293, 257, 3663, 534, 13159, 385, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11342803878013534, "compression_ratio": 1.660649819494585, "no_speech_prob": 1.755562058572413e-12}, {"id": 346, "seek": 149440, "start": 1506.5400000000002, "end": 1514.24, "text": " It points out that education is a strange, almost paradoxical institution because its ultimate goal is self-obsolescence.", "tokens": [50972, 467, 2793, 484, 300, 3309, 307, 257, 5861, 11, 1920, 26221, 804, 7818, 570, 1080, 9705, 3387, 307, 2698, 12, 16537, 7456, 25434, 13, 51357], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11342803878013534, "compression_ratio": 1.660649819494585, "no_speech_prob": 1.755562058572413e-12}, {"id": 347, "seek": 149440, "start": 1514.6200000000001, "end": 1517.48, "text": " Think about the pure mechanics of teaching for a moment.", "tokens": [51376, 6557, 466, 264, 6075, 12939, 295, 4571, 337, 257, 1623, 13, 51519], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11342803878013534, "compression_ratio": 1.660649819494585, "no_speech_prob": 1.755562058572413e-12}, {"id": 348, "seek": 149440, "start": 1517.94, "end": 1522.02, "text": " A true teacher succeeds only when the student no longer needs them in the room.", "tokens": [51542, 316, 2074, 5027, 49263, 787, 562, 264, 3107, 572, 2854, 2203, 552, 294, 264, 1808, 13, 51746], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11342803878013534, "compression_ratio": 1.660649819494585, "no_speech_prob": 1.755562058572413e-12}, {"id": 349, "seek": 152202, "start": 1522.02, "end": 1522.34, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50365, 1779, 13, 50381], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1424021493820917, "compression_ratio": 1.6181102362204725, "no_speech_prob": 1.942746311045518e-12}, {"id": 350, "seek": 152202, "start": 1522.34, "end": 1532.3799999999999, "text": " The entire objective of the interaction is to replace the student's ignorance with a durable understanding so that the student can walk away and solve the problem entirely independently tomorrow.", "tokens": [50381, 440, 2302, 10024, 295, 264, 9285, 307, 281, 7406, 264, 3107, 311, 25390, 365, 257, 22308, 3701, 370, 300, 264, 3107, 393, 1792, 1314, 293, 5039, 264, 1154, 7696, 21761, 4153, 13, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1424021493820917, "compression_ratio": 1.6181102362204725, "no_speech_prob": 1.942746311045518e-12}, {"id": 351, "seek": 152202, "start": 1532.86, "end": 1535.98, "text": " As the paper beautifully puts it, competence is not rented.", "tokens": [50907, 1018, 264, 3035, 16525, 8137, 309, 11, 39965, 307, 406, 32381, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1424021493820917, "compression_ratio": 1.6181102362204725, "no_speech_prob": 1.942746311045518e-12}, {"id": 352, "seek": 152202, "start": 1536.3799999999999, "end": 1537.1399999999999, "text": " It is transferred.", "tokens": [51083, 467, 307, 15809, 13, 51121], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1424021493820917, "compression_ratio": 1.6181102362204725, "no_speech_prob": 1.942746311045518e-12}, {"id": 353, "seek": 152202, "start": 1538.08, "end": 1544.44, "text": " The teacher is actively trying to copy the representation from their mind into yours, making themselves redundant in the process.", "tokens": [51168, 440, 5027, 307, 13022, 1382, 281, 5055, 264, 10290, 490, 641, 1575, 666, 6342, 11, 1455, 2969, 40997, 294, 264, 1399, 13, 51486], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1424021493820917, "compression_ratio": 1.6181102362204725, "no_speech_prob": 1.942746311045518e-12}, {"id": 354, "seek": 154444, "start": 1544.44, "end": 1547.22, "text": " But a platform does the exact opposite.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 3663, 775, 264, 1900, 6182, 13, 50504], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 355, "seek": 154444, "start": 1547.66, "end": 1555.14, "text": " A platform's fundamental design goal is to minimize friction, which sounds fantastic on a marketing brochure.", "tokens": [50526, 316, 3663, 311, 8088, 1715, 3387, 307, 281, 17522, 17710, 11, 597, 3263, 5456, 322, 257, 6370, 48147, 540, 13, 50900], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 356, "seek": 154444, "start": 1555.26, "end": 1556.68, "text": " Oh, everyone loves less friction.", "tokens": [50906, 876, 11, 1518, 6752, 1570, 17710, 13, 50977], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 357, "seek": 154444, "start": 1556.8600000000001, "end": 1558.76, "text": " It automates the complex configuration.", "tokens": [50986, 467, 3553, 1024, 264, 3997, 11694, 13, 51081], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 358, "seek": 154444, "start": 1559.22, "end": 1561.04, "text": " It optimizes the background workflow.", "tokens": [51104, 467, 5028, 5660, 264, 3678, 20993, 13, 51195], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 359, "seek": 154444, "start": 1561.28, "end": 1563.94, "text": " It tries to guess what you want to do and just does it for you.", "tokens": [51207, 467, 9898, 281, 2041, 437, 291, 528, 281, 360, 293, 445, 775, 309, 337, 291, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14229810690578026, "compression_ratio": 1.5330188679245282, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359816263471053e-12}, {"id": 360, "seek": 156394, "start": 1563.94, "end": 1569.46, "text": " But in removing all that friction, it centralizes the representation within itself.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 12720, 439, 300, 17710, 11, 309, 5777, 5660, 264, 10290, 1951, 2564, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 361, "seek": 156394, "start": 1569.72, "end": 1574.68, "text": " It shifts the burden of understanding completely off of your shoulders and onto the infrastructure.", "tokens": [50654, 467, 19201, 264, 12578, 295, 3701, 2584, 766, 295, 428, 10245, 293, 3911, 264, 6896, 13, 50902], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 362, "seek": 156394, "start": 1574.94, "end": 1580.44, "text": " And we must acknowledge that from an immediate productivity standpoint, platforms are phenomenal.", "tokens": [50915, 400, 321, 1633, 10692, 300, 490, 364, 11629, 15604, 15827, 11, 9473, 366, 17778, 13, 51190], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 363, "seek": 156394, "start": 1581.06, "end": 1591.0800000000002, "text": " They have made incredibly sophisticated computation accessible to billions of people who don't know how to code, who don't understand networking protocols or database management.", "tokens": [51221, 814, 362, 1027, 6252, 16950, 24903, 9515, 281, 17375, 295, 561, 567, 500, 380, 458, 577, 281, 3089, 11, 567, 500, 380, 1223, 17985, 20618, 420, 8149, 4592, 13, 51722], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 364, "seek": 156394, "start": 1591.22, "end": 1591.4, "text": " True.", "tokens": [51729, 13587, 13, 51738], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 365, "seek": 156394, "start": 1591.48, "end": 1592.3600000000001, "text": " They are incredibly useful.", "tokens": [51742, 814, 366, 6252, 4420, 13, 51786], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12564035256703696, "compression_ratio": 1.6632996632996633, "no_speech_prob": 1.636217637074333e-12}, {"id": 366, "seek": 159236, "start": 1592.36, "end": 1597.62, "text": " But a platform removes difficulty by making you permanently structurally dependent on it.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 257, 3663, 30445, 10360, 538, 1455, 291, 24042, 6594, 6512, 12334, 322, 309, 13, 50628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 367, "seek": 159236, "start": 1597.9399999999998, "end": 1600.4399999999998, "text": " The solution to your problem remains external.", "tokens": [50644, 440, 3827, 281, 428, 1154, 7023, 8320, 13, 50769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 368, "seek": 159236, "start": 1600.9199999999998, "end": 1605.52, "text": " After using the platform for five years, you haven't internalized any new foundational capability.", "tokens": [50793, 2381, 1228, 264, 3663, 337, 1732, 924, 11, 291, 2378, 380, 6920, 1602, 604, 777, 32195, 13759, 13, 51023], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 369, "seek": 159236, "start": 1605.9799999999998, "end": 1612.86, "text": " The paper highlights a few older software traditions to show the stark contrast here, calling them austere software.", "tokens": [51046, 440, 3035, 14254, 257, 1326, 4906, 4722, 15643, 281, 855, 264, 17417, 8712, 510, 11, 5141, 552, 34916, 323, 4722, 13, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 370, "seek": 159236, "start": 1613.5, "end": 1617.54, "text": " It mentions things like Unix, Latex, Vim, and forth.", "tokens": [51422, 467, 23844, 721, 411, 1156, 970, 11, 31220, 87, 11, 691, 332, 11, 293, 5220, 13, 51624], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 371, "seek": 159236, "start": 1617.6599999999999, "end": 1620.0, "text": " Right, the classic austere environments.", "tokens": [51630, 1779, 11, 264, 7230, 34916, 323, 12388, 13, 51747], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1107314395904541, "compression_ratio": 1.5928571428571427, "no_speech_prob": 1.6427674108185353e-12}, {"id": 372, "seek": 162000, "start": 1620.0, "end": 1624.76, "text": " For listeners who might not be deep into computer science, what exactly makes these systems austere?", "tokens": [50365, 1171, 23274, 567, 1062, 406, 312, 2452, 666, 3820, 3497, 11, 437, 2293, 1669, 613, 3652, 34916, 323, 30, 50603], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914073711488305, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.939899192144768e-12}, {"id": 373, "seek": 162000, "start": 1625.08, "end": 1635.4, "text": " Well, these are systems that are notoriously criticized in the modern era for possessing steep learning curves or for lacking intuitive, frictionless graphical interfaces.", "tokens": [50619, 1042, 11, 613, 366, 3652, 300, 366, 46772, 8994, 28011, 294, 264, 4363, 4249, 337, 17490, 278, 16841, 2539, 19490, 420, 337, 20889, 21769, 11, 17710, 1832, 35942, 28416, 13, 51135], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914073711488305, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.939899192144768e-12}, {"id": 374, "seek": 162000, "start": 1635.54, "end": 1636.38, "text": " A no drag and drop.", "tokens": [51142, 316, 572, 5286, 293, 3270, 13, 51184], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914073711488305, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.939899192144768e-12}, {"id": 375, "seek": 162000, "start": 1636.44, "end": 1640.14, "text": " Take Unix, for example, which is the foundation of many modern operating systems.", "tokens": [51187, 3664, 1156, 970, 11, 337, 1365, 11, 597, 307, 264, 7030, 295, 867, 4363, 7447, 3652, 13, 51372], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09914073711488305, "compression_ratio": 1.5583333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 2.939899192144768e-12}, {"id": 376, "seek": 164014, "start": 1640.14, "end": 1645.18, "text": " When you interact with a traditional Unix environment, you aren't clicking colorful icons.", "tokens": [50365, 1133, 291, 4648, 365, 257, 5164, 1156, 970, 2823, 11, 291, 3212, 380, 9697, 18506, 23308, 13, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1601826144802955, "compression_ratio": 1.2358490566037736, "no_speech_prob": 2.4745847732043913e-12}, {"id": 377, "seek": 164014, "start": 1645.4, "end": 1647.44, "text": " You are typing commands into a terminal.", "tokens": [50628, 509, 366, 18444, 16901, 666, 257, 14709, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1601826144802955, "compression_ratio": 1.2358490566037736, "no_speech_prob": 2.4745847732043913e-12}, {"id": 378, "seek": 164744, "start": 1647.44, "end": 1649.7, "text": " You are staring at a black screen with white text.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 366, 18043, 412, 257, 2211, 2568, 365, 2418, 2487, 13, 50478], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 379, "seek": 164744, "start": 1649.7, "end": 1653.9, "text": " You are continually exposed to the raw mechanics of the file system.", "tokens": [50478, 509, 366, 22277, 9495, 281, 264, 8936, 12939, 295, 264, 3991, 1185, 13, 50688], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 380, "seek": 164744, "start": 1654.3, "end": 1659.1000000000001, "text": " Unix is built on a philosophy of small, specialized programs that do one thing well.", "tokens": [50708, 1156, 970, 307, 3094, 322, 257, 10675, 295, 1359, 11, 19813, 4268, 300, 360, 472, 551, 731, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 381, "seek": 164744, "start": 1659.44, "end": 1660.9, "text": " And you have to connect them yourself, right?", "tokens": [50965, 400, 291, 362, 281, 1745, 552, 1803, 11, 558, 30, 51038], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 382, "seek": 164744, "start": 1661.1000000000001, "end": 1661.38, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51048, 1079, 13, 51062], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 383, "seek": 164744, "start": 1661.78, "end": 1671.3200000000002, "text": " You use things called pipes, literally the vertical bar character on your keyboard, to chain these small programs together, feeding the output of one tool directly into the input of another.", "tokens": [51082, 509, 764, 721, 1219, 21882, 11, 3736, 264, 9429, 2159, 2517, 322, 428, 10186, 11, 281, 5021, 613, 1359, 4268, 1214, 11, 12919, 264, 5598, 295, 472, 2290, 3838, 666, 264, 4846, 295, 1071, 13, 51559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.12447704389257339, "compression_ratio": 1.6457564575645756, "no_speech_prob": 2.1083751064465694e-12}, {"id": 384, "seek": 167132, "start": 1671.32, "end": 1678.76, "text": " It's like being handed a box of individual gears and being told to build your own clock rather than just buying a digital watch.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 311, 411, 885, 16013, 257, 2424, 295, 2609, 20915, 293, 885, 1907, 281, 1322, 428, 1065, 7830, 2831, 813, 445, 6382, 257, 4562, 1159, 13, 50737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 385, "seek": 167132, "start": 1678.9399999999998, "end": 1679.36, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50746, 7587, 13, 50767], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 386, "seek": 167132, "start": 1679.9399999999998, "end": 1682.6399999999999, "text": " Or take latex, which the paper also mentions.", "tokens": [50796, 1610, 747, 3469, 87, 11, 597, 264, 3035, 611, 23844, 13, 50931], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 387, "seek": 167132, "start": 1682.74, "end": 1683.1799999999998, "text": " Okay, yeah.", "tokens": [50936, 1033, 11, 1338, 13, 50958], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 388, "seek": 167132, "start": 1683.48, "end": 1688.62, "text": " Because if I want to write a document today, I open Microsoft Word or Google Docs.", "tokens": [50973, 1436, 498, 286, 528, 281, 2464, 257, 4166, 965, 11, 286, 1269, 8116, 8725, 420, 3329, 16024, 82, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 389, "seek": 167132, "start": 1688.9399999999998, "end": 1693.46, "text": " I type a word, I click the bold button, and the word instantly turns bold on the screen.", "tokens": [51246, 286, 2010, 257, 1349, 11, 286, 2052, 264, 11928, 2960, 11, 293, 264, 1349, 13518, 4523, 11928, 322, 264, 2568, 13, 51472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 390, "seek": 167132, "start": 1693.98, "end": 1697.02, "text": " It's called W-Y-S-I-W-Y-G.", "tokens": [51498, 467, 311, 1219, 343, 12, 56, 12, 50, 12, 40, 12, 54, 12, 56, 12, 38, 13, 51650], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 391, "seek": 167132, "start": 1697.48, "end": 1699.3999999999999, "text": " What you see is what you get.", "tokens": [51673, 708, 291, 536, 307, 437, 291, 483, 13, 51769], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1369178711421906, "compression_ratio": 1.5197132616487454, "no_speech_prob": 1.748562232506412e-12}, {"id": 392, "seek": 169940, "start": 1699.4, "end": 1701.88, "text": " But latex operates entirely differently.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 3469, 87, 22577, 7696, 7614, 13, 50489], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 393, "seek": 169940, "start": 1702.2800000000002, "end": 1708.0, "text": " It is a typesetting system where you write your document in plain text using markup tags to define the structure.", "tokens": [50509, 467, 307, 257, 3467, 302, 783, 1185, 689, 291, 2464, 428, 4166, 294, 11121, 2487, 1228, 1491, 1010, 18632, 281, 6964, 264, 3877, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 394, "seek": 169940, "start": 1708.22, "end": 1708.98, "text": " So it'll look like code.", "tokens": [50806, 407, 309, 603, 574, 411, 3089, 13, 50844], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 395, "seek": 169940, "start": 1709.4, "end": 1715.3400000000001, "text": " You type commands telling the system that a certain line is a chapter heading or that a block of text is an equation.", "tokens": [50865, 509, 2010, 16901, 3585, 264, 1185, 300, 257, 1629, 1622, 307, 257, 7187, 9864, 420, 300, 257, 3461, 295, 2487, 307, 364, 5367, 13, 51162], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 396, "seek": 169940, "start": 1715.68, "end": 1718.7800000000002, "text": " You don't see the final formatted document while you are writing.", "tokens": [51179, 509, 500, 380, 536, 264, 2572, 1254, 32509, 4166, 1339, 291, 366, 3579, 13, 51334], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 397, "seek": 169940, "start": 1718.8400000000001, "end": 1719.48, "text": " Okay, that's so frustrating.", "tokens": [51337, 1033, 11, 300, 311, 370, 16522, 13, 51369], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 398, "seek": 169940, "start": 1719.6000000000001, "end": 1726.5, "text": " You have to run the text through a compiler, which processes your logical instructions and generates a beautifully formatted PDF at the end.", "tokens": [51375, 509, 362, 281, 1190, 264, 2487, 807, 257, 31958, 11, 597, 7555, 428, 14978, 9415, 293, 23815, 257, 16525, 1254, 32509, 17752, 412, 264, 917, 13, 51720], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14373716735839845, "compression_ratio": 1.6813880126182965, "no_speech_prob": 1.5860074755250086e-12}, {"id": 399, "seek": 172650, "start": 1726.5, "end": 1736.86, "text": " Okay, so why on earth would anyone still use latex or Vim or Unix command lines when we have fictionless platforms that do it all for us instantly?", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 370, 983, 322, 4120, 576, 2878, 920, 764, 3469, 87, 420, 691, 332, 420, 1156, 970, 5622, 3876, 562, 321, 362, 13266, 1832, 9473, 300, 360, 309, 439, 337, 505, 13518, 30, 50883], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09748494223262487, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491913970250068e-12}, {"id": 400, "seek": 172650, "start": 1737.1, "end": 1741.82, "text": " Because, as the author argues, their abstractions remain entirely legible.", "tokens": [50895, 1436, 11, 382, 264, 3793, 38218, 11, 641, 12649, 626, 6222, 7696, 1676, 964, 13, 51131], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09748494223262487, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491913970250068e-12}, {"id": 401, "seek": 172650, "start": 1742.66, "end": 1749.68, "text": " They endure and maintain fiercely devoted communities of professionals because they are designed more like workshops than vending machines.", "tokens": [51173, 814, 24732, 293, 6909, 16334, 42879, 21815, 4456, 295, 11954, 570, 436, 366, 4761, 544, 411, 19162, 813, 371, 2029, 8379, 13, 51524], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09748494223262487, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491913970250068e-12}, {"id": 402, "seek": 172650, "start": 1749.82, "end": 1751.38, "text": " Workshops versus vending machines.", "tokens": [51531, 6603, 2716, 3370, 5717, 371, 2029, 8379, 13, 51609], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09748494223262487, "compression_ratio": 1.5816733067729083, "no_speech_prob": 1.2491913970250068e-12}, {"id": 403, "seek": 175138, "start": 1751.38, "end": 1756.3400000000001, "text": " Mastery of these austere tools isn't just about memorizing keyboard shortcuts.", "tokens": [50365, 6140, 88, 295, 613, 34916, 323, 3873, 1943, 380, 445, 466, 10560, 3319, 10186, 34620, 13, 50613], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10266177685229809, "compression_ratio": 1.5502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954029767949573e-12}, {"id": 404, "seek": 175138, "start": 1756.8000000000002, "end": 1763.9, "text": " It's about gradually acquiring the competence to reconstruct, debug, and modify the system itself.", "tokens": [50636, 467, 311, 466, 13145, 37374, 264, 39965, 281, 31499, 11, 24083, 11, 293, 16927, 264, 1185, 2564, 13, 50991], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10266177685229809, "compression_ratio": 1.5502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954029767949573e-12}, {"id": 405, "seek": 175138, "start": 1763.98, "end": 1773.0400000000002, "text": " By forcing you to understand the logic of the compilation or the structure of the data pipeline, they act as a continuous apprenticeship encoded directly into the software.", "tokens": [50995, 3146, 19030, 291, 281, 1223, 264, 9952, 295, 264, 40261, 420, 264, 3877, 295, 264, 1412, 15517, 11, 436, 605, 382, 257, 10957, 47070, 2058, 12340, 3838, 666, 264, 4722, 13, 51448], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10266177685229809, "compression_ratio": 1.5502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954029767949573e-12}, {"id": 406, "seek": 175138, "start": 1773.16, "end": 1773.5400000000002, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [51454, 1079, 13, 51473], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10266177685229809, "compression_ratio": 1.5502183406113537, "no_speech_prob": 1.4954029767949573e-12}, {"id": 407, "seek": 177354, "start": 1773.54, "end": 1775.56, "text": " Okay, I understand the romance of the workshop.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 286, 1223, 264, 19064, 295, 264, 13541, 13, 50466], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 408, "seek": 177354, "start": 1775.7, "end": 1776.3, "text": " I really do.", "tokens": [50473, 286, 534, 360, 13, 50503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 409, "seek": 177354, "start": 1776.8999999999999, "end": 1781.7, "text": " But I'm looking at this from the perspective of an average person, and part of me thinks, so what?", "tokens": [50533, 583, 286, 478, 1237, 412, 341, 490, 264, 4585, 295, 364, 4274, 954, 11, 293, 644, 295, 385, 7309, 11, 370, 437, 30, 50773], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 410, "seek": 177354, "start": 1781.96, "end": 1783.3799999999999, "text": " The so what is very valid.", "tokens": [50786, 440, 370, 437, 307, 588, 7363, 13, 50857], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 411, "seek": 177354, "start": 1783.56, "end": 1783.74, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50866, 1779, 13, 50875], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 412, "seek": 177354, "start": 1783.92, "end": 1793.04, "text": " Like, I don't want to forge my own engine block and drive to the grocery store, and I certainly don't want to learn Unix command line syntax just to write a performance review for my employee.", "tokens": [50884, 1743, 11, 286, 500, 380, 528, 281, 38741, 452, 1065, 2848, 3461, 293, 3332, 281, 264, 14410, 3531, 11, 293, 286, 3297, 500, 380, 528, 281, 1466, 1156, 970, 5622, 1622, 28431, 445, 281, 2464, 257, 3389, 3131, 337, 452, 10738, 13, 51340], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 413, "seek": 177354, "start": 1793.3999999999999, "end": 1796.44, "text": " Isn't convenience the whole point of technological progress?", "tokens": [51358, 6998, 380, 19283, 264, 1379, 935, 295, 18439, 4205, 30, 51510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.09494886063692863, "compression_ratio": 1.6021505376344085, "no_speech_prob": 1.7149004655561684e-12}, {"id": 414, "seek": 179644, "start": 1796.44, "end": 1803.98, "text": " This raises an important question, and it is the absolute most common and most valid defense of the current technological paradigm.", "tokens": [50365, 639, 19658, 364, 1021, 1168, 11, 293, 309, 307, 264, 8236, 881, 2689, 293, 881, 7363, 7654, 295, 264, 2190, 18439, 24709, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17024288177490235, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858840933177798e-12}, {"id": 415, "seek": 179644, "start": 1804.4, "end": 1807.94, "text": " The paper anticipates this pushback and addresses it head on.", "tokens": [50763, 440, 3035, 10416, 1024, 341, 2944, 3207, 293, 16862, 309, 1378, 322, 13, 50940], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17024288177490235, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858840933177798e-12}, {"id": 416, "seek": 179644, "start": 1808.26, "end": 1809.1000000000001, "text": " Okay, what do they say?", "tokens": [50956, 1033, 11, 437, 360, 436, 584, 30, 50998], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17024288177490235, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858840933177798e-12}, {"id": 417, "seek": 179644, "start": 1809.22, "end": 1812.9, "text": " The author states clearly that convenience itself is not the enemy.", "tokens": [51004, 440, 3793, 4368, 4448, 300, 19283, 2564, 307, 406, 264, 5945, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17024288177490235, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858840933177798e-12}, {"id": 418, "seek": 179644, "start": 1813.6200000000001, "end": 1818.16, "text": " Civilization has always advanced by reducing unnecessary physical and cognitive labor.", "tokens": [51224, 13405, 2144, 575, 1009, 7339, 538, 12245, 19350, 4001, 293, 15605, 5938, 13, 51451], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17024288177490235, "compression_ratio": 1.5245901639344261, "no_speech_prob": 1.5858840933177798e-12}, {"id": 419, "seek": 181816, "start": 1818.16, "end": 1827.8200000000002, "text": " Nobody is seriously arguing that we should abandon modern GPS and go back to navigating by sextant and starlight just for the educational value of the struggle.", "tokens": [50365, 9297, 307, 6638, 19697, 300, 321, 820, 9072, 4363, 19462, 293, 352, 646, 281, 32054, 538, 42826, 394, 293, 3543, 2764, 445, 337, 264, 10189, 2158, 295, 264, 7799, 13, 50848], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 420, "seek": 181816, "start": 1828.0800000000002, "end": 1828.16, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [50861, 1779, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 421, "seek": 181816, "start": 1828.24, "end": 1828.94, "text": " I want the GPS.", "tokens": [50869, 286, 528, 264, 19462, 13, 50904], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 422, "seek": 181816, "start": 1829.28, "end": 1829.96, "text": " I want the tractor.", "tokens": [50921, 286, 528, 264, 31857, 13, 50955], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 423, "seek": 181816, "start": 1830.0800000000002, "end": 1832.5600000000002, "text": " I don't want to plow the field by hand to build character.", "tokens": [50961, 286, 500, 380, 528, 281, 499, 305, 264, 2519, 538, 1011, 281, 1322, 2517, 13, 51085], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 424, "seek": 181816, "start": 1832.72, "end": 1833.8600000000001, "text": " We all want the tractor.", "tokens": [51093, 492, 439, 528, 264, 31857, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 425, "seek": 181816, "start": 1834.48, "end": 1838.3400000000001, "text": " The objective of technology is not to artificially maximize difficulty.", "tokens": [51181, 440, 10024, 295, 2899, 307, 406, 281, 39905, 2270, 19874, 10360, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14956995157095102, "compression_ratio": 1.6026785714285714, "no_speech_prob": 1.8398089041832266e-12}, {"id": 426, "seek": 183834, "start": 1838.34, "end": 1849.6999999999998, "text": " The profound danger, however, emerges when convenience ceases to function as a bridge toward greater understanding and instead becomes a total, inescapable substitute for it.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 14382, 4330, 11, 4461, 11, 38965, 562, 19283, 1769, 1957, 281, 2445, 382, 257, 7283, 7361, 5044, 3701, 293, 2602, 3643, 257, 3217, 11, 294, 279, 9485, 712, 15802, 337, 309, 13, 50933], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 427, "seek": 183834, "start": 1849.9399999999998, "end": 1851.56, "text": " So we don't have to get rid of the easy stuff.", "tokens": [50945, 407, 321, 500, 380, 362, 281, 483, 3973, 295, 264, 1858, 1507, 13, 51026], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 428, "seek": 183834, "start": 1851.6599999999999, "end": 1853.34, "text": " We just need the hard stuff to be accessible.", "tokens": [51031, 492, 445, 643, 264, 1152, 1507, 281, 312, 9515, 13, 51115], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 429, "seek": 183834, "start": 1853.6599999999999, "end": 1858.76, "text": " The goal isn't to force every citizen to learn assembly code or compile their own operating systems.", "tokens": [51131, 440, 3387, 1943, 380, 281, 3464, 633, 13326, 281, 1466, 12103, 3089, 420, 31413, 641, 1065, 7447, 3652, 13, 51386], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 430, "seek": 183834, "start": 1859.24, "end": 1864.6, "text": " The goal is to ensure that the underlying abstractions remain permeable for those who do need to learn them.", "tokens": [51410, 440, 3387, 307, 281, 5586, 300, 264, 14217, 12649, 626, 6222, 30287, 712, 337, 729, 567, 360, 643, 281, 1466, 552, 13, 51678], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 431, "seek": 183834, "start": 1864.9399999999998, "end": 1867.34, "text": " Ah, permeable abstractions.", "tokens": [51695, 2438, 11, 30287, 712, 12649, 626, 13, 51815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14714092319294558, "compression_ratio": 1.6946308724832215, "no_speech_prob": 1.5132513297988481e-12}, {"id": 432, "seek": 186734, "start": 1867.34, "end": 1870.76, "text": " We are back to the glass bottom boat.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 366, 646, 281, 264, 4276, 2767, 6582, 13, 50536], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 433, "seek": 186734, "start": 1870.82, "end": 1871.1399999999999, "text": " Yes.", "tokens": [50539, 1079, 13, 50555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 434, "seek": 186734, "start": 1872.4399999999998, "end": 1875.9399999999998, "text": " You don't have to look down at the engine if you just want to sit on the deck and enjoy the sunset.", "tokens": [50620, 509, 500, 380, 362, 281, 574, 760, 412, 264, 2848, 498, 291, 445, 528, 281, 1394, 322, 264, 9341, 293, 2103, 264, 20142, 13, 50795], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 435, "seek": 186734, "start": 1876.1, "end": 1877.3, "text": " You can just consume the ride.", "tokens": [50803, 509, 393, 445, 14732, 264, 5077, 13, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 436, "seek": 186734, "start": 1877.6799999999998, "end": 1880.78, "text": " But if you want to know how the boat works, the glass is there.", "tokens": [50882, 583, 498, 291, 528, 281, 458, 577, 264, 6582, 1985, 11, 264, 4276, 307, 456, 13, 51037], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 437, "seek": 186734, "start": 1880.78, "end": 1885.36, "text": " The mechanism isn't intentionally hidden behind welded steel plates.", "tokens": [51037, 440, 7513, 1943, 380, 22062, 7633, 2261, 49227, 8269, 14231, 13, 51266], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 438, "seek": 186734, "start": 1885.9399999999998, "end": 1887.02, "text": " That is the crucial distinction.", "tokens": [51295, 663, 307, 264, 11462, 16844, 13, 51349], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 439, "seek": 186734, "start": 1887.76, "end": 1895.6, "text": " When a digital ecosystem is entirely closed off, when the abstraction is an impenetrable wall of proprietary code and remote servers,", "tokens": [51386, 1133, 257, 4562, 11311, 307, 7696, 5395, 766, 11, 562, 264, 37765, 307, 364, 704, 268, 302, 424, 638, 2929, 295, 38992, 3089, 293, 8607, 15909, 11, 51778], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1699473222096761, "compression_ratio": 1.6596491228070176, "no_speech_prob": 1.9736430371952718e-12}, {"id": 440, "seek": 189560, "start": 1895.6, "end": 1901.08, "text": " the user experiences a continuous, delightful improvement in practical capability.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 4195, 5235, 257, 10957, 11, 35194, 10444, 294, 8496, 13759, 13, 50639], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1956264227628708, "compression_ratio": 1.0933333333333333, "no_speech_prob": 1.7082028066356392e-12}, {"id": 441, "seek": 190108, "start": 1901.08, "end": 1903.6, "text": " But they are entirely at the mercy of the institution.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 436, 366, 7696, 412, 264, 13174, 295, 264, 7818, 13, 50491], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 442, "seek": 190108, "start": 1903.78, "end": 1904.1799999999998, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50500, 7587, 13, 50520], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 443, "seek": 190108, "start": 1904.6799999999998, "end": 1911.04, "text": " The system works perfectly right up until the company goes bankrupt or changes its pricing model or alters its terms of service", "tokens": [50545, 440, 1185, 1985, 6239, 558, 493, 1826, 264, 2237, 1709, 21780, 420, 2962, 1080, 17621, 2316, 420, 419, 1559, 1080, 2115, 295, 2643, 50863], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 444, "seek": 190108, "start": 1911.04, "end": 1915.54, "text": " or simply decides to deprecate the specific feature you rely on for your livelihood.", "tokens": [50863, 420, 2935, 14898, 281, 1367, 13867, 473, 264, 2685, 4111, 291, 10687, 322, 337, 428, 34343, 13, 51088], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 445, "seek": 190108, "start": 1915.8799999999999, "end": 1917.84, "text": " And because you only ever rented the competence,", "tokens": [51105, 400, 570, 291, 787, 1562, 32381, 264, 39965, 11, 51203], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 446, "seek": 190108, "start": 1918.34, "end": 1922.32, "text": " because the representation was never transferred to your local machine or your local mind,", "tokens": [51228, 570, 264, 10290, 390, 1128, 15809, 281, 428, 2654, 3479, 420, 428, 2654, 1575, 11, 51427], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 447, "seek": 190108, "start": 1922.6799999999998, "end": 1925.8799999999999, "text": " you were left with absolutely nothing when the platform vanishes.", "tokens": [51445, 291, 645, 1411, 365, 3122, 1825, 562, 264, 3663, 3161, 16423, 13, 51605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 448, "seek": 190108, "start": 1926.04, "end": 1926.62, "text": " Nothing at all.", "tokens": [51613, 6693, 412, 439, 13, 51642], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14875152519157342, "compression_ratio": 1.6938775510204083, "no_speech_prob": 1.8542212036620764e-12}, {"id": 449, "seek": 192662, "start": 1926.62, "end": 1930.8, "text": " And this structural dependence is happening everywhere with software right now.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 341, 15067, 31704, 307, 2737, 5315, 365, 4722, 558, 586, 13, 50574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 450, "seek": 192662, "start": 1931.3, "end": 1937.78, "text": " It's the transition from owning a program on a CD-ROM to paying a monthly subscription for SoftShare as a service.", "tokens": [50599, 467, 311, 264, 6034, 490, 29820, 257, 1461, 322, 257, 6743, 12, 49, 5251, 281, 6229, 257, 12878, 17231, 337, 16985, 7774, 543, 382, 257, 2643, 13, 50923], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 451, "seek": 192662, "start": 1937.8799999999999, "end": 1938.54, "text": " It's pervasive.", "tokens": [50928, 467, 311, 680, 39211, 13, 50961], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 452, "seek": 192662, "start": 1938.84, "end": 1941.8799999999999, "text": " But the paper takes this concept of hoarding representation", "tokens": [50976, 583, 264, 3035, 2516, 341, 3410, 295, 45940, 278, 10290, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 453, "seek": 192662, "start": 1941.8799999999999, "end": 1946.52, "text": " and applies it to the ultimate inflection point we are facing today.", "tokens": [51128, 293, 13165, 309, 281, 264, 9705, 1536, 5450, 935, 321, 366, 7170, 965, 13, 51360], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 454, "seek": 192662, "start": 1946.6999999999998, "end": 1951.06, "text": " Because if modern software is already centralizing our structural competence,", "tokens": [51369, 1436, 498, 4363, 4722, 307, 1217, 5777, 3319, 527, 15067, 39965, 11, 51587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 455, "seek": 192662, "start": 1951.28, "end": 1956.32, "text": " what happens when software begins automating the actual process of reasoning itself?", "tokens": [51598, 437, 2314, 562, 4722, 7338, 3553, 990, 264, 3539, 1399, 295, 21577, 2564, 30, 51850], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1603757175830526, "compression_ratio": 1.6567656765676568, "no_speech_prob": 1.6621823275414505e-12}, {"id": 456, "seek": 195662, "start": 1956.62, "end": 1959.02, "text": " Which means we have to dive into artificial intelligence.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 1355, 321, 362, 281, 9192, 666, 11677, 7599, 13, 50485], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 457, "seek": 195662, "start": 1959.2199999999998, "end": 1959.52, "text": " We do.", "tokens": [50495, 492, 360, 13, 50510], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 458, "seek": 195662, "start": 1960.02, "end": 1963.56, "text": " Because AI fundamentally alters the stakes of this entire discussion.", "tokens": [50535, 1436, 7318, 17879, 419, 1559, 264, 28429, 295, 341, 2302, 5017, 13, 50712], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 459, "seek": 195662, "start": 1963.6799999999998, "end": 1964.1599999999999, "text": " It does.", "tokens": [50718, 467, 775, 13, 50742], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 460, "seek": 195662, "start": 1964.4799999999998, "end": 1970.2399999999998, "text": " The paper argues that previous technological revolutions automated relatively well-defined mechanical execution.", "tokens": [50758, 440, 3035, 38218, 300, 3894, 18439, 3698, 15892, 18473, 7226, 731, 12, 37716, 12070, 15058, 13, 51046], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 461, "seek": 195662, "start": 1970.8, "end": 1973.08, "text": " A calculator automates arithmetic rules.", "tokens": [51074, 316, 24993, 3553, 1024, 42973, 4474, 13, 51188], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 462, "seek": 195662, "start": 1973.4799999999998, "end": 1977.2399999999998, "text": " A search engine retrieves and ranks existing documents based on keywords.", "tokens": [51208, 316, 3164, 2848, 19817, 977, 293, 21406, 6741, 8512, 2361, 322, 21009, 13, 51396], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 463, "seek": 195662, "start": 1977.2399999999998, "end": 1981.3, "text": " A compiler translates human-readable code into machine-readable binary.", "tokens": [51396, 316, 31958, 28468, 1952, 12, 2538, 712, 3089, 666, 3479, 12, 2538, 712, 17434, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 464, "seek": 195662, "start": 1981.62, "end": 1981.8799999999999, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51615, 1779, 13, 51628], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 465, "seek": 195662, "start": 1982.36, "end": 1984.9199999999998, "text": " These are complex tasks, but they are execution.", "tokens": [51652, 1981, 366, 3997, 9608, 11, 457, 436, 366, 15058, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16998154294174328, "compression_ratio": 1.630718954248366, "no_speech_prob": 2.068551926970308e-12}, {"id": 466, "seek": 198492, "start": 1984.92, "end": 1991.7, "text": " Modern AI, specifically the architecture of large language models, automates representational labor itself.", "tokens": [50365, 19814, 7318, 11, 4682, 264, 9482, 295, 2416, 2856, 5245, 11, 3553, 1024, 2906, 1478, 5938, 2564, 13, 50704], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20698116074747114, "compression_ratio": 1.4875621890547264, "no_speech_prob": 2.052249429423947e-12}, {"id": 467, "seek": 198492, "start": 1992.04, "end": 1993.72, "text": " They summarize complex arguments.", "tokens": [50721, 814, 20858, 3997, 12869, 13, 50805], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20698116074747114, "compression_ratio": 1.4875621890547264, "no_speech_prob": 2.052249429423947e-12}, {"id": 468, "seek": 198492, "start": 1994.24, "end": 1996.16, "text": " They draft original legal briefs.", "tokens": [50831, 814, 11206, 3380, 5089, 5353, 82, 13, 50927], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20698116074747114, "compression_ratio": 1.4875621890547264, "no_speech_prob": 2.052249429423947e-12}, {"id": 469, "seek": 198492, "start": 1996.3600000000001, "end": 1998.66, "text": " They explain quantum mechanics to five-year-olds.", "tokens": [50937, 814, 2903, 13018, 12939, 281, 1732, 12, 5294, 12, 31518, 13, 51052], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20698116074747114, "compression_ratio": 1.4875621890547264, "no_speech_prob": 2.052249429423947e-12}, {"id": 470, "seek": 198492, "start": 1998.9, "end": 2002.7, "text": " They write novel code architectures from scratch based on a vague prompt.", "tokens": [51064, 814, 2464, 7613, 3089, 6331, 1303, 490, 8459, 2361, 322, 257, 24247, 12391, 13, 51254], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.20698116074747114, "compression_ratio": 1.4875621890547264, "no_speech_prob": 2.052249429423947e-12}, {"id": 471, "seek": 200270, "start": 2002.7, "end": 2008.98, "text": " They are doing the conceptual heavy lifting, the synthesis, that used to be the exclusive domain of human reasoning.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 366, 884, 264, 24106, 4676, 15798, 11, 264, 30252, 11, 300, 1143, 281, 312, 264, 13005, 9274, 295, 1952, 21577, 13, 50679], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516696177030863, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053903380371615e-12}, {"id": 472, "seek": 200270, "start": 2009.2, "end": 2009.6000000000001, "text": " Precisely.", "tokens": [50690, 48746, 736, 13, 50710], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516696177030863, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053903380371615e-12}, {"id": 473, "seek": 200270, "start": 2010.28, "end": 2016.54, "text": " And to understand why this is a crisis of civilizational memory, we have to look at how these models actually function.", "tokens": [50744, 400, 281, 1223, 983, 341, 307, 257, 5869, 295, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 11, 321, 362, 281, 574, 412, 577, 613, 5245, 767, 2445, 13, 51057], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516696177030863, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053903380371615e-12}, {"id": 474, "seek": 200270, "start": 2017.72, "end": 2021.82, "text": " An LLM is, by its very architecture, the ultimate black box.", "tokens": [51116, 1107, 441, 43, 44, 307, 11, 538, 1080, 588, 9482, 11, 264, 9705, 2211, 2424, 13, 51321], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14516696177030863, "compression_ratio": 1.4666666666666666, "no_speech_prob": 2.9053903380371615e-12}, {"id": 475, "seek": 202182, "start": 2021.82, "end": 2026.36, "text": " It doesn't think in rules or logical steps that it can easily explain.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 1177, 380, 519, 294, 4474, 420, 14978, 4439, 300, 309, 393, 3612, 2903, 13, 50592], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14233945763629416, "compression_ratio": 1.5927272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.167603119565542e-12}, {"id": 476, "seek": 202182, "start": 2026.46, "end": 2026.62, "text": " No.", "tokens": [50597, 883, 13, 50605], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14233945763629416, "compression_ratio": 1.5927272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.167603119565542e-12}, {"id": 477, "seek": 202182, "start": 2026.84, "end": 2035.78, "text": " It is a massive neural network containing billions of parameters, calculating the mathematical probability of the next word in a sequence based on vast amounts of training data.", "tokens": [50616, 467, 307, 257, 5994, 18161, 3209, 19273, 17375, 295, 9834, 11, 28258, 264, 18894, 8482, 295, 264, 958, 1349, 294, 257, 8310, 2361, 322, 8369, 11663, 295, 3097, 1412, 13, 51063], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14233945763629416, "compression_ratio": 1.5927272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.167603119565542e-12}, {"id": 478, "seek": 202182, "start": 2036.26, "end": 2042.0, "text": " Even the engineers who build these models often cannot explain exactly why the model chose a specific output over another.", "tokens": [51087, 2754, 264, 11955, 567, 1322, 613, 5245, 2049, 2644, 2903, 2293, 983, 264, 2316, 5111, 257, 2685, 5598, 670, 1071, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14233945763629416, "compression_ratio": 1.5927272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.167603119565542e-12}, {"id": 479, "seek": 202182, "start": 2042.56, "end": 2045.6599999999999, "text": " The reasoning is obscured inside a web of statistical weights.", "tokens": [51402, 440, 21577, 307, 22082, 3831, 1854, 257, 3670, 295, 22820, 17443, 13, 51557], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14233945763629416, "compression_ratio": 1.5927272727272728, "no_speech_prob": 2.167603119565542e-12}, {"id": 480, "seek": 204566, "start": 2045.66, "end": 2051.1800000000003, "text": " So when I ask it a question, I'm getting an output without any transparent underlying logic.", "tokens": [50365, 407, 562, 286, 1029, 309, 257, 1168, 11, 286, 478, 1242, 364, 5598, 1553, 604, 12737, 14217, 9952, 13, 50641], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11542913415929773, "compression_ratio": 1.6933797909407666, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762489612840882e-12}, {"id": 481, "seek": 204566, "start": 2051.82, "end": 2057.6800000000003, "text": " And this is where the difference between renting competence and transferring competence becomes an existential issue for society.", "tokens": [50673, 400, 341, 307, 689, 264, 2649, 1296, 40598, 39965, 293, 31437, 39965, 3643, 364, 37133, 2734, 337, 4086, 13, 50966], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11542913415929773, "compression_ratio": 1.6933797909407666, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762489612840882e-12}, {"id": 482, "seek": 204566, "start": 2057.6800000000003, "end": 2064.98, "text": " The author presents this brilliant thought experiment comparing two hypothetical AI systems that are equally capable.", "tokens": [50966, 440, 3793, 13533, 341, 10248, 1194, 5120, 15763, 732, 33053, 7318, 3652, 300, 366, 12309, 8189, 13, 51331], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11542913415929773, "compression_ratio": 1.6933797909407666, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762489612840882e-12}, {"id": 483, "seek": 204566, "start": 2065.46, "end": 2073.9, "text": " They both solve the exact same engineering problem with the exact same accuracy, but they have totally different impacts on the human using them.", "tokens": [51355, 814, 1293, 5039, 264, 1900, 912, 7043, 1154, 365, 264, 1900, 912, 14170, 11, 457, 436, 362, 3879, 819, 11606, 322, 264, 1952, 1228, 552, 13, 51777], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11542913415929773, "compression_ratio": 1.6933797909407666, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762489612840882e-12}, {"id": 484, "seek": 207390, "start": 2073.9, "end": 2078.64, "text": " Let's walk through these, because this thought experiment perfectly encapsulates the warning of the paper.", "tokens": [50365, 961, 311, 1792, 807, 613, 11, 570, 341, 1194, 5120, 6239, 38745, 26192, 264, 9164, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 50602], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 485, "seek": 207390, "start": 2079.26, "end": 2082.58, "text": " The author calls System 1 the idealized oracle.", "tokens": [50633, 440, 3793, 5498, 8910, 502, 264, 7157, 1602, 420, 7041, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 486, "seek": 207390, "start": 2083.02, "end": 2083.9, "text": " Okay, System 1.", "tokens": [50821, 1033, 11, 8910, 502, 13, 50865], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 487, "seek": 207390, "start": 2084.5, "end": 2085.1, "text": " Picture this.", "tokens": [50895, 35730, 341, 13, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 488, "seek": 207390, "start": 2085.7000000000003, "end": 2090.7200000000003, "text": " You are a programmer, and you have a nasty memory leak in your software that you just can't figure out.", "tokens": [50955, 509, 366, 257, 32116, 11, 293, 291, 362, 257, 17923, 4675, 17143, 294, 428, 4722, 300, 291, 445, 393, 380, 2573, 484, 13, 51206], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 489, "seek": 207390, "start": 2091.44, "end": 2093.64, "text": " You give your code to System 1, the oracle.", "tokens": [51242, 509, 976, 428, 3089, 281, 8910, 502, 11, 264, 420, 7041, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 490, "seek": 207390, "start": 2094.1800000000003, "end": 2094.7200000000003, "text": " And what does it do?", "tokens": [51379, 400, 437, 775, 309, 360, 30, 51406], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 491, "seek": 207390, "start": 2094.98, "end": 2101.1600000000003, "text": " It processes it for two seconds and instantly spits out the perfect, bug-free block of code to replace yours.", "tokens": [51419, 467, 7555, 309, 337, 732, 3949, 293, 13518, 637, 1208, 484, 264, 2176, 11, 7426, 12, 10792, 3461, 295, 3089, 281, 7406, 6342, 13, 51728], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 492, "seek": 207390, "start": 2101.32, "end": 2102.2000000000003, "text": " Just hands you the answer.", "tokens": [51736, 1449, 2377, 291, 264, 1867, 13, 51780], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16414327399675235, "compression_ratio": 1.6387959866220736, "no_speech_prob": 1.7762495033851744e-12}, {"id": 493, "seek": 210220, "start": 2102.2, "end": 2104.06, "text": " The interaction is incredibly efficient.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 9285, 307, 6252, 7148, 13, 50458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 494, "seek": 210220, "start": 2104.4199999999996, "end": 2109.4399999999996, "text": " You copy the code, you paste it into your project, the software works perfectly, and you move on with your day.", "tokens": [50476, 509, 5055, 264, 3089, 11, 291, 9163, 309, 666, 428, 1716, 11, 264, 4722, 1985, 6239, 11, 293, 291, 1286, 322, 365, 428, 786, 13, 50727], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 495, "seek": 210220, "start": 2109.8599999999997, "end": 2111.24, "text": " The immediate problem disappears.", "tokens": [50748, 440, 11629, 1154, 25527, 13, 50817], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 496, "seek": 210220, "start": 2111.8599999999997, "end": 2113.14, "text": " Productivity is maximized.", "tokens": [50848, 22005, 4253, 307, 5138, 1602, 13, 50912], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 497, "seek": 210220, "start": 2113.64, "end": 2119.46, "text": " But, crucially, your personal competence remains exactly the same as it was before you asked the question.", "tokens": [50937, 583, 11, 5140, 1909, 11, 428, 2973, 39965, 7023, 2293, 264, 912, 382, 309, 390, 949, 291, 2351, 264, 1168, 13, 51228], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 498, "seek": 210220, "start": 2119.7999999999997, "end": 2122.24, "text": " You didn't learn why the memory leak happened.", "tokens": [51245, 509, 994, 380, 1466, 983, 264, 4675, 17143, 2011, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 499, "seek": 210220, "start": 2122.64, "end": 2126.8199999999997, "text": " You didn't learn the architectural principle of memory management that fixes it.", "tokens": [51387, 509, 994, 380, 1466, 264, 26621, 8665, 295, 4675, 4592, 300, 32539, 309, 13, 51596], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 500, "seek": 210220, "start": 2127.2, "end": 2128.8799999999997, "text": " You don't know how to spot it next time.", "tokens": [51615, 509, 500, 380, 458, 577, 281, 4008, 309, 958, 565, 13, 51699], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1219990664515002, "compression_ratio": 1.652027027027027, "no_speech_prob": 2.1847664736368566e-12}, {"id": 501, "seek": 212888, "start": 2128.88, "end": 2135.92, "text": " The representation, the conceptual understanding of the system, stayed completely inside the machine's neural network.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 10290, 11, 264, 24106, 3701, 295, 264, 1185, 11, 9181, 2584, 1854, 264, 3479, 311, 18161, 3209, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 502, "seek": 212888, "start": 2136.32, "end": 2140.6, "text": " Only the finished, polished artifact crossed over the screen to you.", "tokens": [50737, 5686, 264, 4335, 11, 29079, 34806, 14622, 670, 264, 2568, 281, 291, 13, 50951], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 503, "seek": 212888, "start": 2140.6, "end": 2140.76, "text": " Yeah.", "tokens": [50951, 865, 13, 50959], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 504, "seek": 212888, "start": 2140.9, "end": 2142.26, "text": " I outsourced my reasoning.", "tokens": [50966, 286, 14758, 396, 1232, 452, 21577, 13, 51034], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 505, "seek": 212888, "start": 2142.56, "end": 2143.1, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51049, 7587, 13, 51076], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 506, "seek": 212888, "start": 2143.82, "end": 2145.12, "text": " Now, consider System 2.", "tokens": [51112, 823, 11, 1949, 8910, 568, 13, 51177], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 507, "seek": 212888, "start": 2145.62, "end": 2147.62, "text": " The author calls this the educator.", "tokens": [51202, 440, 3793, 5498, 341, 264, 31237, 13, 51302], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2015849616792467, "compression_ratio": 1.4306930693069306, "no_speech_prob": 1.4956330444959587e-12}, {"id": 508, "seek": 214762, "start": 2147.62, "end": 2150.18, "text": " You feed it the same broken code.", "tokens": [50365, 509, 3154, 309, 264, 912, 5463, 3089, 13, 50493], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18503019544813368, "compression_ratio": 1.4013157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421190800030127e-12}, {"id": 509, "seek": 214762, "start": 2150.64, "end": 2155.3399999999997, "text": " It analyzes it and reaches the exact same accurate conclusion about how to fix it.", "tokens": [50516, 467, 6459, 12214, 309, 293, 14235, 264, 1900, 912, 8559, 10063, 466, 577, 281, 3191, 309, 13, 50751], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18503019544813368, "compression_ratio": 1.4013157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421190800030127e-12}, {"id": 510, "seek": 214762, "start": 2155.96, "end": 2161.22, "text": " But instead of just handing you the finished code on a silver platter, it exposes the reasoning.", "tokens": [50782, 583, 2602, 295, 445, 34774, 291, 264, 4335, 3089, 322, 257, 8753, 499, 1161, 11, 309, 1278, 4201, 264, 21577, 13, 51045], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.18503019544813368, "compression_ratio": 1.4013157894736843, "no_speech_prob": 1.5421190800030127e-12}, {"id": 511, "seek": 216122, "start": 2161.22, "end": 2164.22, "text": " An educator system would have to be architected entirely differently.", "tokens": [50365, 1107, 31237, 1185, 576, 362, 281, 312, 6331, 292, 7696, 7614, 13, 50515], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 512, "seek": 216122, "start": 2164.52, "end": 2166.54, "text": " It would identify the underlying abstractions.", "tokens": [50530, 467, 576, 5876, 264, 14217, 12649, 626, 13, 50631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 513, "seek": 216122, "start": 2166.7, "end": 2169.16, "text": " It would point out the conceptual structures you violated.", "tokens": [50639, 467, 576, 935, 484, 264, 24106, 9227, 291, 33239, 13, 50762], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 514, "seek": 216122, "start": 2169.4599999999996, "end": 2174.48, "text": " It might say, I notice your program is continuously allocating memory in this loop without freeing it.", "tokens": [50777, 467, 1062, 584, 11, 286, 3449, 428, 1461, 307, 15684, 12660, 990, 4675, 294, 341, 6367, 1553, 1737, 278, 309, 13, 51028], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 515, "seek": 216122, "start": 2174.98, "end": 2177.18, "text": " Here is the principle of garbage collection you are missing.", "tokens": [51053, 1692, 307, 264, 8665, 295, 14150, 5765, 291, 366, 5361, 13, 51163], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 516, "seek": 216122, "start": 2177.6, "end": 2180.22, "text": " And here is a conceptual map of how we construct a solution.", "tokens": [51184, 400, 510, 307, 257, 24106, 4471, 295, 577, 321, 7690, 257, 3827, 13, 51315], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 517, "seek": 216122, "start": 2180.3399999999997, "end": 2181.9199999999996, "text": " It guides you to read the code yourself.", "tokens": [51321, 467, 17007, 291, 281, 1401, 264, 3089, 1803, 13, 51400], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 518, "seek": 216122, "start": 2182.2799999999997, "end": 2185.8999999999996, "text": " It's the difference between a vending machine and a teaching kitchen.", "tokens": [51418, 467, 311, 264, 2649, 1296, 257, 371, 2029, 3479, 293, 257, 4571, 6525, 13, 51599], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14369775509012156, "compression_ratio": 1.7205387205387206, "no_speech_prob": 1.309623633496959e-12}, {"id": 519, "seek": 218590, "start": 2185.9, "end": 2188.86, "text": " System 1 is the vending machine.", "tokens": [50365, 8910, 502, 307, 264, 371, 2029, 3479, 13, 50513], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 520, "seek": 218590, "start": 2189.1600000000003, "end": 2193.86, "text": " You press a button, you insert a coin, and a perfectly cooked gourmet meal drops out.", "tokens": [50528, 509, 1886, 257, 2960, 11, 291, 8969, 257, 11464, 11, 293, 257, 6239, 9267, 46651, 5537, 6791, 11438, 484, 13, 50763], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 521, "seek": 218590, "start": 2193.98, "end": 2194.98, "text": " Fast and effortless.", "tokens": [50769, 15968, 293, 4630, 1832, 13, 50819], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 522, "seek": 218590, "start": 2195.1600000000003, "end": 2197.6800000000003, "text": " Fast, delicious, requires zero effort.", "tokens": [50828, 15968, 11, 4809, 11, 7029, 4018, 4630, 13, 50954], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 523, "seek": 218590, "start": 2198.26, "end": 2203.36, "text": " But if the vending machine ever unplugs, or if the company raises the price of the meal to $1,000,", "tokens": [50983, 583, 498, 264, 371, 2029, 3479, 1562, 32816, 14950, 11, 420, 498, 264, 2237, 19658, 264, 3218, 295, 264, 6791, 281, 1848, 16, 11, 1360, 11, 51238], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 524, "seek": 218590, "start": 2203.9, "end": 2209.82, "text": " you are going to starve because you have absolutely no idea how to chop an onion or turn on a stove.", "tokens": [51265, 291, 366, 516, 281, 46755, 570, 291, 362, 3122, 572, 1558, 577, 281, 7931, 364, 10916, 420, 1261, 322, 257, 19263, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 525, "seek": 218590, "start": 2210.1, "end": 2210.46, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51575, 1779, 13, 51593], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 526, "seek": 218590, "start": 2211.04, "end": 2212.6, "text": " System 2 is the teaching kitchen.", "tokens": [51622, 8910, 568, 307, 264, 4571, 6525, 13, 51700], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.16731206301985116, "compression_ratio": 1.6177606177606179, "no_speech_prob": 1.92810025757828e-12}, {"id": 527, "seek": 221260, "start": 2212.6, "end": 2216.18, "text": " It takes a little bit more time, it requires cognitive friction and engagement,", "tokens": [50365, 467, 2516, 257, 707, 857, 544, 565, 11, 309, 7029, 15605, 17710, 293, 8742, 11, 50544], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 528, "seek": 221260, "start": 2216.6, "end": 2219.2599999999998, "text": " but you walk out of that room actually knowing how to cook.", "tokens": [50565, 457, 291, 1792, 484, 295, 300, 1808, 767, 5276, 577, 281, 2543, 13, 50698], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 529, "seek": 221260, "start": 2219.7799999999997, "end": 2221.3399999999997, "text": " The competence was transferred to you.", "tokens": [50724, 440, 39965, 390, 15809, 281, 291, 13, 50802], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 530, "seek": 221260, "start": 2221.54, "end": 2222.7599999999998, "text": " A fantastic analogy.", "tokens": [50812, 316, 5456, 21663, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 531, "seek": 221260, "start": 2223.06, "end": 2227.4, "text": " And from the perspective of an executive looking at a spreadsheet of immediate productivity,", "tokens": [50888, 400, 490, 264, 4585, 295, 364, 10140, 1237, 412, 257, 27733, 295, 11629, 15604, 11, 51105], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 532, "seek": 221260, "start": 2227.92, "end": 2229.9, "text": " both systems look equally valuable.", "tokens": [51131, 1293, 3652, 574, 12309, 8263, 13, 51230], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 533, "seek": 221260, "start": 2230.2799999999997, "end": 2232.36, "text": " The software bug was fixed in both scenarios.", "tokens": [51249, 440, 4722, 7426, 390, 6806, 294, 1293, 15077, 13, 51353], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 534, "seek": 221260, "start": 2232.88, "end": 2233.72, "text": " The meal was delivered.", "tokens": [51379, 440, 6791, 390, 10144, 13, 51421], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 535, "seek": 221260, "start": 2234.06, "end": 2236.5, "text": " But from the perspective of civilizational memory,", "tokens": [51438, 583, 490, 264, 4585, 295, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 11, 51560], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 536, "seek": 221260, "start": 2237.0, "end": 2241.08, "text": " the paper argues these two systems produce entirely divergent futures.", "tokens": [51585, 264, 3035, 38218, 613, 732, 3652, 5258, 7696, 18558, 6930, 26071, 13, 51789], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15915983814304158, "compression_ratio": 1.6883116883116882, "no_speech_prob": 1.6883089978131371e-12}, {"id": 537, "seek": 224108, "start": 2241.08, "end": 2246.94, "text": " System 1 creates a civilization that accumulates increasingly sophisticated magical artifacts,", "tokens": [50365, 8910, 502, 7829, 257, 18036, 300, 12989, 26192, 12980, 16950, 12066, 24617, 11, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 538, "seek": 224108, "start": 2247.36, "end": 2253.9, "text": " while leaving all the reconstructive competence locked inside the proprietary server farms of a few AI companies.", "tokens": [50679, 1339, 5012, 439, 264, 16891, 21673, 39965, 9376, 1854, 264, 38992, 7154, 20366, 295, 257, 1326, 7318, 3431, 13, 51006], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 539, "seek": 224108, "start": 2254.16, "end": 2255.9, "text": " We become incredibly productive,", "tokens": [51019, 492, 1813, 6252, 13304, 11, 51106], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 540, "seek": 224108, "start": 2256.34, "end": 2261.92, "text": " but our productivity is a brittle house of cards relying entirely on external representation.", "tokens": [51128, 457, 527, 15604, 307, 257, 49325, 1782, 295, 5632, 24140, 7696, 322, 8320, 10290, 13, 51407], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 541, "seek": 224108, "start": 2262.2599999999998, "end": 2267.06, "text": " The paper draws a really sharp parallel here to the history of automation and the de-skilling of labor,", "tokens": [51424, 440, 3035, 20045, 257, 534, 8199, 8952, 510, 281, 264, 2503, 295, 17769, 293, 264, 368, 12, 5161, 7345, 295, 5938, 11, 51664], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 542, "seek": 224108, "start": 2267.2799999999997, "end": 2269.14, "text": " like the tractor analogy we used earlier.", "tokens": [51675, 411, 264, 31857, 21663, 321, 1143, 3071, 13, 51768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14074225227038065, "compression_ratio": 1.6195286195286196, "no_speech_prob": 2.3620972799259787e-12}, {"id": 543, "seek": 226914, "start": 2269.14, "end": 2271.64, "text": " Oh right. When we mechanized farming with the tractor,", "tokens": [50365, 876, 558, 13, 1133, 321, 4236, 1602, 16557, 365, 264, 31857, 11, 50490], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 544, "seek": 226914, "start": 2272.06, "end": 2274.12, "text": " we displaced immense amounts of physical labor.", "tokens": [50511, 321, 33692, 22920, 11663, 295, 4001, 5938, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 545, "seek": 226914, "start": 2274.56, "end": 2278.3199999999997, "text": " We needed far fewer people swinging scythes or guiding oxen in the field.", "tokens": [50636, 492, 2978, 1400, 13366, 561, 29500, 795, 88, 392, 279, 420, 25061, 5976, 268, 294, 264, 2519, 13, 50824], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 546, "seek": 226914, "start": 2278.6, "end": 2280.1, "text": " But in displacing that physical labor,", "tokens": [50838, 583, 294, 14996, 5615, 300, 4001, 5938, 11, 50913], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 547, "seek": 226914, "start": 2280.22, "end": 2283.48, "text": " the technology created an immense demand for new conceptual labor.", "tokens": [50919, 264, 2899, 2942, 364, 22920, 4733, 337, 777, 24106, 5938, 13, 51082], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 548, "seek": 226914, "start": 2283.9, "end": 2286.7999999999997, "text": " We suddenly needed mechanical engineers to design the tractors,", "tokens": [51103, 492, 5800, 2978, 12070, 11955, 281, 1715, 264, 24207, 830, 11, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 549, "seek": 226914, "start": 2287.18, "end": 2289.24, "text": " logisticians to manage the supply chain,", "tokens": [51267, 3565, 3142, 2567, 281, 3067, 264, 5847, 5021, 11, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 550, "seek": 226914, "start": 2289.7999999999997, "end": 2292.7599999999998, "text": " agronomists to study soil chemistry, and industrial managers.", "tokens": [51398, 623, 2044, 298, 1751, 281, 2979, 6704, 12558, 11, 293, 9987, 14084, 13, 51546], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 551, "seek": 226914, "start": 2293.14, "end": 2295.2799999999997, "text": " The physical labor was outsourced to the machine,", "tokens": [51565, 440, 4001, 5938, 390, 14758, 396, 1232, 281, 264, 3479, 11, 51672], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 552, "seek": 226914, "start": 2295.7999999999997, "end": 2297.7799999999997, "text": " but the conceptual labor remained human.", "tokens": [51698, 457, 264, 24106, 5938, 12780, 1952, 13, 51797], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15274424919715293, "compression_ratio": 1.8120805369127517, "no_speech_prob": 1.7485628830277156e-12}, {"id": 553, "seek": 229778, "start": 2297.78, "end": 2302.6400000000003, "text": " But AI isn't a tractor for our muscles, it's a tractor for our minds.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 7318, 1943, 380, 257, 31857, 337, 527, 9530, 11, 309, 311, 257, 31857, 337, 527, 9634, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 554, "seek": 229778, "start": 2303.1600000000003, "end": 2307.1800000000003, "text": " Exactly. AI threatens to centralize the conceptual labor itself.", "tokens": [50634, 7587, 13, 7318, 47511, 281, 5777, 1125, 264, 24106, 5938, 2564, 13, 50835], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 555, "seek": 229778, "start": 2307.7400000000002, "end": 2310.28, "text": " If we use these systems purely as oracles,", "tokens": [50863, 759, 321, 764, 613, 3652, 17491, 382, 420, 9918, 11, 50990], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 556, "seek": 229778, "start": 2310.6000000000004, "end": 2314.82, "text": " we risk building an economy where humans merely act as requesters.", "tokens": [51006, 321, 3148, 2390, 364, 5010, 689, 6255, 17003, 605, 382, 5308, 433, 13, 51217], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 557, "seek": 229778, "start": 2315.0800000000004, "end": 2318.28, "text": " We constantly request brilliant artifacts from the black box,", "tokens": [51230, 492, 6460, 5308, 10248, 24617, 490, 264, 2211, 2424, 11, 51390], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 558, "seek": 229778, "start": 2318.6600000000003, "end": 2323.5600000000004, "text": " but we slowly atrophy the cognitive frameworks required to even critically examine,", "tokens": [51409, 457, 321, 5692, 412, 40826, 264, 15605, 29834, 4739, 281, 754, 22797, 17496, 11, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 559, "seek": 229778, "start": 2323.98, "end": 2327.0, "text": " debug, modify, or extend the results we are given.", "tokens": [51675, 24083, 11, 16927, 11, 420, 10101, 264, 3542, 321, 366, 2212, 13, 51826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17571814400809152, "compression_ratio": 1.6036363636363635, "no_speech_prob": 2.307056889278014e-12}, {"id": 560, "seek": 232700, "start": 2327.0, "end": 2332.04, "text": " If you don't know how to code, how can you verify that the oracle's code is secure?", "tokens": [50365, 759, 291, 500, 380, 458, 577, 281, 3089, 11, 577, 393, 291, 16888, 300, 264, 420, 7041, 311, 3089, 307, 7144, 30, 50617], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 561, "seek": 232700, "start": 2332.58, "end": 2332.86, "text": " You can't.", "tokens": [50644, 509, 393, 380, 13, 50658], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 562, "seek": 232700, "start": 2333.58, "end": 2335.06, "text": " If you don't understand legal precedent,", "tokens": [50694, 759, 291, 500, 380, 1223, 5089, 37388, 11, 50768], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 563, "seek": 232700, "start": 2335.5, "end": 2338.7, "text": " how can you verify that oracle's legal brief isn't a hallucination?", "tokens": [50790, 577, 393, 291, 16888, 300, 420, 7041, 311, 5089, 5353, 1943, 380, 257, 35212, 2486, 30, 50950], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 564, "seek": 232700, "start": 2339.16, "end": 2342.26, "text": " We lose the ability to judge the framework that produced the answer.", "tokens": [50973, 492, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 6995, 264, 8388, 300, 7126, 264, 1867, 13, 51128], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 565, "seek": 232700, "start": 2342.44, "end": 2344.72, "text": " We become a society of passive consumers,", "tokens": [51137, 492, 1813, 257, 4086, 295, 14975, 11883, 11, 51251], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 566, "seek": 232700, "start": 2344.96, "end": 2348.86, "text": " just typing prompts into the void and hoping the magic box gives us something good.", "tokens": [51263, 445, 18444, 41095, 666, 264, 22009, 293, 7159, 264, 5585, 2424, 2709, 505, 746, 665, 13, 51458], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13837188424415958, "compression_ratio": 1.6583333333333334, "no_speech_prob": 1.53708838192268e-12}, {"id": 567, "seek": 234886, "start": 2348.86, "end": 2354.08, "text": " And if we lose the ability to evaluate the answer, we are entirely unmoored from reality.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 498, 321, 3624, 264, 3485, 281, 13059, 264, 1867, 11, 321, 366, 7696, 517, 3280, 2769, 490, 4103, 13, 50626], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 568, "seek": 234886, "start": 2354.44, "end": 2358.06, "text": " Which brings us to the ultimate question posed by this entire deep dive.", "tokens": [50644, 3013, 5607, 505, 281, 264, 9705, 1168, 31399, 538, 341, 2302, 2452, 9192, 13, 50825], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 569, "seek": 234886, "start": 2358.1800000000003, "end": 2359.08, "text": " This is the crux of it.", "tokens": [50831, 639, 307, 264, 5140, 87, 295, 309, 13, 50876], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 570, "seek": 234886, "start": 2359.2200000000003, "end": 2361.56, "text": " If we can't just look at how fast our microchips are,", "tokens": [50883, 759, 321, 393, 380, 445, 574, 412, 577, 2370, 527, 4532, 339, 2600, 366, 11, 51000], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 571, "seek": 234886, "start": 2361.6400000000003, "end": 2363.96, "text": " or how many lines of code our AI can write per minute,", "tokens": [51004, 420, 577, 867, 3876, 295, 3089, 527, 7318, 393, 2464, 680, 3456, 11, 51120], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 572, "seek": 234886, "start": 2364.1200000000003, "end": 2365.76, "text": " or how high the GDP is,", "tokens": [51128, 420, 577, 1090, 264, 19599, 307, 11, 51210], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 573, "seek": 234886, "start": 2365.86, "end": 2368.9, "text": " how should we measure whether our society is actually progressing?", "tokens": [51215, 577, 820, 321, 3481, 1968, 527, 4086, 307, 767, 36305, 30, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13470861544975868, "compression_ratio": 1.5317460317460319, "no_speech_prob": 1.5071378390088541e-12}, {"id": 574, "seek": 236890, "start": 2368.9, "end": 2373.56, "text": " This is where the fliction paper brings all these historical and technical threads together", "tokens": [50365, 639, 307, 689, 264, 932, 4105, 3035, 5607, 439, 613, 8584, 293, 6191, 19314, 1214, 50598], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 575, "seek": 236890, "start": 2373.56, "end": 2376.06, "text": " into a unified theory of progress.", "tokens": [50598, 666, 257, 26787, 5261, 295, 4205, 13, 50723], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 576, "seek": 236890, "start": 2376.64, "end": 2377.9, "text": " The author does not dismiss productivity.", "tokens": [50752, 440, 3793, 775, 406, 16974, 15604, 13, 50815], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 577, "seek": 236890, "start": 2379.06, "end": 2383.0, "text": " Material abundance, economic growth, computational capability,", "tokens": [50873, 29160, 23391, 11, 4836, 4599, 11, 28270, 13759, 11, 51070], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 578, "seek": 236890, "start": 2383.3, "end": 2384.9, "text": " these are undeniably vital.", "tokens": [51085, 613, 366, 674, 15711, 1188, 11707, 13, 51165], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 579, "seek": 236890, "start": 2385.52, "end": 2386.64, "text": " They freed us from famine.", "tokens": [51196, 814, 21796, 505, 490, 42790, 13, 51252], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 580, "seek": 236890, "start": 2386.7400000000002, "end": 2387.2200000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [51257, 7587, 13, 51281], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 581, "seek": 236890, "start": 2387.82, "end": 2391.7200000000003, "text": " They are what freed humanity from the brutal historical realities of scarcity.", "tokens": [51311, 814, 366, 437, 21796, 10243, 490, 264, 17878, 8584, 27785, 295, 44181, 13, 51506], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.19534499304635183, "compression_ratio": 1.5780590717299579, "no_speech_prob": 1.7900185457150886e-12}, {"id": 582, "seek": 239172, "start": 2391.72, "end": 2395.74, "text": " A society that cannot reliably produce food, medicine, or shelter,", "tokens": [50365, 316, 4086, 300, 2644, 49927, 5258, 1755, 11, 7195, 11, 420, 13341, 11, 50566], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 583, "seek": 239172, "start": 2396.18, "end": 2399.02, "text": " cannot sustain high-level scientific inquiry.", "tokens": [50588, 2644, 6769, 1090, 12, 12418, 8134, 25736, 13, 50730], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 584, "seek": 239172, "start": 2399.4399999999996, "end": 2401.04, "text": " We should celebrate our productivity.", "tokens": [50751, 492, 820, 8098, 527, 15604, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 585, "seek": 239172, "start": 2401.54, "end": 2402.9199999999996, "text": " But the author insists,", "tokens": [50856, 583, 264, 3793, 50137, 11, 50925], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 586, "seek": 239172, "start": 2403.2999999999997, "end": 2406.9199999999996, "text": " productivity is an insufficient measure of civilizational success.", "tokens": [50944, 15604, 307, 364, 41709, 3481, 295, 5605, 590, 1478, 2245, 13, 51125], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 587, "seek": 239172, "start": 2407.4399999999996, "end": 2410.98, "text": " Progress must simultaneously be measured by that phrase we started with,", "tokens": [51151, 32587, 1633, 16561, 312, 12690, 538, 300, 9535, 321, 1409, 365, 11, 51328], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 588, "seek": 239172, "start": 2411.3399999999997, "end": 2412.7799999999997, "text": " reconstructive capacity.", "tokens": [51346, 16891, 21673, 6042, 13, 51418], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 589, "seek": 239172, "start": 2413.08, "end": 2417.3999999999996, "text": " And the text gives us one final sweeping thought experiment to really hammer this home.", "tokens": [51433, 400, 264, 2487, 2709, 505, 472, 2572, 33285, 1194, 5120, 281, 534, 13017, 341, 1280, 13, 51649], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 590, "seek": 239172, "start": 2417.7999999999997, "end": 2421.3399999999997, "text": " It asks us to picture two different societies existing side by side.", "tokens": [51669, 467, 8962, 505, 281, 3036, 732, 819, 19329, 6741, 1252, 538, 1252, 13, 51846], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.17674128214518228, "compression_ratio": 1.6262295081967213, "no_speech_prob": 1.6110462573368234e-12}, {"id": 591, "seek": 242134, "start": 2421.34, "end": 2423.2400000000002, "text": " Okay, Society A and Society B.", "tokens": [50365, 1033, 11, 13742, 316, 293, 13742, 363, 13, 50460], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 592, "seek": 242134, "start": 2423.56, "end": 2425.58, "text": " On the surface, they are technologically identical.", "tokens": [50476, 1282, 264, 3753, 11, 436, 366, 1537, 17157, 14800, 13, 50577], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 593, "seek": 242134, "start": 2425.86, "end": 2428.6600000000003, "text": " They both have advanced stealth aircraft, incredible MRI machines,", "tokens": [50591, 814, 1293, 362, 7339, 25756, 9465, 11, 4651, 32812, 8379, 11, 50731], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 594, "seek": 242134, "start": 2429.1400000000003, "end": 2430.56, "text": " light and fast quantum computers.", "tokens": [50755, 1442, 293, 2370, 13018, 10807, 13, 50826], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 595, "seek": 242134, "start": 2430.9, "end": 2434.2000000000003, "text": " If you walk down the main street in Society A or Society B,", "tokens": [50843, 759, 291, 1792, 760, 264, 2135, 4838, 294, 13742, 316, 420, 13742, 363, 11, 51008], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 596, "seek": 242134, "start": 2434.6200000000003, "end": 2438.2000000000003, "text": " the gadgets in people's hands and the cars on the road would look exactly the same.", "tokens": [51029, 264, 37635, 294, 561, 311, 2377, 293, 264, 5163, 322, 264, 3060, 576, 574, 2293, 264, 912, 13, 51208], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 597, "seek": 242134, "start": 2438.4, "end": 2439.6200000000003, "text": " But underneath the surface,", "tokens": [51218, 583, 7223, 264, 3753, 11, 51279], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 598, "seek": 242134, "start": 2440.02, "end": 2442.2000000000003, "text": " their architectures of knowledge are completely different.", "tokens": [51299, 641, 6331, 1303, 295, 3601, 366, 2584, 819, 13, 51408], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 599, "seek": 242134, "start": 2442.38, "end": 2442.6800000000003, "text": " Right.", "tokens": [51417, 1779, 13, 51432], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 600, "seek": 242134, "start": 2443.06, "end": 2445.26, "text": " In Society A, knowledge is highly distributed.", "tokens": [51451, 682, 13742, 316, 11, 3601, 307, 5405, 12631, 13, 51561], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 601, "seek": 242134, "start": 2445.76, "end": 2448.78, "text": " Engineers, educators, mechanics, open source communities,", "tokens": [51586, 43950, 11, 22819, 11, 12939, 11, 1269, 4009, 4456, 11, 51737], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15209141988602895, "compression_ratio": 1.6645569620253164, "no_speech_prob": 2.134214246302113e-12}, {"id": 602, "seek": 244878, "start": 2448.78, "end": 2453.6400000000003, "text": " and ordinary citizens collectively hold the understanding of how their world works.", "tokens": [50365, 293, 10547, 7180, 24341, 1797, 264, 3701, 295, 577, 641, 1002, 1985, 13, 50608], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 603, "seek": 244878, "start": 2454.1600000000003, "end": 2458.2000000000003, "text": " No single institution acts as an irreplaceable bottleneck for competence.", "tokens": [50634, 883, 2167, 7818, 10672, 382, 364, 16014, 6742, 712, 44641, 547, 337, 39965, 13, 50836], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 604, "seek": 244878, "start": 2458.36, "end": 2458.6800000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50844, 7587, 13, 50860], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 605, "seek": 244878, "start": 2459.38, "end": 2462.26, "text": " The knowledge flows freely between university research labs,", "tokens": [50895, 440, 3601, 12867, 16433, 1296, 5454, 2132, 20339, 11, 51039], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 606, "seek": 244878, "start": 2462.5400000000004, "end": 2464.28, "text": " private industry, and public life.", "tokens": [51053, 4551, 3518, 11, 293, 1908, 993, 13, 51140], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 607, "seek": 244878, "start": 2464.6800000000003, "end": 2466.6200000000003, "text": " The tools they build are permeable.", "tokens": [51160, 440, 3873, 436, 1322, 366, 30287, 712, 13, 51257], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 608, "seek": 244878, "start": 2467.1200000000003, "end": 2468.34, "text": " The abstractions are ladders.", "tokens": [51282, 440, 12649, 626, 366, 6632, 15633, 13, 51343], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 609, "seek": 244878, "start": 2468.52, "end": 2469.96, "text": " The representations are shared.", "tokens": [51352, 440, 33358, 366, 5507, 13, 51424], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.1707756548042757, "compression_ratio": 1.5517241379310345, "no_speech_prob": 1.7689024073633264e-12}, {"id": 610, "seek": 246996, "start": 2469.96, "end": 2474.16, "text": " But in Society B, they have the exact same glittering gadgets.", "tokens": [50365, 583, 294, 13742, 363, 11, 436, 362, 264, 1900, 912, 18620, 278, 37635, 13, 50575], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 611, "seek": 246996, "start": 2474.62, "end": 2478.52, "text": " But the reconstructive competence is held by a tiny handful of opaque,", "tokens": [50598, 583, 264, 16891, 21673, 39965, 307, 5167, 538, 257, 5870, 16458, 295, 42687, 11, 50793], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 612, "seek": 246996, "start": 2479.06, "end": 2480.7200000000003, "text": " hyper-centralized organizations.", "tokens": [50820, 9848, 12, 2207, 2155, 1602, 6150, 13, 50903], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 613, "seek": 246996, "start": 2481.4, "end": 2483.52, "text": " The citizens interact with magic every day.", "tokens": [50937, 440, 7180, 4648, 365, 5585, 633, 786, 13, 51043], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 614, "seek": 246996, "start": 2483.9, "end": 2485.66, "text": " They touch glass screens and things happen.", "tokens": [51062, 814, 2557, 4276, 11171, 293, 721, 1051, 13, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 615, "seek": 246996, "start": 2485.94, "end": 2488.6, "text": " But hardly anyone outside those few corporate campuses", "tokens": [51164, 583, 13572, 2878, 2380, 729, 1326, 10896, 24233, 51297], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 616, "seek": 246996, "start": 2488.6, "end": 2493.76, "text": " possesses the conceptual resources to understand, modify, or rebuild the systems independently.", "tokens": [51297, 17490, 279, 264, 24106, 3593, 281, 1223, 11, 16927, 11, 420, 16877, 264, 3652, 21761, 13, 51555], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 617, "seek": 246996, "start": 2494.06, "end": 2495.7400000000002, "text": " Their tools are sealed black boxes.", "tokens": [51570, 6710, 3873, 366, 21514, 2211, 9002, 13, 51654], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 618, "seek": 246996, "start": 2495.88, "end": 2498.3, "text": " And here is the terrifying punchline of the paper.", "tokens": [51661, 400, 510, 307, 264, 18106, 8135, 1889, 295, 264, 3035, 13, 51782], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15279270273394288, "compression_ratio": 1.5870967741935484, "no_speech_prob": 1.8537758134096194e-12}, {"id": 619, "seek": 249830, "start": 2498.3, "end": 2501.82, "text": " However, conventional economics cannot tell these two societies apart.", "tokens": [50365, 2908, 11, 16011, 14564, 2644, 980, 613, 732, 19329, 4936, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 620, "seek": 249830, "start": 2502.1800000000003, "end": 2503.28, "text": " Their GDP is identical.", "tokens": [50559, 6710, 19599, 307, 14800, 13, 50614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 621, "seek": 249830, "start": 2503.76, "end": 2505.5800000000004, "text": " Their average standard of living is identical.", "tokens": [50638, 6710, 4274, 3832, 295, 2647, 307, 14800, 13, 50729], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 622, "seek": 249830, "start": 2506.2200000000003, "end": 2508.6800000000003, "text": " Consumer satisfaction surveys might even be identical.", "tokens": [50761, 39494, 18715, 22711, 1062, 754, 312, 14800, 13, 50884], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 623, "seek": 249830, "start": 2509.28, "end": 2512.84, "text": " But Society A has accumulated durable competence.", "tokens": [50914, 583, 13742, 316, 575, 31346, 22308, 39965, 13, 51092], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 624, "seek": 249830, "start": 2513.5800000000004, "end": 2516.6400000000003, "text": " Society B has only accumulated fragile artifacts.", "tokens": [51129, 13742, 363, 575, 787, 31346, 23847, 24617, 13, 51282], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 625, "seek": 249830, "start": 2517.04, "end": 2518.34, "text": " Society B is brittle.", "tokens": [51302, 13742, 363, 307, 49325, 13, 51367], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.21606124656787817, "compression_ratio": 1.614213197969543, "no_speech_prob": 2.3617639961781567e-12}, {"id": 626, "seek": 251834, "start": 2518.34, "end": 2524.98, "text": " If a massive disruption occurs, a political collapse, a geomagnetic storm that wipes out data centers,", "tokens": [50365, 759, 257, 5994, 28751, 11843, 11, 257, 3905, 15584, 11, 257, 1519, 298, 4535, 3532, 7679, 300, 41228, 484, 1412, 10898, 11, 50697], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 627, "seek": 251834, "start": 2525.28, "end": 2528.26, "text": " a shift in corporate incentives, or an economic catastrophe,", "tokens": [50712, 257, 5513, 294, 10896, 23374, 11, 420, 364, 4836, 36043, 11, 50861], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 628, "seek": 251834, "start": 2528.7200000000003, "end": 2532.36, "text": " the artifacts will remain for a while, just like the Roman aqueducts.", "tokens": [50884, 264, 24617, 486, 6222, 337, 257, 1339, 11, 445, 411, 264, 8566, 2373, 292, 11130, 82, 13, 51066], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 629, "seek": 251834, "start": 2532.44, "end": 2537.1200000000003, "text": " But the capacity to regenerate those systems, to fix them when they break, will rapidly vanish.", "tokens": [51070, 583, 264, 6042, 281, 26358, 473, 729, 3652, 11, 281, 3191, 552, 562, 436, 1821, 11, 486, 12910, 43584, 13, 51304], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 630, "seek": 251834, "start": 2537.32, "end": 2538.44, "text": " So what does this all mean?", "tokens": [51314, 407, 437, 775, 341, 439, 914, 30, 51370], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 631, "seek": 251834, "start": 2538.86, "end": 2543.94, "text": " Well, when you strip away all the academic terminology, the hashing algorithms, a history of calculus,", "tokens": [51391, 1042, 11, 562, 291, 12828, 1314, 439, 264, 7778, 27575, 11, 264, 575, 571, 14642, 11, 257, 2503, 295, 33400, 11, 51645], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11599011080605644, "compression_ratio": 1.5916955017301038, "no_speech_prob": 2.3715970593612967e-12}, {"id": 632, "seek": 254394, "start": 2543.94, "end": 2550.02, "text": " the core warning of this source material is that we are currently making a silent, unacknowledged trade.", "tokens": [50365, 264, 4965, 9164, 295, 341, 4009, 2527, 307, 300, 321, 366, 4362, 1455, 257, 12784, 11, 517, 501, 3785, 1493, 3004, 4923, 13, 50669], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13045019033003827, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359781569001534e-12}, {"id": 633, "seek": 254394, "start": 2550.2200000000003, "end": 2554.1, "text": " We are trading our permanent civilizational memory for temporary capability.", "tokens": [50679, 492, 366, 9529, 527, 10996, 5605, 590, 1478, 4675, 337, 13413, 13759, 13, 50873], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13045019033003827, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359781569001534e-12}, {"id": 634, "seek": 254394, "start": 2554.5, "end": 2559.64, "text": " We are trading the messy, slow, occasionally frustrating, but incredibly resilient process", "tokens": [50893, 492, 366, 9529, 264, 16191, 11, 2964, 11, 16895, 16522, 11, 457, 6252, 23699, 1399, 51150], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13045019033003827, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359781569001534e-12}, {"id": 635, "seek": 254394, "start": 2559.64, "end": 2566.2200000000003, "text": " of distributing knowledge for the frictionless, lightning-fast, incredibly fragile process of renting convenience.", "tokens": [51150, 295, 41406, 3601, 337, 264, 17710, 1832, 11, 16589, 12, 7011, 11, 6252, 23847, 1399, 295, 40598, 19283, 13, 51479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13045019033003827, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359781569001534e-12}, {"id": 636, "seek": 254394, "start": 2566.54, "end": 2571.0, "text": " What's fascinating here is how this framework redefines the entire purpose of technology.", "tokens": [51495, 708, 311, 10343, 510, 307, 577, 341, 8388, 38818, 1652, 264, 2302, 4334, 295, 2899, 13, 51718], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13045019033003827, "compression_ratio": 1.7096774193548387, "no_speech_prob": 2.0359781569001534e-12}, {"id": 637, "seek": 257100, "start": 2571.0, "end": 2577.92, "text": " The author concludes that the highest purpose of technological innovation isn't actually making sophisticated machines.", "tokens": [50365, 440, 3793, 24643, 300, 264, 6343, 4334, 295, 18439, 8504, 1943, 380, 767, 1455, 16950, 8379, 13, 50711], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 638, "seek": 257100, "start": 2578.16, "end": 2578.6, "text": " It's not.", "tokens": [50723, 467, 311, 406, 13, 50745], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 639, "seek": 257100, "start": 2578.88, "end": 2582.66, "text": " The machines, the software, the AI, they're just a byproduct.", "tokens": [50759, 440, 8379, 11, 264, 4722, 11, 264, 7318, 11, 436, 434, 445, 257, 538, 33244, 13, 50948], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 640, "seek": 257100, "start": 2583.3, "end": 2588.28, "text": " The true purpose of technology is expanding humanity's representational repertoire.", "tokens": [50980, 440, 2074, 4334, 295, 2899, 307, 14702, 10243, 311, 2906, 1478, 49604, 13, 51229], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 641, "seek": 257100, "start": 2589.12, "end": 2590.74, "text": " Representational repertoire. Explain that.", "tokens": [51271, 19945, 1478, 49604, 13, 39574, 300, 13, 51352], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 642, "seek": 257100, "start": 2590.86, "end": 2594.76, "text": " When Euclid formalized geometry, or when Newton formalized mechanics,", "tokens": [51358, 1133, 462, 1311, 75, 327, 9860, 1602, 18426, 11, 420, 562, 19541, 9860, 1602, 12939, 11, 51553], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 643, "seek": 257100, "start": 2595.32, "end": 2600.02, "text": " they didn't just give us tools to build better aqueducts or aim cannons more accurately.", "tokens": [51581, 436, 994, 380, 445, 976, 505, 3873, 281, 1322, 1101, 2373, 292, 11130, 82, 420, 5939, 47649, 544, 20095, 13, 51816], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.15342169945393133, "compression_ratio": 1.65625, "no_speech_prob": 1.8253243968396893e-12}, {"id": 644, "seek": 260002, "start": 2600.02, "end": 2604.46, "text": " They fundamentally expanded humanity's shared capacity to think.", "tokens": [50365, 814, 17879, 14342, 10243, 311, 5507, 6042, 281, 519, 13, 50587], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 645, "seek": 260002, "start": 2604.6, "end": 2605.08, "text": " Oh, I see.", "tokens": [50594, 876, 11, 286, 536, 13, 50618], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 646, "seek": 260002, "start": 2605.12, "end": 2608.7, "text": " That geometry and that physics became a permanent part of who we are as a species.", "tokens": [50620, 663, 18426, 293, 300, 10649, 3062, 257, 10996, 644, 295, 567, 321, 366, 382, 257, 6172, 13, 50799], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 647, "seek": 260002, "start": 2609.12, "end": 2613.22, "text": " They gave future generations a richer conceptual foundation to stand on.", "tokens": [50820, 814, 2729, 2027, 10593, 257, 29021, 24106, 7030, 281, 1463, 322, 13, 51025], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 648, "seek": 260002, "start": 2613.64, "end": 2615.38, "text": " That is true progress.", "tokens": [51046, 663, 307, 2074, 4205, 13, 51133], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 649, "seek": 260002, "start": 2615.58, "end": 2619.5, "text": " When a tool becomes a new language for human thought, civilization advances.", "tokens": [51143, 1133, 257, 2290, 3643, 257, 777, 2856, 337, 1952, 1194, 11, 18036, 25297, 13, 51339], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 650, "seek": 260002, "start": 2620.06, "end": 2624.84, "text": " When a tool just performs a magic trick behind a proprietary curtain, we really consume.", "tokens": [51367, 1133, 257, 2290, 445, 26213, 257, 5585, 4282, 2261, 257, 38992, 26789, 11, 321, 534, 14732, 13, 51606], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13348477085431418, "compression_ratio": 1.5789473684210527, "no_speech_prob": 1.7761011845279784e-12}, {"id": 651, "seek": 262484, "start": 2624.84, "end": 2633.1200000000003, "text": " And that puts the responsibility squarely on us, on the consumers, and crucially on the engineers and institutions building the next generation of infrastructure.", "tokens": [50365, 400, 300, 8137, 264, 6357, 3732, 356, 322, 505, 11, 322, 264, 11883, 11, 293, 5140, 1909, 322, 264, 11955, 293, 8142, 2390, 264, 958, 5125, 295, 6896, 13, 50779], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801763080415272, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 2.166814470905276e-12}, {"id": 652, "seek": 262484, "start": 2633.42, "end": 2640.28, "text": " Because the AI models, the cloud platforms, the digital ecosystems, they don't have an intrinsic bias toward opacity.", "tokens": [50794, 1436, 264, 7318, 5245, 11, 264, 4588, 9473, 11, 264, 4562, 32647, 11, 436, 500, 380, 362, 364, 35698, 12577, 7361, 41693, 13, 51137], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801763080415272, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 2.166814470905276e-12}, {"id": 653, "seek": 262484, "start": 2640.6600000000003, "end": 2643.26, "text": " They can be built as ladders or they can be built as walls.", "tokens": [51156, 814, 393, 312, 3094, 382, 6632, 15633, 420, 436, 393, 312, 3094, 382, 7920, 13, 51286], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801763080415272, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 2.166814470905276e-12}, {"id": 654, "seek": 262484, "start": 2643.44, "end": 2649.48, "text": " They can be engineered to transfer competence, to act as educators, or they can be built to hoard it, to act as oracles.", "tokens": [51295, 814, 393, 312, 38648, 281, 5003, 39965, 11, 281, 605, 382, 22819, 11, 420, 436, 393, 312, 3094, 281, 45940, 309, 11, 281, 605, 382, 420, 9918, 13, 51597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10801763080415272, "compression_ratio": 1.7868217054263567, "no_speech_prob": 2.166814470905276e-12}, {"id": 655, "seek": 264948, "start": 2649.48, "end": 2651.62, "text": " It is an architectural choice.", "tokens": [50365, 467, 307, 364, 26621, 3922, 13, 50472], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 656, "seek": 264948, "start": 2651.86, "end": 2653.0, "text": " It is entirely a choice.", "tokens": [50484, 467, 307, 7696, 257, 3922, 13, 50541], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 657, "seek": 264948, "start": 2653.64, "end": 2656.52, "text": " The technology itself cannot determine which future emerges.", "tokens": [50573, 440, 2899, 2564, 2644, 6997, 597, 2027, 38965, 13, 50717], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 658, "seek": 264948, "start": 2657.34, "end": 2663.26, "text": " It depends on whether our economic structures continue to exclusively reward the artificial scarcity of competence,", "tokens": [50758, 467, 5946, 322, 1968, 527, 4836, 9227, 2354, 281, 20638, 7782, 264, 11677, 44181, 295, 39965, 11, 51054], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 659, "seek": 264948, "start": 2663.64, "end": 2669.66, "text": " or whether we demand systems that leave behind more capable human minds after every interaction.", "tokens": [51073, 420, 1968, 321, 4733, 3652, 300, 1856, 2261, 544, 8189, 1952, 9634, 934, 633, 9285, 13, 51374], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 660, "seek": 264948, "start": 2669.88, "end": 2674.8, "text": " A civilization only truly remembers its inventions when its citizens remember how to invent.", "tokens": [51385, 316, 18036, 787, 4908, 26228, 1080, 43748, 562, 1080, 7180, 1604, 577, 281, 7962, 13, 51631], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13458169224750566, "compression_ratio": 1.623076923076923, "no_speech_prob": 1.6682413913823857e-12}, {"id": 661, "seek": 267480, "start": 2674.8, "end": 2677.6600000000003, "text": " Which brings us all back to you, listening to this right now.", "tokens": [50365, 3013, 5607, 505, 439, 646, 281, 291, 11, 4764, 281, 341, 558, 586, 13, 50508], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10534129952484707, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 1.790189307557255e-12}, {"id": 662, "seek": 267480, "start": 2678.1000000000004, "end": 2684.1200000000003, "text": " Tomorrow morning, you are going to wake up and immediately interact with dozens of deeply complex, beautifully designed digital systems.", "tokens": [50530, 17499, 2446, 11, 291, 366, 516, 281, 6634, 493, 293, 4258, 4648, 365, 18431, 295, 8760, 3997, 11, 16525, 4761, 4562, 3652, 13, 50831], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10534129952484707, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 1.790189307557255e-12}, {"id": 663, "seek": 267480, "start": 2684.26, "end": 2686.2200000000003, "text": " You are going to use perfectly optimized platforms.", "tokens": [50838, 509, 366, 516, 281, 764, 6239, 26941, 9473, 13, 50936], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10534129952484707, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 1.790189307557255e-12}, {"id": 664, "seek": 267480, "start": 2686.38, "end": 2692.46, "text": " You might ask an AI to draft an email, debug a piece of code, or explain a complex concept for a meeting.", "tokens": [50944, 509, 1062, 1029, 364, 7318, 281, 11206, 364, 3796, 11, 24083, 257, 2522, 295, 3089, 11, 420, 2903, 257, 3997, 3410, 337, 257, 3440, 13, 51248], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10534129952484707, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 1.790189307557255e-12}, {"id": 665, "seek": 267480, "start": 2692.8, "end": 2699.78, "text": " And when you do, the source material we've explored today asks you to pause and ask yourself one simple question.", "tokens": [51265, 400, 562, 291, 360, 11, 264, 4009, 2527, 321, 600, 24016, 965, 8962, 291, 281, 10465, 293, 1029, 1803, 472, 2199, 1168, 13, 51614], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.10534129952484707, "compression_ratio": 1.6095890410958904, "no_speech_prob": 1.790189307557255e-12}, {"id": 666, "seek": 269978, "start": 2699.78, "end": 2703.2200000000003, "text": " Is this tool acting as a ladder or a wall?", "tokens": [50365, 1119, 341, 2290, 6577, 382, 257, 18325, 420, 257, 2929, 30, 50537], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 667, "seek": 269978, "start": 2703.88, "end": 2707.8, "text": " Are you renting this competence, or is it being transferred to you?", "tokens": [50570, 2014, 291, 40598, 341, 39965, 11, 420, 307, 309, 885, 15809, 281, 291, 30, 50766], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 668, "seek": 269978, "start": 2708.1000000000004, "end": 2712.38, "text": " Are you acquiring a new capability, or are you just happily consuming a result?", "tokens": [50781, 2014, 291, 37374, 257, 777, 13759, 11, 420, 366, 291, 445, 19909, 19867, 257, 1874, 30, 50995], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 669, "seek": 269978, "start": 2712.6200000000003, "end": 2713.76, "text": " I'd take it a step further.", "tokens": [51007, 286, 1116, 747, 309, 257, 1823, 3052, 13, 51064], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 670, "seek": 269978, "start": 2714.2200000000003, "end": 2720.7200000000003, "text": " Because if we continue down this current path, if we blindly accept the convenience without demanding the representation,", "tokens": [51087, 1436, 498, 321, 2354, 760, 341, 2190, 3100, 11, 498, 321, 47744, 3241, 264, 19283, 1553, 19960, 264, 10290, 11, 51412], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 671, "seek": 269978, "start": 2721.42, "end": 2727.78, "text": " if we continue outsourcing our capacity to reason and reconstruct to proprietary black boxes...", "tokens": [51447, 498, 321, 2354, 14758, 41849, 527, 6042, 281, 1778, 293, 31499, 281, 38992, 2211, 9002, 485, 51765], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14644643995496961, "compression_ratio": 1.6833976833976834, "no_speech_prob": 1.5310998996431735e-12}, {"id": 672, "seek": 272778, "start": 2727.78, "end": 2731.6600000000003, "text": " We have to ask ourselves what kind of world we are leaving behind for the next generation.", "tokens": [50365, 492, 362, 281, 1029, 4175, 437, 733, 295, 1002, 321, 366, 5012, 2261, 337, 264, 958, 5125, 13, 50559], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 673, "seek": 272778, "start": 2731.82, "end": 2732.1800000000003, "text": " Exactly.", "tokens": [50567, 7587, 13, 50585], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 674, "seek": 272778, "start": 2732.78, "end": 2737.6400000000003, "text": " Will historians of the future look back at our era, not as the pinnacle of the information age,", "tokens": [50615, 3099, 26442, 295, 264, 2027, 574, 646, 412, 527, 4249, 11, 406, 382, 264, 5447, 77, 7041, 295, 264, 1589, 3205, 11, 50858], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 675, "seek": 272778, "start": 2737.98, "end": 2742.38, "text": " but as the quiet, comfortable, frictionless beginning of a technological dark age?", "tokens": [50875, 457, 382, 264, 5677, 11, 4619, 11, 17710, 1832, 2863, 295, 257, 18439, 2877, 3205, 30, 51095], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 676, "seek": 272778, "start": 2742.5, "end": 2749.28, "text": " An era where the cities were dazzlingly bright, the algorithms ran flawlessly, the information flowed endlessly...", "tokens": [51101, 1107, 4249, 689, 264, 6486, 645, 44078, 1688, 356, 4730, 11, 264, 14642, 5872, 13717, 12048, 11, 264, 1589, 3095, 292, 44920, 485, 51440], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 677, "seek": 272778, "start": 2749.28, "end": 2750.5400000000004, "text": " But nobody was actually home.", "tokens": [51440, 583, 5079, 390, 767, 1280, 13, 51503], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 678, "seek": 272778, "start": 2750.6400000000003, "end": 2751.96, "text": " ...a haunting extrapolation.", "tokens": [51508, 1097, 64, 44512, 48224, 399, 13, 51574], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 679, "seek": 272778, "start": 2752.2200000000003, "end": 2756.44, "text": " But an absolutely essential one to consider before the walls get too high to climb.", "tokens": [51587, 583, 364, 3122, 7115, 472, 281, 1949, 949, 264, 7920, 483, 886, 1090, 281, 10724, 13, 51798], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.14221425694743478, "compression_ratio": 1.6594427244582044, "no_speech_prob": 1.85424115298205e-12}, {"id": 680, "seek": 275644, "start": 2756.44, "end": 2758.7200000000003, "text": " That's our deep dive for today.", "tokens": [50365, 663, 311, 527, 2452, 9192, 337, 965, 13, 50479], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13724603476347746, "compression_ratio": 1.0470588235294118, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}, {"id": 681, "seek": 275644, "start": 2759.04, "end": 2761.08, "text": " Keep climbing the ladders, and we'll catch you next time.", "tokens": [50495, 5527, 14780, 264, 6632, 15633, 11, 293, 321, 603, 3745, 291, 958, 565, 13, 50597], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.13724603476347746, "compression_ratio": 1.0470588235294118, "no_speech_prob": 2.068024137352742e-12}], "language": "en"}
